  <para style="toc3">Luk</para>
  <para style="mt1">Luk</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="LUK 1" />
  <para style="s1">Ntọọñọ Ikọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 1:1" />Uwak awo e-edomo ukeme adiwet mbaña mme ñkpọ se ikitịppe e-emaekewuọ isu ke ufọọd ñnyịn, <verse eid="LUK 1:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 1:2" />ukem-ukem naña ekeyaak inọọ ñnyịn ato ke ubọk mbon se ikiba ke ntọọñọ nte ntiense inyʌñ ikwọrọ ikọ Abasi. <verse eid="LUK 1:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 1:3" />Utọ ntak ntom anam ami ñko ndat anyan ini ñkeene afịd ñkpọ ami usʌk-usʌk tọọñọ ke aditọọñọ, ndin mbiere adinekke ñwet mbʌk ami unọọ fiin, Adodukpono Tiofilọs <verse eid="LUK 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 1:4" />nọ ato do afo anekke adiọọñọ se ido akpanikọ ke mme ukpeebñkpọ a-afo abọọhọ.<verse eid="LUK 1:4" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Etañ Ebaña Emana Yọọn Aduọkmmọọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 1:5" />Ke ini Herọd a-akedooho adidem ke Yudia, aku keed amaaba a-akekereke Sakaraiya, a-akesịneke ke ikpeghe aku Abiya; a-anwaan amọ akekereke Elisabed, akenyʌññọ ato ubon Erọn. <verse eid="LUK 1:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 1:6" />Ammọ awo iba emaenam se inen ke iso Abasi, enana ndo ke adisaña ke afịd mme item ye mme ewʌhọ Abọọñ Abasi. <verse eid="LUK 1:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 1:7" />Ado ammọ ikinieghe ayịn, sia Elisabed akedo ada, ñko ammọ awo iba emaenekke esọñ.<verse eid="LUK 1:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 1:8" />Akem ke ini ikpeghe a-Sakaraiya akesịneke akenieghe adinam utom, a-Sakaraiya ke idem amọ akenyʌññọ aba ke utom nte aku Abasi, <verse eid="LUK 1:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 1:9" />naña ndutʌm mme aku akesido, emaesịn ukañ ndin emaemek anye ebo adʌk tembịd Abọọñ akefọp insensi. <verse eid="LUK 1:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 1:10" />Idaha ufọb insensi amaakekem, afịd mme akpono Abasi emaeda ke anwa ebọñ akam.<verse eid="LUK 1:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 1:11" />Ndin enyere Abọọñ amaawuọ ada Sakaraiya ke ubọk nnasia tembịd ufọp insensi. <verse eid="LUK 1:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 1:12" />Idem amaanyeñ Sakaraiya ke ini anye akekịtte enyere ami, ndịk amaanyʌñ anam anye. <verse eid="LUK 1:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 1:13" />Ado enyere amaabo anye: “Sakaraiya, kuufeghe ndịk, sia Abasi a-akop akam mfo. Anwaan mfo Elisabed ayaaman ayịn unọ fiin, ndin afo uduukoot anye Yọọn. <verse eid="LUK 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 1:14" />Afo ayaakop idaara ye inemesịd, uwak awo ñko eyaedaara ke emana amọ, <verse eid="LUK 1:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 1:15" />sia anye adiido ekamba awo ke iso Abọọñ. Inaaha anye anwọñ ukọd me unwọwọñ ñkpọ mfen anaamanaam awo, ñko anye ayaayọhọ ye Adisana Sịbidịd tọọñọ ke idịb eka amọ. <verse eid="LUK 1:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 1:16" />Anye ayaanam uwak nditọ Isrel etịmme ebịne Abọọñ Abasi ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 1:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 1:17" />Ndin anye ayaaboiyo ke iso Abasi ke sịbidịd ye adudu Elaiya, nọ anye anam esịd mme ete ewọññọ ekeene nditọ ammọ, anyʌñ anam mbon ntịdutọñ ekpeep ifiọk eto mme anam unen, anyʌñ abeeñe mme awo idem anọ Abọọñ Abasi.”<verse eid="LUK 1:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 1:18" />Ado Sakaraiya amaabịp enyere ate, “Ami ndiinam die ndiọọñọ ke ñkpọ ami ayaado ntoro? Ami ndo akaanadeen, anwaan mmi anyʌñ asọñ ke isua emana.”<verse eid="LUK 1:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 1:19" />Enyere amaabo anye, “Ami ndo Kebreel andaaha ke iso Abasi. Endọọdọñ ebo nditañ ikọ unọ ñnyʌñ mben eti mbʌk ami usọk fiin. <verse eid="LUK 1:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 1:20" />Ndin, idahami afo adiido imuum, uduutañña ikọ tutu usen ñkpọ ami amaadisu, sia afo ukunịmme ikọ mmi ke akpanikọ, a-adooho ayaasu ke ini amaakem.”<verse eid="LUK 1:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 1:21" />Mme awo e-ekedaaha ke anwa ebet Sakaraiya emaeba ke ñkpaidem ke anye adikikpeene adiwuọ ndi ke tembịd. <verse eid="LUK 1:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 1:22" />Ke ini anye akewuọhọ adi, anye ikikanna itañ ikọ inọ ammọ. Ammọ emaediọọñọ ke anye amaakịt ñkukịd ke tembịd, sia anye akekama ubọk atañ ikọ anọ ammọ ke idiọọñọ sia anye amaakappa imuum.<verse eid="LUK 1:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 1:23" />Ke ini ubiọñutom amọ ke tembịd amaakekweeñe, anye amaanyọñ ufọk amọ. <verse eid="LUK 1:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 1:24" />Akekem anwaan amọ Elisabed amaayommo, ndin ke afịd afiọñ ition anye ikiwuọhọ esiin. <verse eid="LUK 1:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 1:25" />Anye amaanyʌñ abo, “Abọọñ anam ami annọ miin, sia idahami anye añwọt miin mfọn amọ anyʌñ añkwokko abuud a-ami ñkediaha ke atu mbon awo.”<verse eid="LUK 1:25" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Etañ Ebaña Emana Yisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 1:26" />Ke ayọhọ afiọñ itiokeed tọọñọ Elisabed akeyommo, Abasi amaadọñ enyere Kebreel aka Nasared ke Kalili, <verse eid="LUK 1:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 1:27" />abịne adisịre abọikpa, a-Yosef awo ufọk Defid akeyemme adidọ. Adisịre abọikpa ado akekere Mmeri. <verse eid="LUK 1:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 1:28" />Ndin enyere Kebreel amaakebo Mmeri ate, “Mmekọọm-o, afo a-ayọhọke ye mfọn; Abọọñ mmọdo ye afo.”<verse eid="LUK 1:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 1:29" />Esịd amaatịmede Mmeri eti-eti ke ikọ ami, ndin anye amaakere se utọ ekọọm ami akpewuọñọ. <verse eid="LUK 1:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 1:30" />Ado enyere amaabo anye ate, “Mmeri, kuukop ndịk sia afo amebọ mfọn ato Abasi. <verse eid="LUK 1:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 1:31" />Afo ayaayommo idịb anyʌñ aman ayịn, ndin afo uduukoot anye Yisọs. <verse eid="LUK 1:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 1:32" />Anye ayaanie uku; ediikoot anye Ayịn Abasi Andikoñ Ñkan. Abọọñ Abasi ayaanọ anye ebekpo ete amọ Defid, <verse eid="LUK 1:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 1:33" />anye ñko ayaakara ubon ufọk Yekọb ke nsi-nsi, ndin abioubọọñ amọ idiinieghe utịd.”<verse eid="LUK 1:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 1:34" />Ndin Mmeri amaabịp enyere ate, “Ñkpọ ami adiisaña die itịppe sia ami ndo adisịre abọikpa a-mmendiọọñọke awodeen?”<verse eid="LUK 1:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 1:35" />Ado enyere amaabo anye, “Adisana Sịbidịd ayaadudoro fiin ke idem, ndin adudu Abasi Andikoñ Ñkan ayaufʌk fiin. Ke ntoro, ediikoot<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Ke ntoro </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ediikoot ayịn adiidimana adisana.</char></note> adisana ayịn a-afo uduuman Ayịn Abasi. <verse eid="LUK 1:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 1:36" />Idem ayakka mfo Elisabed, ayaaman ayịn ke ayio usọñ amọ. Ndin anye e-ekebooho ke ikanna iyommo asaña ye idịb afiọñ itiokeed. <verse eid="LUK 1:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 1:37" />Sia ibaaha ikọ ndomokeed a-atooho Abasi atreke adisu.”<verse eid="LUK 1:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 1:38" />Mmeri amaabọọrọ anye ate, “Ami ndo ayịnufọk Abọọñ Abasi, yak atịppe annọ miin kpa naña afo atañ.” Ndin enyere amaadakka akpọñ anye.<verse eid="LUK 1:38" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mmeri Akese Elisabed</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 1:39" />Ke ufọọd ini ado, Mmeri amaabeeñe idem asọp akaa idʌñ keed ke abod-abod abio Yudia, <verse eid="LUK 1:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 1:40" />akaa ufọk Sakaraiya anyʌñ akekọọm Elisabed. <verse eid="LUK 1:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 1:41" />Elisabed akekop uyio ekọọm Mmeri, ayịn amaatuak anye ke ntʌñidịb itie nnaa ayịn, anọ idaara; ndin anye amaanyʌñ ayọhọ ye Adisana Sịbidịd. <verse eid="LUK 1:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 1:42" />Ndin Elisabed amaabọñ ke akpọsọñ uyio ate, “Afọfọn unọ fiin ke atu afịd ibaan, anyʌñ afọfọn anọ mfịd idịb a-afo uduuman! <verse eid="LUK 1:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 1:43" />Ami nsaña die ndot utọ ukpono ami nọ afo nte eka Abọọñ mmi adinse miin? <verse eid="LUK 1:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="LUK 1:44" />Kpa ke idaha a-ami ñkoppo uyio ekọọm mfo, ayịn amantuak miin ke idịb anọ idaara. <verse eid="LUK 1:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="LUK 1:45" />Afọfọn anọ anye a-anịmme ke mme enwọñọ se Abọọñ Abasi akenam anọ anye ayaasu!”<verse eid="LUK 1:45" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mmeri Atañ Ase</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" sid="LUK 1:46" />Ndin Mmeri amaabo:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 1:46">“Ukpọñ mmi a-atooro Abọọñ,<verse eid="LUK 1:46" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="47" style="v" sid="LUK 1:47" />ndin sịbidịd mmi a-adaara ke Abasi Andinyaaña miin,<verse eid="LUK 1:47" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="48" style="v" sid="LUK 1:48" />sia anye a-akop mbọm abaña usuuhọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:48">itie afʌnanwaan amọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 1:48">Tọọñọ ke ami afịd emana eyaeñkoot miin anye a-Abasi adiọññọ,<verse eid="LUK 1:48" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="49" style="v" sid="LUK 1:49" />sia Akpọsọñ Abasi a-anam ñkpoon ñkpọ annọ miin,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:49">ndin anyịñ amọ ado adisana.<verse eid="LUK 1:49" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="50" style="v" sid="LUK 1:50" />Mbọm amọ a-aba ye mbon</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:50">e-ebaaha anye, tọọñọ ke emana keed tutu asịm emana mfen.<verse eid="LUK 1:50" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="51" style="v" sid="LUK 1:51" />Anye a-awọt adudu ubọk amọ;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:51">anyʌñ asuan mbon ñkịdidem ke mme akikere esịd ammọ.<verse eid="LUK 1:51" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="52" style="v" sid="LUK 1:52" />Anye a-adooro mme adaukara ke mme ebekpo ubọọñ ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:52">anyʌñ adịppe mbon nsuukidem.<verse eid="LUK 1:52" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="53" style="v" sid="LUK 1:53" />Anye a-ayʌkkọ mbon abiọọñ ye nti ñkpọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:53">anyʌñ abịn mbon imọ enyọñọ ñkaña ubọk.<verse eid="LUK 1:53" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="54" style="v" sid="LUK 1:54" />Anye a-anwam ikọd amọ Isrel,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:54">ke aditoiyo aditua mbọm<verse eid="LUK 1:54" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="55" style="v" sid="LUK 1:55" />naña anye akenwọñọ anọ Ebraham ye ubon amọ ke nsi-nsi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:55">ukem naña akenyʌñ anwọñọ anọ mme eteete ñnyịn.”<verse eid="LUK 1:55" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="56" style="v" sid="LUK 1:56" />Mmeri amaakaa iso aba ye Elisabed ke ñkpọ nte afiọñ ita ndin anye aditịmme anyọñ ufọk amọ.<verse eid="LUK 1:56" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Emana Yọọn Aduọkmmọọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="57" style="v" sid="LUK 1:57" />Ini amaakedikem, Elisabed amaaman ayịn awodeen. <verse eid="LUK 1:57" /><verse number="58" style="v" sid="LUK 1:58" />Mme mbọhọidʌñ ye imaan amọ emaekop ke Abọọñ amaatua anye mbọm, ndin ammọ emaedaara ye anye.<verse eid="LUK 1:58" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="59" style="v" sid="LUK 1:59" />Ke ayọhọ usen itiaita, emaedi adifọọrọ ayịn edʌd ñnyʌñ nsio anye anyịñ, ndin ekeyem edikoot anye Sakaraiya, ndian ete amọ, <verse eid="LUK 1:59" /><verse number="60" style="v" sid="LUK 1:60" />ado eka amọ amaafaaña ate, “Iyoo! Ana ekoot anye Yọọn.”<verse eid="LUK 1:60" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="61" style="v" sid="LUK 1:61" />Ado mme awo emaebo anye ete, “Ibaaha awo ke ekpək ndufo a-akereke utọ anyịñ ami.”<verse eid="LUK 1:61" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="62" style="v" sid="LUK 1:62" />Ndin emaenam idiọọñọ enọ ete amọ adibịp anye se anyịñ anye akpeyem nọ esio ayịn amọ. <verse eid="LUK 1:62" /><verse number="63" style="v" sid="LUK 1:63" />Sakaraiya amaabo yak inọ itiad ñwed, ndin ke ñkpaidem afịd awo, anye amaawet, “Anyịñ amọ ado Yọọn.” <verse eid="LUK 1:63" /><verse number="64" style="v" sid="LUK 1:64" />Kpa idaha-idaha ado, inua Sakaraiya amaakʌppọ, edeme amọ anyʌñ atara, ndin anye amaatọọñọ aditañ ikọ, anyʌñ atooro Abasi. <verse eid="LUK 1:64" /><verse number="65" style="v" sid="LUK 1:65" />Akedo ataa ñkpọ ñkpaidem anọ mme mbọhọidʌñ, ndin afịd mme andidʌñ ke mbood-mbood abio Yudia emaetañ ebaña mme ñkpọ ami. <verse eid="LUK 1:65" /><verse number="66" style="v" sid="LUK 1:66" />Afịd mbon se ikikop mme ñkpọ ami emaekere ke esịd ammọ ete, “Me nsoo ke ayịn ami adiido?” Sia ubọk Abọọñ Abasi amaaba ye anye.<verse eid="LUK 1:66" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Sakaraiya Atañ Ase</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="67" style="v" sid="LUK 1:67" />Sakaraiya amaayọhọ ye Adisana Sịbidịd, ndin anye amaatañ prọfesi ate:<verse eid="LUK 1:67" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="68" style="v" sid="LUK 1:68" />“Itooro anie Abọọñ Abasi Isrel,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:68">sia anye a-adise anyʌñ afak ikọd amọ.<verse eid="LUK 1:68" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="69" style="v" sid="LUK 1:69" />Anye awuuk nnʌk<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:69 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Nnʌk</char><char style="ft" closed="false">mi ada anọ akpọsọñ adidem.</char></note> adinyaaña inọ ñnyịn</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:69">ke ufọk Defid ayịnufọk amọ,<verse eid="LUK 1:69" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="70" style="v" sid="LUK 1:70" />(kpa naña anye aketañ ke inua mme ndisana prọfed amọ tọọñọ ke esed),<verse eid="LUK 1:70" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="71" style="v" sid="LUK 1:71" />adinyaaña ñnyịn nsio ke ubọk mme asua ñnyịn,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:71">ye mbon i-isuaha ñnyịn,<verse eid="LUK 1:71" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="72" style="v" sid="LUK 1:72" />ke adiwọt mbọm nnọọ mme eteete</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:72">ñnyịn ye aditoiyo adisana edioomo amọ,<verse eid="LUK 1:72" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="73" style="v" sid="LUK 1:73" />enwọñọ a-anye akenwọñọke anọ ete ñnyịn Ebraham:<verse eid="LUK 1:73" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="74" style="v" sid="LUK 1:74" />Ate imọ iyaifak ñnyịn isio ke ubọk mme asua ñnyịn,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:74">nọ ato do ñnyịn ikan inam ñkpọ ikpono anye, ikoppo ndịk,<verse eid="LUK 1:74" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="75" style="v" sid="LUK 1:75" />ye ke adisana ye adinenido ke iso amọ afịd ayio uwem ñnyịn.<verse eid="LUK 1:75" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="76" style="v" sid="LUK 1:76" />“Ndin afo ayịn mmi, eduukoot fiin prọfed Andikoñ Ñkan;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:76">sia afo ayaaboiyo Abọọñ iso akediọñ usʌñ anịm anọ anye,<verse eid="LUK 1:76" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="77" style="v" sid="LUK 1:77" />nọ ato ke adifeen mme idiọọkñkpọ ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:77">ikọd amọ ediọọñọ ebaña adinyaaña Abasi,<verse eid="LUK 1:77" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="78" style="v" sid="LUK 1:78" />ke ntak esịd mbọm Abasi ñnyịn,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:78">utịn asakka ato hefịn inọ ñnyịn,<verse eid="LUK 1:78" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="79" style="v" sid="LUK 1:79" />nọ anam unwana asịm</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 1:79">mbon e-ebaaha ke ekịm ye ndukpọñ ñkpa,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 1:79">anyʌñ akpeme ñkpad ñnyịn asịn ke usʌñ emem.”<verse eid="LUK 1:79" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="80" style="v" sid="LUK 1:80" />Ndin ayịn ado amaakọt anyʌñ akop uko ke sịbidịd. Anye akedʌñ ke anaan tutu akem ini se anye akeyaara idem amọ anwa-anwa anọ Isrel.<verse eid="LUK 1:80" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="LUK 2" />
  <para style="s1">Emana Yisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 2:1" />Akekem ke idaha ukara Sisa Akọstus, anye amaanịm ewʌhọ abo enam ubadawo ke afịd ekondo ñkañ Rom. <verse eid="LUK 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 2:2" />(Ami akedo akpa ubadawo e-ekenamma ke idaha<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2:2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Ubadawo ami akedat itie mbemiso</char></note> Kwirinius akedọọhọ adaukara ke Siria.) <verse eid="LUK 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 2:3" />Afịd awo emaekaiya abio ammọ nọ ekesịn anyịñ ke ñwed ubadawo.<verse eid="LUK 2:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 2:4" />Ndin Yosef amaato ke Nasared ke Kalili akaa Betlehem ke Yudia, abio Defid akesịn anyịñ, sia anye aketo ufọk ye aduuk Defid. <verse eid="LUK 2:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 2:5" />Yosef akesaña ye Mmeri, awonwaan a-anye akeyemme idọ, a-akenyʌññọ asaña ye idịb, akaa uwedanyịñ. <verse eid="LUK 2:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 2:6" />Uman amaaketọọñọ Mmeri ke ini a-ammọ ekebaaha ke Betlehem, <verse eid="LUK 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 2:7" />ndin anye amaaman akpan amọ, anyʌñ awañ anye ke afọñ anịm ke itie usịn ndidia ufene, sia ufañ ikibaaha se ammọ eba ke ufọk isen.<verse eid="LUK 2:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 2:8" />Mme akpemeedọñ emaeba ke ikọd ekpere, e-ekekpemeke mme edọñ ammọ ke akonayio ado. <verse eid="LUK 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 2:9" />Ndin enyere Abọọñ amaabiọññọ, ubọọñ Abasi amaanyʌñ ayamma afʌk ammọ, ndịk amaanyʌñ amʌm ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 2:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 2:10" />Ado enyere amaabo ammọ ate, “Ikiidịkke, sia mben eti etob isọk ndufo, a-adiinọ afịd awo ke ederimbod ekamba idaara. <verse eid="LUK 2:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 2:11" />Mfịn ami ke abio Defid, Andinyaaña amana inọ ndufo; anye ado Krais, a-adooho Abọọñ. <verse eid="LUK 2:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 2:12" />Ndin idiọọñọ ado ke ndufo eyaekịt ayịn e-ewañña ke afọñ naña ana ke itie usịn ndidia ufene.”<verse eid="LUK 2:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 2:13" />Kpa ke ndo-ndo ado, ataa uwak udịm mbon hefịn emaebiọññọ, ediana ye enyere ado etooro Abasi ete:<verse eid="LUK 2:13" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 2:14" />“Itooro anie Abasi ke ataa anyọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 2:14">emem anyʌñ aba ke isọñ ye mbon a-anye anọọhọ mfọn.”<verse eid="LUK 2:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 2:15" />Mme enyere ekedaaña ekpọñ ammọ eka hefịn, mme akpemeedọñ emaeneme ke atu idem ammọ ete, “Yak ñnyịn ika Betlehem ikise ñkpọntịppe a-Abọọñ atañña inọọ ñnyịn.”<verse eid="LUK 2:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 2:16" />Ndin ammọ emaesọp ekaa Betlehem, enyʌñ ekesoobo Mmeri ye Yosef ye nsekayịn naña ana ke itie usịn ndidia ufene. <verse eid="LUK 2:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 2:17" />Ke ini ammọ emaekekịt anye, ammọ emaesuan etob ebaña se eketañ ebaña ayịn ado enọ mbon awo, <verse eid="LUK 2:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 2:18" />idem amaanyʌñ akpa afịd awo se ikikop se mme akpemeedọñ eketañ enọ ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 2:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 2:19" />Ado Mmeri amaatʌm amʌm afịd se eketañ akama ke esịd amọ. <verse eid="LUK 2:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 2:20" />Mme akpemeedọñ emaetịmme enyọñọ, ekaiso ekpono enyʌñ etooro Abasi ke afịd ñkpọ se ammọ ekekịt enyʌñ ekop, a-akesañake akekem naña ekedọkkọ ammọ.<verse eid="LUK 2:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 2:21" />Akedikem ayọhọ usen itiaita, a-akedooho ini adifọọrọ ayịn edʌd ñnyʌñ nsio anye anyịñ, emaesio anye Yisọs, anyịñ a-enyere akenọọhọ mbemiso ediyoyommo anye.<verse eid="LUK 2:21" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Eben Yisọs Ekewọt ke Tembịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 2:22" />Ke usen ndutʌm adinam asana amaakedikem naña Mbed Moses aketemme, Yosef ye Mmeri emaeben Yisọs ekaa Yeruselem nọ ato do ekesaana anye eyaak enọ Abọọñ Abasi <verse eid="LUK 2:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 2:23" />(kpa naña ewet ke ñwed Mbed Abasi ete: “Ana eyaak akpa ayịn enịm asaña-asaña enọ Abọọñ”), <verse eid="LUK 2:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 2:24" />enyʌñ enam uwa kpa naña Mbed Abọọñ aketemme: “Ntək ibiom iba, imiidooho anye ado abomoñkuku iba.”<verse eid="LUK 2:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 2:25" />Ekamba awodeen keed amaaba ke Yeruselem, a-akekereke Simiọn, a-akedooho adinen awo anyʌñ anie mbaak Abasi. Anye aketie abet idọñesịd Isrel, ndin Adisana Sịbidịd amaadoro anye ke idem. <verse eid="LUK 2:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 2:26" />Adisana Sịbidịd amaayaara awọt Simiọn ke anye idiikpaaha tutu anye akịt Krais Abọọñ. <verse eid="LUK 2:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 2:27" />Sịbidịd amaaben anye akaa afe tembịd. Ke ini ete ye eka Yisọs ekebenne ayịn edi nọ enam naña Mbed aketemme, <verse eid="LUK 2:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 2:28" />Simiọn amaabọ Yisọs akama ke ubọk anyʌñ atooro Abasi, ate:<verse eid="LUK 2:28" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 2:29" />“Abọọñ Andikara, kpa naña afo akenwọñọ ke ikọ mfo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 2:29">yak isʌñutom mfo anyọñ ke emem.<verse eid="LUK 2:29" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 2:30" />Sia anyen mmi akịt adinyaaña mfo,<verse eid="LUK 2:30" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 2:31" />a-afo akenamma anịm ke iso afịd ederimbod,<verse eid="LUK 2:31" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 2:32" />nọ ado unwana adiyaara anọ mme Gentile,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 2:32">anyʌñ ado ubọọñ anọ mbon Isrel.”<verse eid="LUK 2:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 2:33" />Idem amaakpa ete ye eka Yisọs eti-eti ke afịd se eketañ ebaña anye. <verse eid="LUK 2:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 2:34" />Ndin Simiọn amaadiọñ ammọ, anyʌñ abo eka amọ Mmeri ate, “Ayịn ami adiido ñkpọ iduọ ye ñkpọ adidakka nda anọ uwak awo ke Isrel, anye adiido idiọọñọ ñkpọ ndoduyio, <verse eid="LUK 2:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 2:35" />nọ ato do eyaara akikere esịd uwak awo. Ndin akañkañ ayaakịm ukpọñ mfo ñko.”<verse eid="LUK 2:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 2:36" />Prọfed awonwaan keed a-akekereke Ana, ayịn Fanuel a-aketooho ufọk Asa, amaaba ke ini adinam ado. Anye amaasọñ eti-eti; akedọ ndọ isua itiaba kpọd, <verse eid="LUK 2:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 2:37" />ndin ebe amọ akekpa, ndin anye amaado ebekpa tutu anye asịm isua anaañ ye inaañ. Afịd ini anye akesiba ke tembịd, akpono Abasi akonayio ye uweemeayio, atie utreudia anyʌñ abọñ akam. <verse eid="LUK 2:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 2:38" />Ana amaadʌk adi ke ebe ado, anọ Abasi ekọọm anyʌñ atañ ikọ abaña ayịn ado anọ afịd awo se ikinie idodanyen ibaña ufak Yeruselem.<verse eid="LUK 2:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 2:39" />Ke ini Yosef ye Mmeri emaekenam afịd se ammọ ekenie edinam kpa naña Mbed Abọọñ aketemme, ammọ emaetịmme enyọñ Kalili, ekaa abio ammọ Nasared. <verse eid="LUK 2:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 2:40" />Ayịn ado amaakọt anyʌñ akop uko, ayọhọ ye aniọñ ye mfọn Abasi.<verse eid="LUK 2:40" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Akaa Tembịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 2:41" />Ke isua ke isua, Yosef ye Mmeri emaesika Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo ke Yeruselem. <verse eid="LUK 2:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 2:42" />Ndin ke Yisọs amaakeyọhọ isua duob mme iba, Yosef ye Mmeri emaeben anye ekaa Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo naña ido ammọ akesido. <verse eid="LUK 2:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 2:43" />Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo akekweeñe, ke ete ye eka Yisọs emaeketọọñọ isañ unyọñ, etəkayịn, Yisọs amaatịmme atie ke Yeruselem, ado ete ye eka amọ ikidiọọñọke. <verse eid="LUK 2:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="LUK 2:44" />Sia ammọ ekekereke ke Yisọs asʌk asaña ye mmimọ, ammọ emaekaa iso ke isañ unyọñ ke afịd usen keed. Ndin ammọ emaetọọñọ adiyem anye ke atu mme ufan ye mme ayakka ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 2:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="LUK 2:45" />Ke ini ammọ miikikịtte anye, ammọ emaetịmme edem ekaa Yeruselem ekeyem anye. <verse eid="LUK 2:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="LUK 2:46" />Ke usen ita amaakeboiyo, ammọ emaekekịt anye ke afe tembịd naña atie ye mme ñkpoon andikpeeb, asʌk akpañ utọñ anọ ammọ anyʌñ abịp ammọ mbuume. <verse eid="LUK 2:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="LUK 2:47" />Afịd awo se ikiba ke ndo ekeba ke ñkpaidem ebaña aniọñ ye mme ibọọrọ amọ. <verse eid="LUK 2:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="LUK 2:48" />Ke ini ete ye eka amọ ekedikịtte anye, idem amaakpa ammọ. Eka amọ amaabo anye, “Yịn, nsoo ido nọ afo inam ñnyịn ntom? Ami ye ete mfo imuyem fiin ye ayeemensia.”<verse eid="LUK 2:48" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" sid="LUK 2:49" />Anye amaabịp ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Nsoo ido nọ ndufo ekeñyem miin? Nte ndufo ikidiọọñọke ibo ke ana ami mba ke ufọk Ete mmi?”</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2:49 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido </char><char style="fq" closed="false">mba </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ke ndubeghe Ete mmi</char></note> <verse eid="LUK 2:49" /><verse number="50" style="v" sid="LUK 2:50" />Ado se anye aketañ ikinwañake ete ye eka amọ.<verse eid="LUK 2:50" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" sid="LUK 2:51" />Ndin anye amaakeene ammọ anyọñ Nasared, anyʌñ akop item anọ ammọ. Ado eka amọ amaamʌm afịd mme ikọ ami adọñ ke esịd amọ. <verse eid="LUK 2:51" /><verse number="52" style="v" sid="LUK 2:52" />Ndin Yisọs amaakọt ke aniọñ ye idaha, anyʌñ akịt mfọn ke iso Abasi ye ke iso awo.<verse eid="LUK 2:52" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="LUK 3" />
  <para style="s1">Yọọn Aduọkmmọọñ Aneeñe Usʌñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 3:1" />Ke ayọhọ isua duob mme ition ke ini ukara akwa Adidem Tiberiọs Sisa, Pọntiọs Pailed akekara ikpeghe Yudia, Herọd akeda iwuod ikpeghe Kalili, ke ini Filib, ayịneka Herọd akedaaha iwuod ukara Ituria ye Trakọnitis ndin Lisanias akeda iwuod ke ikpeghe Abilene, <verse eid="LUK 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 3:2" />ke ini Anas ye Kaifas ekedoññoke mme ñkpoon aku; uyio Abasi amaadisịm Yọọn ayịn Sakaraiya ke anaan. <verse eid="LUK 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 3:3" />Anye amaasaaña ke afịd ñkanñkʌk abio Yọdan, akwọrọ uduọkmmọọñ adikappa esịd nọ efeen mme idiọọkñkpọ. <verse eid="LUK 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 3:4" />Nte naña ewet ke ñwed Prọfed Aisaiya ete:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 3:4">“Uyio awo a-abọññọ ke anaan abo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 3:4">‘Idiọñ usʌñ inọ Abọọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 3:4">inam nnen-nnen usʌñ inọ anye.<verse eid="LUK 3:4" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 3:5" />Eyaefʌk afịd abedeñ ayọhọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 3:5">enyʌñ eduen afịd ekamba abod ye ntək abod.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 3:5">Eyaenekke mme usʌñ se ikwaña,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 3:5">mme usʌñ i-imiidọnọke eyaedọnọ.<verse eid="LUK 3:5" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 3:6" />Ndin afịd awo eyaekịt adinyaaña Abasi.’ ”<verse eid="LUK 3:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 3:7" />Yọọn amaabo atu awo e-ekewuọñọke edi nọ anye aduọk ammọ mmọọñ, ate, “Ndufo nditọ udʌkikọd! Anie awo ikitemme ndufo ibo efeghe iyadesịd Abasi a-adiighe? <verse eid="LUK 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 3:8" />Iwọt mfịd idiọọñọ a-asañake akekem ke aditua ñkpọfiọk mbaña idiọọkñkpọ. Ndufo ikiibo idem ndufo ite, ‘Ñnyịn iminie Ebraham nte ete ñnyịn.’ Ami ibo ndufo nte ke Abasi akeme adinam mme itiad ami ekappa nditọ enọ Ebraham. <verse eid="LUK 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 3:9" />E-ekọkọñ ekịd ke adʌñ mme eto, ndin eto akeedodo i-miinwịmme eti mfịd, eyaekpịkke anye eduọọk enyʌñ etop esịn ke ikañ.”<verse eid="LUK 3:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 3:10" />Atu awo emaebịp anye ate, “Nsoo ndin ke ñnyịn idiinam?”<verse eid="LUK 3:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 3:11" />Yọọn amaabọọrọ ate, “Awo a-anieghe afọñ iba yak ayaak keed anọ awo i-imiinieghe, awo a-anieghe ndidia yak awana adia ye awo i-imiinieghe.”<verse eid="LUK 3:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 3:12" />Mme abọọ taks emaenyʌñ edibọ uduọkmmọọñ. Ammọ emaebịp anye ete, “Andikpeeb, nsoo ke ñnyịn idiinam?”<verse eid="LUK 3:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 3:13" />Anye amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, “Ikiibọ ikan se ebo yak ebọ.”<verse eid="LUK 3:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 3:14" />Mme anwana ekọñ ñko emaenyʌñ edibịp anye ete, “Nsoo ke ñnyịn idiinam?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 3:14">Anye amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, “Ikiibọọ awo ñkpọ ke ñkanubọk, ikiinyʌñ idot awo uyio; iyʌkkọ ye se ikpe ndufo.”<verse eid="LUK 3:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 3:15" />Sia mme awo ekedotto anyen ebaña Andinyaaña, ammọ emaekere ke esịd ammọ ebo me Yọọn akap ado Krais. <verse eid="LUK 3:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 3:16" />Yọọn amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, “Ami ñkama mmọọñ inịm ndufo uduọkmmọọñ. Ado a-aba awo a-akponno añkan miin adiidi, a-adooho ami ndotto aditat udʌk ikpaukod amọ. Anye ayaiduọk ndufo mmọọñ ke Adisana Sịbidịd ye ikañ. <verse eid="LUK 3:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 3:17" />Anye a-akama ñkpọ ubeek abakpa ke ubọk adibeek abakpa, nọ asat idem abakpa akebono ke ise, anyʌn akeñ ñkpata afọp ke ikañ i-idiiduakka inịme.” <verse eid="LUK 3:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 3:18" />Ndin Yọọn amaaben mme nsio-nsio ikọitem akwọrọ eti etob anọ mme ammọ.<verse eid="LUK 3:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 3:19" />Ado ke ini Yọọn amaakesua anọ Herọd andikara ke ntak Herọdias, anwaan ayịneka amọ a-anye akedatta adọ, ye mme ndiọi-ndiọi ido mfen a-anye akenaññake, <verse eid="LUK 3:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 3:20" />Herọd amaaben ukeed ami adian, anyʌñ amʌm Yọọn akesịn ke ufọk ñkpakọb.<verse eid="LUK 3:20" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Uduọkmmọọñ ye Ntịppe Emana Yisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 3:21" />Ke ini Yọọn akeduọkkọ uwak awo mmọọñ, Yisọs ñko amaakeene akebọ uduọkmmọọñ. Naña a-anye akesʌkkọ abọñ akam, hefịn amaabeere, <verse eid="LUK 3:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 3:22" />ndin Adisana Sịbidịd amaasọiyọ adoro anye ke idem nte ibiom. Uyio amaanyʌñ ato hefịn ate, “Afo ado Ayịn mmi, a-ami mmaaha, mmenekke ñkop inemesịd ye afo.”<verse eid="LUK 3:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 3:23" />Yisọs akedo ñkpọ nte isua edịb mme duob ke ini anye aketọọñọke utom amọ. Mbon awo ekekere ke anye akedo ayịn Yosef:</para>
  <para style="b" vid="LUK 3:23" />
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:23">Yosef akedo ayịn Heli, <verse eid="LUK 3:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 3:24" />a-akedooho ayịn Mattad,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:24">a-akedooho ayịn Lifai, a-akedooho ayịn Melki,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:24">a-akedooho ayịn Yannai, a-akedooho ayịn Yosef,<verse eid="LUK 3:24" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 3:25" />a-akedooho ayịn Matatias, a-akedooho ayịn Emọs,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:25">a-akedooho ayịn Nahum, a-akedooho ayịn Esli,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:25">a-akedooho ayịn Nakkai, <verse eid="LUK 3:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 3:26" />a-akedooho ayịn Maat,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:26">a-akedooho ayịn Matatias, a-akedooho ayịn Semein,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:26">a-akedooho ayịn Yosek, a-akedooho ayịn Yoda,<verse eid="LUK 3:26" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 3:27" />a-akedooho ayịn Yoanan, a-akedooho ayịn Resa,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:27">a-akedooho ayịn Serubabel, a-akedooho ayịn Sietiel,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:27">a-akedooho ayịn Neri, <verse eid="LUK 3:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 3:28" />a-akedooho ayịn Melki,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:28">a-akedooho ayịn Addi, a-akedooho ayịn Kọsam,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:28">a-akedooho ayịn Elmadam, a-akedooho ayịn Er,<verse eid="LUK 3:28" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 3:29" />a-akedooho ayịn Yọsua, a-akedooho ayịn Eliesa,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:29">a-akedooho ayịn Yorim,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:29">a-akedooho ayịn Mattad, a-akedooho ayịn Lifai, <verse eid="LUK 3:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 3:30" />a-akedooho ayịn Simiọn,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:30">a-akedooho ayịn Yuda, a-akedooho ayịn Yosef,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:30">a-akedooho ayịn Yonam, a-akedooho ayịn Eliakim,<verse eid="LUK 3:30" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 3:31" />a-akedooho ayịn Melea, a-akedooho ayịn Menna,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:31">a-akedooho ayịn Matata, a-akedooho ayịn Natan,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:31">a-akedooho ayịn Defid, <verse eid="LUK 3:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 3:32" />a-akedooho ayịn Yesi,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:32">a-akedooho ayịn Obed, a-akedooho ayịn Boas,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:32">Boas a-akedooho ayịn Salmọn,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3:32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Usʌk mme akpa ikpañwed ewet </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Sala</char></note> a-akedooho ayịn Nasọn,<verse eid="LUK 3:32" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 3:33" />Nasọn akedo ayịn Aminadab, a-akedooho ayịn Ram,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:33">Ram akedo ayịn Esrọn, a-akedooho ayịn Peres,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:33">Peres akedo ayịn Yuda, <verse eid="LUK 3:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 3:34" />Yuda akedo ayịn Yekọb a-akedooho ayịn Aisik,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:34">Aisik akedo ayịn Ebraham a-akedooho ayịn Tera,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:34">Tera akedo ayịn Nahọ,<verse eid="LUK 3:34" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 3:35" />Nahọ akedo ayịn Seruk a-akedooho ayịn Reu,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:35">Reu akedo ayịn Pedek a-akedooho ayịn Ebee,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:35">Ebee akedo ayịn Sela, <verse eid="LUK 3:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 3:36" />Sela akedo ayịn Kenan,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:36">Kenan akedo ayịn Afasad a-akedooho ayịn Sem. Sem akedo ayịn Nua,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:36">Nua akedo ayịn Lamek a-akedooho ayịn Metusela,<verse eid="LUK 3:36" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 3:37" />Metusela akedo ayịn Inọk,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:37">Inọk akedo ayịn Yared a-akedooho ayịn Mahalalel,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:37">a-akedooho ayịn Kenan. <verse eid="LUK 3:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 3:38" />Kenan akedo ayịn Enọs,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:38">a-akedooho ayịn Sed, a-akedooho ayịn Adam,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 3:38">Adam akedo ayịn Abasi.<verse eid="LUK 3:38" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="LUK 4" />
  <para style="s1">Edomo Yisọs ke Anaan</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 4:1" />Ndin Yisọs ke uyọhọ Adisana Sịbidịd amaakpọñ Yọdan, ndin Sịbidịd amaadat anye akaa anaan. <verse eid="LUK 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 4:2" />Do, ke afịd usen aba setan amaadomo anye idomo. Ke afịd mme usen ado anye ikidiaha ñkpọ ndomokeed; ndin ke akpatre, abiọọñ amaadọñ anye.<verse eid="LUK 4:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 4:3" />Setan amaabo anye ate, “Adieke afo adooho Ayịn Abasi, bo itiad ami akappa ado uyo.”<verse eid="LUK 4:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 4:4" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ, <char style="wj">“E-ewet ete, ‘Idiidooho uyo ikpọọñ ke awo adiidat idu uwem.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 4:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 4:5" />Setan amaaben anye akaa anyọñ ekamba abod anyʌñ akewọt anye, ke ataa etək ini, afịd mme abioubọọñ ke ederimbod. <verse eid="LUK 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 4:6" />Setan amaabo Yisọs, “Ami ñyaayaak afịd ubọọñ ekondo ami ye afịd inie ke esịd unọ fiin, sia emaeyaak afịd ennọ miin; ami mmenie ukeme adiyaak anye nnọọ awo ake mmama. <verse eid="LUK 4:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 4:7" />Afo ukputuak iwuod uñkpono miin, ñyaayaak afịd ami unọ fiin.”<verse eid="LUK 4:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 4:8" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ anye ate, <char style="wj">“E-ewet ete, ‘Kpono Abọọñ Abasi mfo nyʌñ nam ñkpọ nọ anye ikpọọñ.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 4:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 4:9" />Ndin setan amaaben anye akaa Yeruselem, anyʌñ akenam anye ada ke atịñe anyọñ tembịd, anyʌñ abo anye ate, “Adieke afo adooho Ayịn Abasi, da mi tamma keduọ ke isọñ. <verse eid="LUK 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 4:10" />Sia e-ewewet ete:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 4:10">“ ‘Anye ayaanọ mme enyere amọ ewʌhọ ubaña fiin</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 4:10">nọ ukpeme fiin dek-dek;<verse eid="LUK 4:10" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 4:11" />ammọ eyaukama fiin ke ubọk ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 4:11">mbaak afo udutuak ukod mfo ke itiad.’ ”<verse eid="LUK 4:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 4:12" />Ndin Yisọs amaabọọrọ anye ate, <char style="wj">“Emaebo: ‘Kuudomo Abọọñ Abasi mfo idomo.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 4:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 4:13" />Ke setan amaakekweñe afịd idomo ami, anye amaadakka akpọñ Yisọs akebet tutu ufañ mfen.<verse eid="LUK 4:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mbon Nasared Esịn Yisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 4:14" />Yisọs amaatịmme anyọñ Kalili ye ayọhọ adudu Adisana Sịbidịd, ndin etob amọ amaasuana ayọhọ afịd ñkanñkʌk ado. <verse eid="LUK 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 4:15" />Anye amaakpeep ñkpọ ke mme sinakọk ammọ, ndin afịd awo emaetooro anye.<verse eid="LUK 4:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 4:16" />Akekem anye amaakaa Nasared, abio a-anye akekponno, ndin naña ido amọ akesido, anye amaakaa sinakọk ke usen Sabad. Ke anye amaakedakka ada adikoot ñwed Abasi, <verse eid="LUK 4:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 4:17" />emaenọ anye ñwed prọfed Aisaiya. Ke anye amaaketat ikpañwed ado, anye amaakịt itie e-ekewette ete:<verse eid="LUK 4:17" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 4:18" />
    <char style="wj">“Sịbidịd Abọọñ andoro miin ke idem,</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 4:18">
    <char style="wj">sia anye añyet miin adan anịm,</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 4:18">
    <char style="wj">adikwọrọ eti mbʌk nnọọ mbon uweene.</char></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 4:18">
    <char style="wj">Anye andọñ miin adikwọrọ uwuọufʌn nnọọ mbon ñkpakọb,</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 4:18">
    <char style="wj">ye aditịmme ñkịt usʌñ nnọọ mme nnan,</char></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 4:18">
    <char style="wj">ye ñkpọkñyak nnọọ mbon e-efiighe,</char><verse eid="LUK 4:18" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 4:19" />
    <char style="wj">ñnyʌñ ñkwọrọ isua mfọnido Abọọñ.”</char><verse eid="LUK 4:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 4:20" />Ndin anye amaafʌt ikpañwed ado, ayaak anọ akamautom, anyʌñ asuuk atie. Afịd awo ke sinakọk emaewuuk anyen ese anye. <verse eid="LUK 4:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 4:21" />Ndin anye amaatọọñọ ke adibo ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ikọ Ñwed Abasi ami asu mfịn ami, nte ndufo ekoppo ke utọñ ndufo.”</char><verse eid="LUK 4:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 4:22" />Afịd atu awo emaetañ nti ikọ ebaña anye. Idem amaanyʌñ akpa ammọ eti-eti ke utọ nti ikọ a-akewuọñọke ke inua amọ. Anam ammọ emaebịp ebo, “Idooho ayịn Yosef ado ami?”<verse eid="LUK 4:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 4:23" />Yisọs amaabo ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ke akpanikọ ndufo idiitreke aditop ñke ami innọọ miin ite: ‘Abiaibọk, kọk idem mfo!’ Ndufo eyaenyʌñ embo miin, ‘Nam mi ke idʌñ ndufo se ikop naña akenam ke Kapanum.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 4:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 4:24" />Anye amaadian do ate, <char style="wj">“Ntañ akpanikọ inọ ndufo, prọfed ndomokeed isinieghe ukpono ke abio emana amọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 4:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 4:25" /><char style="wj">Ado akpanikọ ke uwak mme ebekpa emaeba ke Isrel ke ayio Elaiya, idaha a-Abasi akesiide ikpaanyọñ ke afịd isua ita ye afiọñ itiokeed, ndin akpọsọñ akañ akeba ke iso isọñ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 4:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 4:26" /><char style="wj">Ado Abasi ikidọññọ Elaiya abịne ammọ ndomokeed ibọhọke ebekpa keed a-akebaaha ke Sarefad ke ukañ Sidọn.</char> <verse eid="LUK 4:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 4:27" /><char style="wj">Ñkpọ mfen ado, uwak mme adọñọ akpamfia</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4:27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek, ikọ a-adaaha anọ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">akpamfia</char><char style="ft" closed="false">akewuọñọ mme nsio-nsio ñkpọnta ke ikpaidem.</char></note> <char style="wj">mmọdo ekeba ke Isrel ke ini Prọfed Elisa, kpayeado ammọ ndomokeed ikibọọhọ ukọk ibọhọke Neman awo Siria ke ekenam asana.”</char><verse eid="LUK 4:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 4:28" />Afịd mbon se ikiba ke sinakọk ikop ikọ ami, emaebịmme iyadesịd. <verse eid="LUK 4:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 4:29" />Ammọ emaebịmme esịd keed emʌm anye esio ke abio, eben anye ekaa anyọñ abod e-ekebọppọ idʌñ ammọ nọ ato do enək anye eduọọk ke isọñ. <verse eid="LUK 4:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 4:30" />Ado Yisọs amaasaña ke ufọọd ammọ aboiyo akaa ndubeghe amọ.<verse eid="LUK 4:30" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Abịn Idiọọk Sịbidịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 4:31" />Akem anye amaadika Kapanum, ke abio Kalili, ndin ke usen Sabad anye amaakpeep mbon awo ñkpọ. <verse eid="LUK 4:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 4:32" />Ukpeebñkpọ amọ amaakpa mme awo idem, sia ikọ amọ akesaña ye adudu.<verse eid="LUK 4:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 4:33" />Awodeen keed a-dimọn, idiọọk sịbidịd, akefịnake amaaba ke sinakọk. Anye amaabọọñ ke akpọsọñ uyio ate, <verse eid="LUK 4:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 4:34" />“Kpọñ itie ami! Nsoo ke afo ayem ito ñnyịn, Yisọs Ayịn Nasared? Afo amedi adisobo ñnyịn? Mmediọọñọ awo a-afo adooho: Adisana Ayịn Abasi!”<verse eid="LUK 4:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 4:35" />Ndin Yisọs amaawuuk anye ate, <char style="wj">“Dop uyio! Wuọ anye ke idem!”</char> Ndin dimọn ami amaanək anye atọ ke isọñ ke iso afịd awo, awuọ akpọñ anye, ado inọọhọ anye unan ndomokeed.<verse eid="LUK 4:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 4:36" />Idem amaakpa afịd awo, ndin ammọ emaeneme ke atu idem ammọ ete, “Nsoo utọ ukpeebñkpọ ido ami! Sia ke adudu ye uko anye a-anọ mme ndiọi sịbidịd ewʌhọ ate ewuọñọ, ndin ammọ enyʌñ ewuọñọ!” <verse eid="LUK 4:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 4:37" />Ndin etob amọ amaasuana ke afịd ñkanñkʌk ado.<verse eid="LUK 4:37" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Akọk Uwak Awo Udọñọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 4:38" />Akekem Yisọs amaakpọñ sinakọk akaa ufọk Saimọn. Eka anwaan Saimọn akenie akpọsọñ ufiobidem, ndin ammọ emaebeeñe Yisọs ebo anwam anye. <verse eid="LUK 4:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 4:39" />Yisọs amaasịkke akpere mma ado anyʌñ asua anọ ufiobidem, ndin udọñọ ado amaakweeñe anye. Idaha-idaha ado mma ado amaadakka ada akenam ndidia anọ ammọ.<verse eid="LUK 4:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 4:40" />Ke utekke ndubiayio mme awo emaekoono mbon e-ekedọñọke nsio-nsio udọñọ esọk anye, anye amaanyʌñ adot ammọ keedekeed ubọk, akọk ammọ udọñọ. <verse eid="LUK 4:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 4:41" />Mme dimọn emaenyʌñ ewuọñọ uwak awo ke idem, ebọọñ ñkpo ete, “Afo ado Ayịn Abasi!” Ado anye amaawuuk ammọ inyʌññọ iyak ammọ etañ ikọ, sia ammọ emaediọọñọ ke anye ado Krais.<verse eid="LUK 4:41" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 4:42" />Ayio akesiere, Yisọs amaakpọñ do akaa ndobo-ndobo itie. Mbon awo emaedʌk eyem anye ndin ke emaekediwuọ nte anye akeba, emaenwana adinam anye akikpọñ mmimọ. <verse eid="LUK 4:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 4:43" />Ado anye amaabo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Ana ami ñkwọrọ eti mbʌk abioubọọñ Abasi nnọ mme idịd mfen ñko, sia ke ntak ado ke ekennọọ miin ndi.”</char> <verse eid="LUK 4:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="LUK 4:44" />Ndin anye amaakaa iso akwọrọ ikọ ke mme sinakọk ke Yudia.<verse eid="LUK 4:44" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="LUK 5" />
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Akoot mme Akpa Mbed Amọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 5:1" />Usen keed, naña Yisọs akesʌkkọ ada ke mben Ibiok Yenesaded,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho, Akpainyañ Kalili</char></note> uwak awo emaediyọhọ ekanna anye ekʌk adikop ikọ Abasi. <verse eid="LUK 5:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 5:2" />Anye amaakịt ubom iba a-mme akọiyak ekeyaaha ebon ke mben mmọọñ, sia ammọ ekewuọñọ eka adiyet iyịre ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 5:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 5:3" />Anye amaadʌk ubom keed, a-akenieghe Saimọn, anyʌñ abeeñe Saimọn ate anək ubom ado akpọñ mben esʌk etək. Anye ndin amaasuuk atie ke ubom akpeep atu awo ñkpọ.<verse eid="LUK 5:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 5:4" />Ke anye amaaketañ ikọ ama, anye amaabo Saimọn, <char style="wj">“Wat wuọ kaa utəño mmọọñ, nyʌñ top iyịre nọ amʌm iyak.”</char><verse eid="LUK 5:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 5:5" />Saimọn amaabọọrọ anye ate, “Eteufọk, ñnyịn imaikpa utom afịd akonayio ami, ado ikimʌmmọ ñkpọ ndomokeed. Ado sia adooho afo atañ, ñyaatop iyịre nsịn ke mmọọñ.”<verse eid="LUK 5:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 5:6" />Ke ammọ emaekenam ntoro, ammọ emaemʌm ataa uwak iyak tutu iyịre ammọ atọọñọ adikịppe. <verse eid="LUK 5:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 5:7" />Ndin ammọ emaenam idiọọñọ ekoot mme nsaña ammọ e-ekesịneke ke ubom mfen ete edinwam mmimọ. Mbon ado emaedi edidọñ iyak eyọhọ naña ubom iba tutu mme ubom ami etọọñọ adideñ.<verse eid="LUK 5:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 5:8" />Saimọn Pita akekịt ami, anye amaaduọ Yisọs ke edọñ ate, “Dakka ñkpọñ miin Abọọñ, sia ami ndo anam idiọọkñkpọ.” <verse eid="LUK 5:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 5:9" />Sia idem amaanekke akpa anye ye mme nsaña amọ ke utọ uwak iyak a-ammọ ekemʌmmọ, <verse eid="LUK 5:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 5:10" />ukem-ukem naña idem akekpa Yems ye Yọọn, nditọ Sebidi e-ekedoññoke nsaña Saimọn.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 5:10">Ndin Yisọs amaabo Saimọn, <char style="wj">“Kuuyak idem unyeñ, tọọñọ ke idahami kaa iso, afo uduusukọ awo.”</char> <verse eid="LUK 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 5:11" />Ke ammọ emaekewat mme ubom ammọ ekewuọ esʌk, ammọ emaekpọñ afịd ñkpọ enyʌñ ekeene anye.<verse eid="LUK 5:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Akọk Awo Akpamfia</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 5:12" />Usen keed, naña Yisọs akebaaha ke abio keed, awodeen a-akpamfia<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5:12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek, ikọ adaaha anọ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">akpamfia</char><char style="ft" closed="false">akewuọñọ mme nsio-nsio ñkpọnta ke ikpaidem.</char></note> akefʌkkọ afịd idem amaadi. Ke ini anye akekịtte Yisọs, anye amaaduọ akʌp iso ke isọñ akpeiye anye ate, “Abọọñ, adieke afo anyịmmeke, amekeme inam ami nsana.”<verse eid="LUK 5:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 5:13" />Yisọs amaanyan ubọk amọ atuuk anye ate, <char style="wj">“Ami mmenyịmme, sana!”</char> Kpa idahado, akpamfia amaakweeñe anye.<verse eid="LUK 5:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 5:14" />Ndin Yisọs amaadʌt anye utọñ ate, <char style="wj">“Kuutañ unọọ awo ndomokeed, ado kaa ke wọt aku idem nyʌñ wa uwa naña Moses aketemme abaña adinam afo asana, nte ñkpọ ntiense anọ mme awo.”</char><verse eid="LUK 5:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 5:15" />Ado etob amọ amaanenekke asuana, ndin uwak atu awo emaewuọñọ edi edikop ikọ amọ ye adibọ ukọk ke mme udọñọ ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 5:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 5:16" />Ado Yisọs amaasikpọñ ammọ ke ini ke ini, akaa itie se idobo akebọñ akam.<verse eid="LUK 5:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Afeen Anyʌñ Akọk Awo Akpaubeñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 5:17" />Akedo usen keed, idaha Yisọs akekpeebe mme awo ñkpọ, mme Farisi ye mme andikpeeb mbed emaebono do. Ammọ eketo afịd mme idʌñ ke Kalili, ye Yudia, ye Yeruselem edi. Ndin adudu Abọọñ amaaba ye Yisọs adikọk mme awo e-ekedọñọke udọñọ. <verse eid="LUK 5:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 5:18" />Akem mme awo emaeben awo akpaubeñ ewañ ke aya eyem usʌñ naña eben anye edʌk ufọk ekenịm ke iso Yisọs. <verse eid="LUK 5:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 5:19" />Ado akeene udịm awo se ikiba, ammọ ikikịtte ufañ naña eboiyo edʌk. Ado anam ammọ emaedọọk ekeyaara akọm ufọk, esuuk anye ke aya a-anye akenaaha, enịm ke ufọọd atu awo, kpa ke iso Yisọs.<verse eid="LUK 5:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 5:20" />Ke Yisọs amaakekịt mbuọdidem ammọ, anye amaabo awo ado ate, <char style="wj">“Ufan, e-efeen ndiọiñkpọ mfo.”</char><verse eid="LUK 5:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 5:21" />Mme Farisi ye mme akpeeb mbed emaetọọñọ adikere ke atu idem ammọ ete, “Anie awo idodo ami a-asuuhọ Abasi uyio? Anie akeme adifeen ndiọiñkpọ ke miibọhọke Abasi ikpọọñ?”<verse eid="LUK 5:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 5:22" />Yisọs amaadiọọñọ se ammọ ekekere, amaanyʌñ abịp ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Nsoo ido ntak a-ndufo ekereke utọ mme ñkpọ ami ke esịd ndufo?</char> <verse eid="LUK 5:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 5:23" /><char style="wj">Akee imem ikan: Adibo, ‘Efeen mme idiọọkñkpọ mfo,’ me adibo, ‘Dakka da saña’?</char> <verse eid="LUK 5:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 5:24" /><char style="wj">Ado ami ñyem inam ndufo ediọọñọ ke Ayịn Awo anie adudu ke isọñ adifeen mme idiọọkñkpọ.”</char> Ndin anye amaabo awo akpaubeñ ado ate, <char style="wj">“Ami ubo fiin, dakka da, ben aya mfo, nyʌñ nyọñ ufọk.”</char> <verse eid="LUK 5:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 5:25" />Kpa ke ukem idahado, anye amaadakka ada ke iso afịd ammọ, aben aya amọ anyọñ ufọk, asaña asʌk atooro Abasi. <verse eid="LUK 5:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 5:26" />Afịd awo emaeba ke ñkpaidem, enyʌñ enọ Abasi itooro. Idem amaakpa ammọ eti-eti, tutu emaebo ete, “Ñnyịn imikịt utịppe ñkpọ mfịn.”<verse eid="LUK 5:26" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Akoot Lifai anyʌñ Adia Ñkpọ ye mme Anam Idiọọk</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 5:27" />Ke ado amaakeboiyo, Yisọs amaawuọ usʌñ anyʌñ akekịt abọọ taks a-akekereke Lifai naña atie ke atayad ubọ taks. Yisọs amaakoot anye ate <char style="wj">“Ñkeene miin,”</char> <verse eid="LUK 5:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 5:28" />ndin Lifai amaakpọñ afịd ñkpọ, adakka ada anyʌñ akeene anye.<verse eid="LUK 5:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 5:29" />Ndin Lifai amaanam ekamba usọrọ anọ Yisọs ke ufọk amọ, ndin uwak mme abọọ taks ye mbon mfen emaesịne ke atu mbon e-ekediaha ñkpọ ye ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 5:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 5:30" />Ado mme akpeeb mbed ye mme Farisi emaedukuunọ enọ mme mbed Yisọs ete, “Ntak a-ndufo ediaha enyʌñ enwọñ ñkpọ ye mme abọọ taks ye mme anam idiọọkñkpọ-ọ?”<verse eid="LUK 5:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 5:31" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Idooho mbon se idem asọñ esiyem abiaibọk, ado mbon udọñọ esiyem.</char> <verse eid="LUK 5:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 5:32" /><char style="wj">Ami ñkidiighe adikoot ndinen awo, ado ñkedi adikoot mme anamidiọọk mbo ekappa esịd.”</char><verse eid="LUK 5:32" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ebịp Yisọs Ñkpọ Ebaña Utreudia</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 5:33" />Ammọ emaebo Yisọs ete, “Mme mbed Yọọn esitre ndidia ndin-ndin, ebọñ akam, ukem ado ye mme mbed mme Farisi, ado mme mbed mfo esʌk edia enyʌñ enwọñ ñkpọ.”<verse eid="LUK 5:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 5:34" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Nte ndufo ekpaekan enam mme ufan ebendọ etre ndidia naña ebendọ abaaha ye ammọ?</char> <verse eid="LUK 5:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 5:35" /><char style="wj">Ado ini asʌk adi e-ediiben ebendọ idakka ikpọñ ammọ, ini ado ke ammọ ediitre ndidia.”</char><verse eid="LUK 5:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 5:36" />Ndin Yisọs amaatop ñke ami anọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Awo ndomokeed isiwaaha ibio ufa afọñ iben idian ke akaan ikịm. Akpenam ntom, ufa afọñ ayaawakka, ufa afọñ ado ñko idiidooho ukem ye akaan.</char> <verse eid="LUK 5:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 5:37" /><char style="wj">Ñko, awo ndomokeed isibenne ufa ukọd inwañña idọñ ke ñkaan ikịm ukọd. Akpenam ntoro, ufa ukọd ayaaduat mme ikịm ado abom; ukọd ado ayaanyʌñ aduọkkọ, mme ikịm enyʌñ eboomo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 5:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 5:38" /><char style="wj">Ana enwañña ufa ukọd edọñ ke mme ufa ikịm.</char> <verse eid="LUK 5:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 5:39" /><char style="wj">Ibaaha awo ndomokeed a-anwọññọ akaan ukọd amaana akeyem ufa, sia ammọ ebo, ‘Akaan ado anem akan.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 5:39" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 5" />
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="LUK 6" />
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Ado Abọọñ Sabad</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 6:1" />Ke usen Sabad keed Yisọs amaasaña aboiyo ke mme inwañ abakpa,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akesido eduuwem ammọ adiyaak mme akaisañ se ikop mbiọñ nnọ ekịppe abakpa ke inwañ mfịd eta.</char></note> ndin mme mbed amọ emaetọọñọ adikịppe usʌk mfịd nta. <verse eid="LUK 6:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 6:2" />Ubaak mme Farisi emaebịp ammọ ebo, “Ntak a-ndufo enamma ñkpọ se mbed akpan ke usen Sabad-a?”<verse eid="LUK 6:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 6:3" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Nte akenam ndufo ikoodo se Defid ye mme nsaña amọ ekenam ke ini abiọọñ akedọññọ ammọ?</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 6:4" /><char style="wj">Anye amaadʌk ufọk Abasi anyʌñ akesio uyo e-emaekediọñ ata, uyo a-adooho mme aku kpọd ekenie unen adita. Anye amaanyʌñ anọ mme nsaña amọ ubaak.”</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 6:5" />Ndin Yisọs amaadian do abo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Ayịn Awo ado Abọọñ Sabad.”</char><verse eid="LUK 6:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 6:6" />Ke usen Sabad mfen, anye amaadʌk akaa ke sinakọk anyʌñ akekpeep ñkpọ; ndin awodeen keed u-ubọk nnasia amọ amaakekpa amaaba do. <verse eid="LUK 6:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 6:7" />Mme Farisi ye mme akpeeb mbed emaeyem se ekpedat edot Yisọs ikọ, ado amaanam ammọ enekke ewuuk anyen ese me anye ayaakọk udọñọ ke usen Sabad. <verse eid="LUK 6:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 6:8" />Ado Yisọs amaadiọọñọ se ammọ ekekere, ndin amaabo awodeen a-akenieghe ñkpaikpa ubọk ate, <char style="wj">“Dakka da ke iso afịd awo.”</char> Ndin awo ado amaanyʌñ adakka ada.<verse eid="LUK 6:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 6:9" />Yisọs ndin amaabo ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Yak ami ibịp ndufo ñkpọ ise: Akee ado se mbed atemme abo enam ke usen Sabad, adinam eti me adinam idiọọk, adinyaaña uwem me adisobo?”</char><verse eid="LUK 6:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 6:10" />Anye amaakanna anyen aseet afịd ammọ, anyʌñ abo awo u-ubọk amaakekpa ate, <char style="wj">“Nyanna ubọk mfo.”</char> Anye amaanam se Yisọs akebo anye anam, ndin ubọk amọ amaamaana akappa adeghe ataa afịd-afịd. <verse eid="LUK 6:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 6:11" />Ado mme Farisi ye mme akpeeb mbed emaekop akpọsọñ iyadesịd enyʌñ etọọñọ adidioomo ye emọ-emọ se ammọ ekpenam Yisọs.<verse eid="LUK 6:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Mbed Duob mme Iba</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 6:12" />Akedo usen keed, Yisọs amaawuọ akaa mben ekamba abod adikibọñ akam, ndin anye amaatie afịd akonayio abọñ akam anọ Abasi. <verse eid="LUK 6:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 6:13" />Ayio akesiere, anye amaakoot mme mbed amọ akpere idem, ndin anye amaamek awo duob mme iba ke atu ammọ a-anye akekoodo mme abọsịd:<verse eid="LUK 6:13" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 6:14" />Saimọn (a-anye akekoodo Pita), ye ayịneka amọ awodeen Andru,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 6:14">Yems,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 6:14">Yọọn,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 6:14">Filib,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 6:14">Batolomiu,<verse eid="LUK 6:14" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 6:15" />Matiu,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 6:15">Tọmọs,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 6:15">Yems ayịn Alfiọs,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 6:15">Saimọn e-ekekoodo Amaidʌñ.<verse eid="LUK 6:15" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 6:16" />Yudas ayịn Yems,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="LUK 6:16">ye Yudas Iskariọd, a-akedooho andikitap Yisọs nnọọ ñkpa.<verse eid="LUK 6:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Adidiọñ ye Isuuñọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 6:17" />Akem anye amaasọiyọ ye mme mbed amọ adida ke unaisọñ. Ataa uwak mme mbed amọ ye uwak atu awo emaeto ke afịd Yudia, Yeruselem, ye mben esʌk Tai ye Sidọn edi, <verse eid="LUK 6:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 6:18" />e-ekediighe adikop ikọ amọ ye adibọ ukọk udọñọ. Anye amaakọk mme awo se ndiọi sịbidịd akefịna, <verse eid="LUK 6:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 6:19" />ndin afịd awo emaeyem adituuk anye, sia adudu akesʌk ato idem amọ awuọ anyʌñ akọk afịd ammọ udọñọ.<verse eid="LUK 6:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 6:20" />Ke anye amaakebenne anyen ase mme mbed amọ, anye amaabo:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 6:20">
    <char style="wj">“Afọfọn inọ ndufo e-edooho uweene,</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 6:20">
    <char style="wj">sia abioubọọñ Abasi inie ndufo.</char><verse eid="LUK 6:20" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 6:21" />
    <char style="wj">Afọfọn inọ ndufo e-etieghe abiọọñ idahami,</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 6:21">
    <char style="wj">sia eyaekop uyʌkkọ.</char></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 6:21">
    <char style="wj">Afọfọn inọ ndufo e-etuaha ayịd idahami,</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 6:21">
    <char style="wj">sia eyaesak imam.</char><verse eid="LUK 6:21" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 6:22" />
    <char style="wj">Afọfọn inọ ndufo ke mbon awo emaisua ndufo,</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 6:22">
    <char style="wj">ammọ emaisara ndufo ke atu, enyʌñ isuenne ndufo</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 6:22">
    <char style="wj">enyʌñ esịn anyịñ ndufo nte idiọọk,</char></para>
  <para style="q3" vid="LUK 6:22">
    <char style="wj">ke ntak Ayịn Awo.</char><verse eid="LUK 6:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 6:23" />
    <char style="wj">“Idaara ke usen ado inyʌñ ikop ataa inemesịd, sia utịb ndufo akpon ke hefịn. Sia ukem ado ke mme eteete ammọ ekenam mme prọfed.</char><verse eid="LUK 6:23" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 6:24" />
    <char style="wj">“Ado adọdiọọk inọ ndufo e-edoññoke mme imọ awo,</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 6:24">
    <char style="wj">sia ndufo emebọbọ idọñesịd ndufo.</char><verse eid="LUK 6:24" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 6:25" />
    <char style="wj">Adọdiọọk inọ ndufo e-ediaha eyʌkkọ idahami,</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 6:25">
    <char style="wj">sia abiọọñ ayaidọñ ndufo.</char></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 6:25">
    <char style="wj">Adọdiọọk inọ ndufo e-esakka imam idahami,</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 6:25">
    <char style="wj">sia ndufo eyaefʌhọ enyʌñ etua ayịd.</char><verse eid="LUK 6:25" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 6:26" />
    <char style="wj">Adọdiọọk inọ ndufo a-mme awo etañña nti ikọ ebaña,</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 6:26">
    <char style="wj">sia ntoro ke mme eteete ammọ ekesinam mme prọfed abiaña.</char><verse eid="LUK 6:26" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adima mme Asua</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 6:27" />
    <char style="wj">“Ado ami ntañ ami inọ ndufo e-ekpañña utọñ ennọ miin: Ima mme asua ndufo, inam nti ñkpọ inọ mbon i-isuaha ndufo,</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 6:28" /><char style="wj">idiọñ mbon i-isueñe ndufo, ibọñ akam inọ mbon i-inamma ndufo idiọọk.</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 6:29" /><char style="wj">Awo akpisiak ndufo ufia ke mbañ keed, ikanna mbañ edem uko inọ anye. Awo akpiwappa ndufo ewịra abọ, yak anye adat afọñidem ndufo ñko.</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 6:30" /><char style="wj">Awo akpibeeñe ñkpọ, inọ anye, ndin awo akpeben ñkpọ ndufo ikiiyem aba.</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 6:31" /><char style="wj">Inam inọ mbon mfen se ndufo ekpema ammọ enam inọ ndufo.</char><verse eid="LUK 6:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 6:32" />
    <char style="wj">“Adieke ndufo emaaha mbon i-imaaha ndufo, nsoo ido udod ndufo? Akapado ndiọi awo esʌk ema mbon e-emaaha ammọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 6:33" /><char style="wj">Ñko ndufo ekpenam nti ñkpọ enọ mbon e-efọnnọ ido ye ndufo, nsoo ido udod ndufo, sia mme ndiọi awo e-enam ukem ado.</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 6:34" /><char style="wj">Ñko ndufo ekpewuọt mme awo e-ediikan imaana ikpe ndufo, nsoo ido udod ndufo? Mme ndiọi awo ewuọt akpo ammọ ke idodanyen ke eyaekpọñ inọ mmimọ ayọhọ-ayọhọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 6:35" /><char style="wj">Ado ima mme asua ndufo, inyʌñ isio ammọ eti usiene, iwuọt ammọ ñkpọ, ikiinyʌñ inie idodanyen aditịmme mbọọ. Ndin utịb ndufo ayaakpon, ndufo eyaedoñño nditọ Andikoñ Ñkan, sia anye afọfọn ido ye mme anana esịd ekọọm ye mbon ibak.</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 6:36" /><char style="wj">Itua awo mbọm, kpa naña Ete ndufo atua awo mbọm.</char><verse eid="LUK 6:36" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ubiereikpe Nnọọ Mbon Mfen</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 6:37" />
    <char style="wj">“Ikiibiide ikpe inọọ awo, mbaak awo adibiide ikpe ndufo. Ikiibiat awo, mbaak awo adibiat ndufo. Ifeen inọ awo, nọ awo afeen inọ ndufo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 6:38" /><char style="wj">Inọ ke eyainọ ndufo. Eti udomo, efiik, enyeghe, anekke ayọhọ aduọiyọ, adiido udeeme ndufo. Sia ukem udomo ñkpọ a-ndufo ekamake edomo, ke ediinyʌñ ikama idomo inọ ndufo.”</char><verse eid="LUK 6:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 6:39" />Anye amaanyʌñ atop ñke ami anọ ammọ: <char style="wj">“Nte nnan akeme adidat nnan usʌñ? Nte ammọ awo iba idiiduọññọke idọñọ ube?</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 6:40" /><char style="wj">Ayịn ufọkñwed ikponno ikan andikpeeb amọ, ado anye a-abọọhọ ayọhọ ukpeeb ayaatie nte andikpeeb amọ.</char><verse eid="LUK 6:40" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 6:41" />
    <char style="wj">“Ntak a-afo akịtte etək ndueeto ke anyen ayịneka mfo, ado ukịtte adukpọk a-asịneke ke anyen mfo-o?</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 6:42" /><char style="wj">Asaña die adibo ayịneka mfo, ‘Ayịneka, yak ami nsio etək mbio ke anyen mfo mfep,’ ke ini afo ke idem mfo umuukanna ukịt adukpọk a-asịneke ke anyen mfo? Afo awo mbubịk, bemiso sio eka adukpọk ke anyen mfo nọ afo anekke amọọnọ etək mbio a-asịneke ke anyen ayịneka mfo.</char><verse eid="LUK 6:42" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Eto ye Mfịd Amọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 6:43" />
    <char style="wj">“Ibaaha eti eto a-anwịmme idiọọk mfịd, inyʌññọ iba idiọọk eto anwịmme eti mfịd.</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="LUK 6:44" /><char style="wj">Ediọọñọ eto ekeene mfịd se anye anwịm. Sia awo isikịppeke fik ito eto ñkukịm, awo inyʌññọ ikịppe kreb ito udañaya.</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="LUK 6:45" /><char style="wj">Eti awo asịññe nti ñkpọ a-adọñọke ke ise esịd amọ, ukem ado idiọọk awo asịññe ndiọiñkpọ a-adọñọke anye ke esịd. Sia se iwuọ awo ke inua akeene se ifịghe anye ke esịd.</char><verse eid="LUK 6:45" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Adiọọñọñkpọ ye mme Ndisịme Abọbufọk</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" sid="LUK 6:46" />
    <char style="wj">“Ntak a-ndufo eñkoodo miin, ‘Abọọñ, Abọọñ,’ ado ndufo inamma se ami mboo?</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="LUK 6:47" /><char style="wj">Ami ñyaaben iwọt ndufo nte udomo ñkpọ naña awo a-adiighe ambịne miin, akop ikọ mmi anyʌñ aben asịn ke adinam aba.</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="LUK 6:48" /><char style="wj">Ammọ eba nte awo a-abọppọ ufọk, a-amaakedọk isọñ atəño ndin asịn itiad idakisọñ. Ke atọ amaakedi, mmọọñ anyʌñ atọ ufọk ado, kpayeado ikikanna iwuut anye, sia emaenekke ebọp anye.</char> <verse eid="LUK 6:48" /><verse number="49" style="v" sid="LUK 6:49" /><char style="wj">Ado awo a-akoppo ikọ mmi ndin ibenne isịn ke adinam atie nte awo a-akebọppọ ufọk ado isịnne itiad idakisọñ. Ke ini atọ amaakeditọ ufọk ado, anye amaaduọ ataa afịd-afịd.”</char><verse eid="LUK 6:49" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 6" />
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="LUK 7" />
  <para style="s1">Mbuọdidem Sentudiọn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 7:1" />Ke Yisọs amaakekweeñe se anye akenie aditañ nnọọ mbon e-ekekpañña utọñ enọ anye, anye amaaboiyo akaa abio Kapanum. <verse eid="LUK 7:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 7:2" />Do, ayịnufọk sentudiọn keed e-eteufọk amọ akemaaha eti-eti amaadọñọ akpere ñkpa. <verse eid="LUK 7:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 7:3" />Ndin sentudiọn akekop abaña Yisọs, anye amaadọñ mme ñkpisọñ mme Yuu ate ekekoot anye nọ adikọk ayịnufọk imọ udọñọ. <verse eid="LUK 7:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 7:4" />Ammọ emaedinekke ekpeiye Yisọs ete, “Mbọk di nwam sentudiọn ami ke anye adot se afo akpenwam, <verse eid="LUK 7:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 7:5" />sia anye a-ama abio ñnyịn; amaanyʌñ abọp sinakọk inọ ñnyịn.” <verse eid="LUK 7:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 7:6" />Ndin Yisọs amaakeene ammọ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 7:6">Ado mbemiso anye akesịm ufọk ado, sentudiọn amaasio mme ufan amọ adọñ ekedọkkọ Yisọs ebo, “Abọọñ, mbọk kuukpa idem adidi ufọk mmi sia ami ndotto nte afo akpedʌkkọ idak akọm mmi. <verse eid="LUK 7:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 7:7" />Anye anam nọ ami mmiikikpaaha idem adubịne fiin sia ami ndotto. Ado kap sʌk tañ ikọ kpọd ke udọñọ ayaakweñe ayịnufọk mmi. <verse eid="LUK 7:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 7:8" />Sia ami ke idem mmi mba ke idak ukara, ye mme mbon ekọñ ke idak mmi. Ami mbo keed ke atu ammọ ‘Kaa,’ anye akaa; mbo anye ako, ‘Di,’ anye anyʌñ adi. Ñnyʌñ mbo ayịnufọk mmi, ‘Nam ami,’ anye anam.”<verse eid="LUK 7:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 7:9" />Idem amaakpa Yisọs adikop ikọ sentudiọn ami, ndin anye amaakanna iso atañ anọ atu awo se ikikeene anye ke edem ate, <char style="wj">“Ntañ akpanikọ inọ ndufo nte ke kpaanam ami ñkịtte utọ mbuọdidem akponno ntom, kpa ke Isrel.”</char> <verse eid="LUK 7:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 7:10" />Ndin mme isʌñutom ami eketịmme enyọñ ufọk, ammọ emaekekịt ayịnufọk ado ke nsọñidem.<verse eid="LUK 7:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Anam Ayịn Ebekpa Aset ke Ñkpa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 7:11" />Usen ifañ akeboiyo, Yisọs amaasaña ye mme mbed amọ ye atu awo akaa abio a-akereke Neen. <verse eid="LUK 7:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 7:12" />Anye akekpere inuaatob abio ado, amaakịt naña ebiom akpo awo ewuọ edi. Eka akpañkpa ami akedo ebekpa, akenyʌñ anie sʌk ayịn keed ado kpọd. Ndin ekamba udịm awo ke abio ado emaeba ye mma ado. <verse eid="LUK 7:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 7:13" />Ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakekịt ebekpa ami, mbọm amaanam anye, ndin anye amaabo anye ate, <char style="wj">“Kuutua.”</char><verse eid="LUK 7:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 7:14" />Ndin anye amaasaña aketuuk ñkpana e-ekedotto akpo amọ, mme andikibiom emaetuak eda, ndin anye amaabo, <char style="wj">“Akparawa, ami ubo fiin, dakka da!”</char> <verse eid="LUK 7:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 7:15" />Ndin akpañkpa amaadakka ada atie, anyʌñ atọọñọ aditañ ikọ, ndin Yisọs amaayaak anye anọ eka amọ.<verse eid="LUK 7:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 7:16" />Uteñe amaamʌm afịd awo, ndin ammọ emaenyʌñ etooro Abasi ete, “Akwa prọfed awuọ awọt idem ke ufọọd ñnyịn, Abasi adise ikọd amọ.” <verse eid="LUK 7:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 7:17" />Etob amọ amaasuana akesịm Yudia ye afịd ñkanñkʌk abio ado.<verse eid="LUK 7:17" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs ye Yọọn Aduọkmmọọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 7:18" />Mme mbed Yọọn emaetañ afịd ñkpọ se Yisọs akenañña enọ Yọọn. <verse eid="LUK 7:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 7:19" />Ndin Yọọn amaasio mbed amọ iba adọñ ate ekebịp Abọọñ ebo, “Afo ado awo a-akenaaha nte adi, me ana itie ibet awo mfen?”<verse eid="LUK 7:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 7:20" />Ke ammọ emaekedikịt Yisọs, ammọ emaebo anye, “Yọọn Aduọkmmọọñ akidọñ ate idubịp fiin ibo, ‘Afo ado awo a-akenaaha nte adi, me itie ibet awo mfen?’ ”<verse eid="LUK 7:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 7:21" />Ke ukem idahado Yisọs amaakọk uwak awo udọñọ, ayọ mfịna ammọ, abịn ndiọi sịbidịd ke idem mme awo asịññe, anyʌñ anam uwak mbon nnan ekịt usʌñ. <verse eid="LUK 7:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 7:22" />Anye amaabọọrọ mme isʌñutom ate, <char style="wj">“Itịmme ikaa ikidọkkọ Yọọn se ndufo ekịt enyʌñ ekop: Mme nnan ekịt usʌñ, mme mbʌñọ esaña isañ, mme akpamfia</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7:22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek, ikọ adaaha anọ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">akpamfia</char><char style="ft" closed="false">akewuọñọ mme nsio-nsio ñkpọnta ke ikpaidem.</char></note> <char style="wj">esana, mme inan ekop ñkpọ, mme akpañkpa eset, enyʌñ ekwọrọ eti mbʌk Abasi enọ mme uweene.</char> <verse eid="LUK 7:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 7:23" /><char style="wj">Afọfọn anọ awo i-imiiduọhọ ke ntak mmi.”</char><verse eid="LUK 7:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 7:24" />Mme isʌñutom Yọọn emaekenyọñọ, Yisọs amaatọọñọ aditañ ikọ nnọọ atu awo mbaña Yọọn ate, <char style="wj">“Nsoo ke ndufo ekewuọñọ ekaa ke anaan adikikịt? Me ñnyanyaha a-afịm anyeeñeke?</char> <verse eid="LUK 7:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 7:25" /><char style="wj">Mmiidooho ntoro, nsoo ke ndufo ekewuọ ekaa ise? Awo a-asịneke uyaiya afọñidem? Iyoo, mbon se isịne uyaiya afọñidem inyʌñ inie uwak nti ñkpọ ebañña ke ufọk mbọọñ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 7:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 7:26" /><char style="wj">Ado nsoo ndin ke ndufo ekewuọñọ ekaa adise? Prọfed? Ii, ami ntañ inọ ndufo, anye idooho prọfed kpọd, anye mi akpon akan prọfed.</char> <verse eid="LUK 7:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 7:27" /><char style="wj">Anye ke ñwed Abasi atañ abaña, abo:</char></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 7:27">
    <char style="wj">“ ‘Sese, ami ñyaadọñ isʌñutom mmi</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 7:27">
    <char style="wj">ubem fiin iso nọ ato do adiikidiọñ usʌñ inịm unọ fiin.’</char><verse eid="LUK 7:27" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 7:28" />
    <char style="wj">Ami ibo ndufo nte, ibaaha awo ndomokeed ke afịd mbon se eka aman a-akponno akan Yọọn, ado awo andisịp ñkan ke abioubọọñ Abasi akpon akan anye.”</char><verse eid="LUK 7:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 7:29" />(Afịd mbon se ikikop ikọ amọ ye mme abọọ taks ñko emaedaara adinyaaña Abasi ke adikibọ uduọkmmọọñ Yọọn. <verse eid="LUK 7:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 7:30" />Ado mme Farisi ye mme nta akpeeb mbed emaesịn uduak Abasi ke idem ammọ sia ikibọọhọ uduọkmmọọñ Yọọn.)<verse eid="LUK 7:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 7:31" />Yisọs amaadian do ate, <char style="wj">“Nsoo ndin ke ami ñkpedat ndomo ye emana ami? Nsoo ke ammọ ebit?</char> <verse eid="LUK 7:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 7:32" /><char style="wj">Ammọ eba nte ntəkayịn e-etieghe ke anwa udua ebọñ ekoot emọ-emọ ete:</char></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 7:32">
    <char style="wj">“ ‘Ñnyịn imaifịt adukpoñ inọ ndufo,</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 7:32">
    <char style="wj">ado ndufo ikinekke unek;</char></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 7:32">
    <char style="wj">imaikwọ ikwọ ikpo,</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 7:32">
    <char style="wj">ado ndufo ikituaha ayịd.’</char><verse eid="LUK 7:32" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 7:33" />
    <char style="wj">Sia Yọọn Aduọkmmọọñ amaadi, idiaha ñkpọ inyʌññọ inwọñ ukọd, ndin ndufo ete, ‘Anye anie dimọn.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 7:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 7:34" /><char style="wj">Ayịn Awo amaadi, adia ñkpọ anyʌñ anwọñ ukọd, ndin ndufo ete, ‘Se adiauyʌkkọ ye akpammịn ado mi, ufan mme abọọ taks ye mme anam idiọọkñkpọ.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 7:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 7:35" /><char style="wj">Ado se edat ediọọñọ ke aniọñ anen akeene se nditọ aniọñ enam.”</char><verse eid="LUK 7:35" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Awonwaan Anam Idiọọkñkpọ Ayet Yisọs Adan</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 7:36" />Awo Farisi keed amaakoot Yisọs ufọk, anye amaakaa aketie, akañña abere ke akpokoro ndidia ke ufọk awo ado. <verse eid="LUK 7:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 7:37" />Mma keed ke abio ado a-akedooho anam idiọọkñkpọ, akekop ke Yisọs asʌk adia ñkpọ ke ufọk awo Farisi ado, amaaben pefium ke ekpeme alabasta adika do. <verse eid="LUK 7:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 7:38" />Naña anye akedaaha ke edem Yisọs atua ayịd, mmọọñayịd ado amaaduọkkọ Yisọs ke ukod. Ndin anye amaakama ided amọ akwokko mmọọñayịd ado, atʌm inua ke ukod Yisọs anyʌñ adat pefium afiọññọ anye ke ukod.<verse eid="LUK 7:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 7:39" />Ke ini Farisi a-akekoodo anye ufọk akekịtte ami, anye amaatañ ke esịd amọ ate, “Akpedo ete ami ado prọfed, anye akpaadiọọñọ se utọ awo awonwaan a-atuuhọ anye ado, ke anye ado anamidiọọk.”<verse eid="LUK 7:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 7:40" />Yisọs amaadiọọñọ akikere amọ, ndin amaabo anye, <char style="wj">“Saimọn, mmenie se mbo ntañ unọ.”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 7:40">Saimọn amaabo, “Andikpeeb, tañ.”<verse eid="LUK 7:40" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 7:41" />Yisọs amaabo anye ate, <char style="wj">“Awo iba ekekama awuọdakʌk isʌñ. Awo keed akekama anye denari</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7:41 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">denari keed akesido akʌk utom usen debra keed (se ke <char style="xt"><ref loc="MAT 20:2">Mat 20:2</ref></char>).</char></note> <char style="wj">ikie ition, anye ako akama denari aba mme duob.</char> <verse eid="LUK 7:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 7:42" /><char style="wj">Sia ammọ imiikinieghe akʌk se ekpe anye isʌñ, anye amaafeen anọ ammọ. Anie ke atu iba ami adiima anye ikan?”</char><verse eid="LUK 7:42" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 7:43" />Saimọn amaabọọrọ, “Mmekere ke anye e-ekefeene isʌñ se iwak ikan.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 7:43">Yisọs amaabo, <char style="wj">“Afo amebiide nnen-nnen.”</char><verse eid="LUK 7:43" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="LUK 7:44" />Ndin Yisọs amaawọññọ ase mma ado anyʌñ abo Saimọn ate, <char style="wj">“Amekịt mma ami? Ami ñkedʌk ufọk mfo, afo ukunnọọhọ miin mmọọñ uyieukod, ado mma ami amaadat mmọọñayịd amọ añyet ukod anyʌñ adat ided iwuod amọ akwokko ukod mmi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 7:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="LUK 7:45" /><char style="wj">Afo ukuntʌmmọ miin inua, ado tọọñọ ñkedi mma ami itreke aditʌm inua ke ukod mmi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 7:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="LUK 7:46" /><char style="wj">Afo ukumfiọññọke miin adan ke iwuod, ado anye amfiọññọ miin pefium ke ukod.</char> <verse eid="LUK 7:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="LUK 7:47" /><char style="wj">Ke ntak ado, ubo fiin ke akpesʌkado nte idiọọkñkpọ amọ awakka, e-efeen enọ anye sia anye awọt ekamba ima. Awo e-efeene etək-etək ndudue, ima amọ anyʌñ ado etək-etək.”</char><verse eid="LUK 7:47" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" sid="LUK 7:48" />Akema, anye amaabo mma ado, <char style="wj">“E-efeen mme idiọọkñkpọ mfo unọ.”</char><verse eid="LUK 7:48" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" sid="LUK 7:49" />Do ke mbon e-ekebaaha ke akpokoro ndidia ye anye ekebo emọ-emọ ete, “Awo ami ado anie a-afeene mme idiọọkñkpọ?”<verse eid="LUK 7:49" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" sid="LUK 7:50" />Ndin Yisọs amaabo mma ado, <char style="wj">“Mbuọdidem mfo unyaaña fiin; nyọñ ke emem.”</char><verse eid="LUK 7:50" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 7" />
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="LUK 8" />
  <para style="s1">Ñke Atọinwañ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 8:1" />Ke ado aboiyoke, Yisọs amaasaña ye mme mbed amọ duob mme iba ke mme nsio-nsio abio ye mme idʌñ akwọrọ eti etob abioubọọñ Abasi. <verse eid="LUK 8:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 8:2" />Usʌk ibaan e-ekekọkkọ udọñọ enyʌñ esịññe mme ndiọi sịbidịd emaenyʌñ esaña ye Yisọs: keed akedo Mmeri e-ekenyʌññọ esikoot (Makdalin), ake dimọn itiaba ekewuọhọ anye ke idem; <verse eid="LUK 8:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 8:3" />Yoana anwaan Susa, akama ukpọhọde ufọk Herọd, Susana ye uwak ibaan mfen. Mme ibaan ami ekedat inie ammọ enam ñkpọ enọ Yisọs ye mme mbed amọ.<verse eid="LUK 8:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 8:4" />Ke uwak awo emaeketo nsio-nsio abio ibịne Yisọs, anye amaatop ñke ami anọ ammọ: <verse eid="LUK 8:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 8:5" /><char style="wj">“Atọ inwañ akekaa aditọ ñkpasi. Naña anye asuanna mme ñkpasi ami, ubaak emaeduọññọ ke akpọusʌñ; mme awo emaefiik eboiyo, mme inuen anyọñ emaenyʌñ ekoono eta.</char> <verse eid="LUK 8:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 8:6" /><char style="wj">Ubaak emaeduọññọ ke anyọñ itiad, ammọ emaeyeeme sia mmọọñ ikibaaha inọ ammọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 8:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 8:7" /><char style="wj">Ubaak ñko emaeduọññọ ke ikọd ñkukịm, ado mme ñkukịm ami emaekọt efuuk ñkpasi se ikitịppe.</char> <verse eid="LUK 8:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 8:8" /><char style="wj">Kpayeado mme ñkpasi mfen emaeduọññọ ke eti isọñ. Emaetịppe, esịññe uwak mfịd, utịm ikie akan naña eketọọhọtọ.”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 8:8">Anye aketop ñke ami ama, anye amaabenne uyio ke anyọñ abo, <char style="wj">“Awo akeedodo a-anieghe utọñ, yak anye akop.”</char><verse eid="LUK 8:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 8:9" />Mme mbed amọ emaebịp anye se ñke ado akewuọñọ. <verse eid="LUK 8:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 8:10" />Anye amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Eyaak ifiọk ndedịbe ñkpọ abioubọọñ Abasi inọ ndufo, ado ntañ nnọ mbon mfen ke ñke nọ ato do,</char></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 8:10">
    <char style="wj">“ ‘ekpekekịt, ammọ ikịtte;</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 8:10">
    <char style="wj">ekpenyʌñ ekokop, inwañake ammọ.’</char><verse eid="LUK 8:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 8:11" />
    <char style="wj">“Ikop se ñke ami awuọñọ mi: Ñkpasi ado ikọ a-atooho Abasi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 8:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 8:12" /><char style="wj">Mbon e-eduọññọke ke akpọusʌñ edoñño mbon e-ekoppo, ado andidiọọk adisio ikọ ado ke esịd ammọ, nọ ato do ammọ ikiinịm, inyʌñ ibọọ adinyaaña.</char> <verse eid="LUK 8:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 8:13" /><char style="wj">Mme ñkpasi e-eduọññọke ke anyọñ itiad edoñño mbon e-ekoppo ikọ ye inemesịd ado inieghe adʌñ. Ammọ enịm ke etək-etək ini, ado idomo amaadi ammọ eduọññọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 8:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 8:14" /><char style="wj">Ñkpasi ake akeduọhọ ke ufọọd ikọd ñkukịm ada anọ mbon se ikop ikọ ami, ado mfịna, inie ye inem uwem iyakka nọ ammọ enekke ekpon.</char> <verse eid="LUK 8:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 8:15" /><char style="wj">Ado ñkpasi e-eduọññọke ke eti isọñ eda enọ mbon e-enieghe eti esịd, enie ime ye nsọọñọnda, e-ekoppo ikọ emʌm esịn ke esịd, enyʌñ enwịm nti mfịd.</char><verse eid="LUK 8:15" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Utuenikañ ke Ñkpọ Udod Utuenikañ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 8:16" />
    <char style="wj">“Awo isidomoke utuenikañ iben idịp ke esịd abañ me ke idak ikʌk. Ado esidomo utuenikañ edot ke ñkpọ udod utuenikañ nọ ato do mbon se idʌk idi ekịt unwana.</char> <verse eid="LUK 8:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 8:17" /><char style="wj">Sia ibaaha se idịbe i-imiidiiyaarake, inyʌññọ iba se efʌk awo miidiidiọọñọke me awo mmiidiinamma nọ ana ke eferife.</char> <verse eid="LUK 8:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 8:18" /><char style="wj">Ke ntoro, nekke diọọñọ naña afo akpañ utọñ. Awo akeedodo se inie eyaedian enọ anye, ado anye ake miinieghe, eyaebọ anye etək se anye akap akere ke imọ iminie.”</char><verse eid="LUK 8:18" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Eka Yisọs ye Nditọeka Amọ Ideen</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 8:19" />Eka Yisọs ye nditọeka amọ ideen emaedi edikịt anye, ado ammọ ikikanna ikịt anye akeene uwak atu awo se ikiba ye anye. <verse eid="LUK 8:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 8:20" />Awo amaadọkkọ Yisọs ate, “Eka mfo ye nditọeka mfo ideen mmọdo eda ke esiin eyem edukịt fiin.”<verse eid="LUK 8:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 8:21" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ ate, <char style="wj">“Eka mmi ye nditọeka mmi ideen edoñño mbon e-ekoppo ikọ Abasi enyʌñ eben esịn ke adinam.”</char><verse eid="LUK 8:21" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Anam Ayobio Adobo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 8:22" />Usen keed Yisọs amaabo mme mbed amọ ate, <char style="wj">“Yak iwọññọ ika edem ibiok uko.”</char> Ndin ammọ emaedọñọ ubom ewat edaaña. <verse eid="LUK 8:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 8:23" />Ubom akesio, Yisọs amaadaiya. Ayobio amaabịmme ke ibiok ado, ndin ubom akpere adisịp, ndin mme mbed emaekere ke iyaideñ.<verse eid="LUK 8:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 8:24" />Mme mbed emaeketọi anye ke idab, ete, “Etubom, Etubom, ñnyịn iyaideñ!”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 8:24">Anye amaadakka ada asua anọ ayobio ye mbufuud akpa; ndin ayobio amaasuuhọ, afịd ñkpọ adobo biai. <verse eid="LUK 8:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 8:25" />Yisọs amaabịp mme mbed abo, <char style="wj">“Mmọ mbuọdidem ndufo?”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 8:25">Ke ndịk ye ñkpaidem, mme mbed emaebịp emọ-emọ ete, “Anie awo ido ami? Anye anọ ikpan ndin ayobio ye akpa mmọọñ ekop uyio amọ edobo enọ anye.”<verse eid="LUK 8:25" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Akọk Awodeen a-Anieghe Dimọn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 8:26" />Yisọs ye mme mbed amọ emaewat ekaa abio Kerasin<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8:26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Usʌk mme ikpañwed ewet, </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">mbon Kadarin</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; usʌk ewet </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">mbon Kekesin</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; se ñko <char style="xt"><ref loc="LUK 8:37">Luk 8:37</ref></char></char></note>, a-asakkaiso ase ibiok Kalili. <verse eid="LUK 8:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 8:27" />Ke ini Yisọs akewuọhọ ke ubom asʌk atọ ñkpad ke esʌk, anye amaasoobo awodeen keed a-aketooho abio ado a-adimọn akesịneke anye ke idem. Awo ami ikisisịneke afọñ, idʌññọ ke ufọk, ado akesidʌñ ke mme udi, itie esibuuhọ mbon awo. <verse eid="LUK 8:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 8:28" />Anye akekịt Yisọs, anye amaaduọ ke iso amọ, asio ñkpo ate, “Nsoo ke afo ayem anto miin, Yisọs Ayịn Abasi Andikoñ Ñkan? Mbọk, mmukpeiye kuntʌkkọ miin!” <verse eid="LUK 8:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 8:29" />Sia Yisọs amaanọ idiọọk sịbidịd ado uyio ate awuọ anye ke idem. Akpesʌkado ekesidọññọ anye ñkpọnọ ke ukod ye ke ubọk enyʌñ ekpekpeme anye uwak ini, idiọọk sịbidịd ami amaasidịppe anye atọ, anam anye abʌñ mme ñkpọnọ ado anyʌñ abịn anye akesịn ke anaan.<verse eid="LUK 8:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 8:30" />Yisọs amaabịp anye ate, <char style="wj">“Afo akere die?”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 8:30">Anye amaabọọrọ ate, “Liyọn,” sia uwak dimọn emaedọñọ anye ke idem. <verse eid="LUK 8:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 8:31" />Mme dimọn ado emaekaa iso ekpeiye Yisọs ete akiibịn mmimọ asịññe adọñ ke ekamba ukpe nsi-nsi ufen.<verse eid="LUK 8:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 8:32" />Mme uwak udịm edi ekesʌk edia ñkpọ ke mben etək abod. Ndin mme dimọn ado emaekpeiye Yisọs ete anam mmimọ ikidọñọ ke mme edi ado. Yisọs amaanyịmme. <verse eid="LUK 8:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 8:33" />Ke ini mme dimọn ado emaekewuọñọ ke idem ete ado, ammọ emaekedọñọ ke idem mme edi ado; ndin udịm edi ado emaekeduọññọ edọñọ ibiok enyʌñ edeñ ekpañña.<verse eid="LUK 8:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 8:34" />Mme akpeme edi ado ekekịt se ikitịppe ami, ammọ emaefeeñe ekesuan etob ami ke afịd abio ye ke ñkanñkʌk ado, <verse eid="LUK 8:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 8:35" />ndin mme awo emaewuọñọ ekaa adise se ikitịppe. Ammọ ekekịt Yisọs, ye awodeen ado ake dimọn akewuọhọ ke idem naña atie ye Yisọs, asịne afọn anyʌñ adiọọñọidem nte awo ake iwuod afọnnọ; ndin idem amaanyeñ ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 8:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 8:36" />Mbon se ikikịt emaedọkkọ mme awo naña ekekọk awo a-mme dimọn akedọñọke ke idem. <verse eid="LUK 8:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 8:37" />Ndin afịd mbon awo ke ñkanñkʌk Kerasin emaekpeiye Yisọs ete yak anye akpọñ ukañ mmimọ, sia ndịk amaanam ammọ ataa eti-eti. Ke ntak ado, anye amaadʌk ubom anyʌñ anyọñ.<verse eid="LUK 8:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 8:38" />Awo ake dimọn akewuọhọ ke idem amaakpeiye Yisọs ate yak ikeene isaña ye anye, ado Yisọs amaabo anye ate, <verse eid="LUK 8:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 8:39" /><char style="wj">“Tịmme nyọñ ufọk, nyʌñ kaa ke tañ afịd se Abasi anam unọọ fiin.”</char> Ndin anye amaanyʌñ akaa akebʌk afịd se Yisọs akenam anọ anye ke afịd ñkanñkʌk abio ado.<verse eid="LUK 8:39" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Anam Abọikpa Aset anyʌñ Akọk Awonwaan Udọñọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 8:40" />Ke Yisọs amaaketo adi, atu awo emaedaara anye eti-eti, sia ammọ eketeetie ebet anye. <verse eid="LUK 8:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 8:41" />Akekem ete keed a-akekereke Yairọs, keed ke atu mme adaaha ke sinakọk, amaadiduọ Yisọs ke ukod akpeiye ate yak anye adi ufọk imọ <verse eid="LUK 8:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 8:42" />sia ukweeñe ayịn amọ awonwaan, a-adooho ñkpọ nte isua duob mme iba, amaakpere ñkpa.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 8:42">Yisọs akedakka adika ufọk Yariọs, etək ayak atu awo ekpaefiik anye iwot. <verse eid="LUK 8:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 8:43" />Ñko awonwaan keed amaaba do a-akedọñọke udọñọ uwuọiyiib ke isua duob mme iba,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8:43 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Uwak mme ikpañwed edian, mme isua </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ndin anye amaabiat afịd se anye akenie anọ mme mbiaibọk</char></note> ado ibaaha awo se ikikan ikọk anye. <verse eid="LUK 8:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="LUK 8:44" />Awonwaan ami amaato edem-edem asaña akaa aketuuk mben afọñidem Yisọs, ndin kpa ke ndo-ndo ado, uwuọiyiib ado amaatre.<verse eid="LUK 8:44" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" sid="LUK 8:45" />Yisọs amaabịp ate, <char style="wj">“Anie awo ikiintuuk?”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 8:45">Ke afịd awo emaekekañ, ke awo mmimọ ndomokeed ikituuhọ anye, Pita amaabo, “Etubom, sese afịd udịm awo ufiighe fiin mi.”<verse eid="LUK 8:45" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" sid="LUK 8:46" />Ado Yisọs amaabọọrọ ate, <char style="wj">“Awo antuuk miin; ami mmediọọñọ ke adudu añwuọ miin ke idem.”</char><verse eid="LUK 8:46" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" sid="LUK 8:47" />Ndin awonwaan ado amaakediọọñọ ke imọ ibooho ikan idịbe, anye amaawuọ adi ke ñnyeñidem, adiduọ Yisọs ke ukod. Ke iso afịd uwak awo ado, anye amaatañ ntak ake imọ ikituuhọ Yisọs ye naña imọ ikibọ ukọk ke ndo-ndo ado. <verse eid="LUK 8:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="LUK 8:48" />Yisọs amaabo anye ate, <char style="wj">“Yịn awonwaan, mbuọdidem mfo u-ukọk fiin. Nyọñ ke emem.”</char><verse eid="LUK 8:48" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" sid="LUK 8:49" />Naña Yisọs akesʌkkọ atañ ikọ do, awo amaato ufọk Yairọs adadusʌñ ke sinakọk, adidọkkọ anye ate, “Ayịn abọikpa mfo akpa. Kuufịna Andikpeeb aba.”<verse eid="LUK 8:49" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" sid="LUK 8:50" />Yisọs akekop ami, anye amaabo Yairọs ate, <char style="wj">“Kuuyak idem unyeñ; kap nịm ke akpanikọ, ndin anye ayaakop nsọñidem.”</char><verse eid="LUK 8:50" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" sid="LUK 8:51" />Ke ini anye amaakewuọ ufọk Yairọs, anye ikiyakka awo ndomokeed adʌk ufọk ye anye, ibọhọke Pita, Yọọn ye Yems ye ete ye eka ayịn ado. <verse eid="LUK 8:51" /><verse number="52" style="v" sid="LUK 8:52" />Afịd awo ekesʌk etuaha enyʌñ ebọọñ ñkpo ke ñkpa ayịn ado. Do ke Yisọs akebo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Idop ayịd. Ayịn ado ikpaahakpa, adadaiya.”</char><verse eid="LUK 8:52" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="53" style="v" sid="LUK 8:53" />Ammọ emaesaha anye, sia afịd awo emaediọọñọ ke ayịn ado amaakpa. <verse eid="LUK 8:53" /><verse number="54" style="v" sid="LUK 8:54" />Ado Yisọs amaamʌm ayịn ado ke ubọk ate, <char style="wj">“Yịn mmi, dakka da!”</char> <verse eid="LUK 8:54" /><verse number="55" style="v" sid="LUK 8:55" />Idahado, sịbidịd uwem amaatịmme adʌk ayịn ado idem, anye amaadakka ada ini keed. Yisọs amaabo ammọ enọ anye ñkpọ adia. <verse eid="LUK 8:55" /><verse number="56" style="v" sid="LUK 8:56" />Idem amaakpa ete ye eka ayịn ado eti-eti, ado Yisọs amaawuuk ammọ abo ke etañ se ikitịppe inọọ awo ndomokeed.<verse eid="LUK 8:56" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 8" />
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="LUK 9" />
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Adọñ Mbed Duob Mme Iba Utom</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 9:1" />Ke ini Yisọs amaakekoot mme mbed duob mme iba abon itie keed, anye amaanọ ammọ adudu ye ukeme adibịn afịd mme dimọn nsio ñnyʌñ ñkọk mme udọñọ. <verse eid="LUK 9:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 9:2" />Ndin anye amaasio ammọ adọñ ate ekekwọrọ abioubọọñ Abasi enyʌñ ekọk mbon udọñọ. <verse eid="LUK 9:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 9:3" />Anye amaabo ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ikiidat ñkpọ ndomokeed ikama ke isañ ndufo, me esañ, ekpad, ndidia, akʌk, me ukpʌhọ afọñ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 9:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 9:4" /><char style="wj">Ufọk keed akeedodo a-ndufo edʌkkọ, iba do tutu ndufo ekpọñ abio ado.</char> <verse eid="LUK 9:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 9:5" /><char style="wj">Adieke mbon awo imiidaarake ndufo, ikpọñ abio ado inyʌñ ikeñ ntan ñkpad ndufo nte ñkpọ ntiense inọ ammọ.”</char> <verse eid="LUK 9:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 9:6" />Ke ntoro ammọ emaedaaña isañ edʌk ke idʌñ mme idʌñ ekekwọrọ eti etob enyʌñ ekọk mbon awo udọñọ ke afịd itie.<verse eid="LUK 9:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 9:7" />Ndin Herọd a-akedooho andikara amaakop afịd se ikitịppe. Ke ntak ado akikere amọ amaatịmede sia usʌk awo ekebo ke Yọọn Aduọkmmọọñ akeset ke ñkpa, <verse eid="LUK 9:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 9:8" />ubaak awo emaebo ke Elaiya aketịmme adi, ñko mbon mfen emaebo ke keed ke atu mme prọfed a-akekpaaha akeset atọọñọ ntak adidu uwem. <verse eid="LUK 9:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 9:9" />Ado Herọd amaabo, “Ami mmaakpịkke Yọọn iwuod. Anie ndin ke ami ñkop mme ñkpọ ntịppe ami mbaña?” Ndin Herọd amaayem usʌñ naña akpenam akịt anye.<verse eid="LUK 9:9" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Anọ Awo Tọsịn Ition Ndidia</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 9:10" />Ke ini mme abọsịd emaekenyọñ edi, ammọ emaeditañ enọ Yisọs se ammọ ekenañña. Ndin anye amaaben mme mbed amọ awuọ ammọ-ammọ ekaa abio a-akereke Bedsaida, <verse eid="LUK 9:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 9:11" />ado mme atu awo emaekeyaara ediọọñọ, emaekeene anye. Anye amaadaara ammọ anyʌñ atañ ikọ anọ ammọ abaña abioubọọñ Abasi anyʌñ akọk mbon e-ekedọñọke udọñọ.<verse eid="LUK 9:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 9:12" />Ayio aketekke, mbed amọ duob mme iba emaedibo anye, “Nọ mme atu awo ami enyọñọ nọ ammọ ekaiya mme esịdidʌñ ye ñkanñkʌk ekeyem ñkpọ se edia ye itie e-ediina sia itie a-ñnyịn ibaaha mi anyọọñ usʌñ akpọñ nte mme awo edʌñọ.”<verse eid="LUK 9:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 9:13" />Anye amaabọọrọ ammọ abo, <char style="wj">“Ndufo inọ ammọ ñkpọ nọ edia.”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 9:13">Ammọ emaenyʌñ ebọọrọ anye ate, “Ñnyịn inie uyo ition ye iyak iba kpọd, ibọhọke ñnyịn ika esịd idʌñ ikidep ndidia a-adiikem afịd atu awo ami.” <verse eid="LUK 9:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 9:14" />(Ñkpọ nte tọsịn awo ition (5,000) ekeba do.)</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 9:14">Ado anye amaabo mme mbed, <char style="wj">“Inam mme awo ami etie ke eboho aba mme duob aba mme duob.”</char> <verse eid="LUK 9:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 9:15" />Mme mbed emaenyʌñ enam naña anye akebo enam; afịd awo emaesuuk etie. <verse eid="LUK 9:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 9:16" />Anye amaaben uyo ition ye iyak iba ado, adịppe anyen ase hefịn, anọ ekọọm anyʌñ abuuñ, ayaak anọ mme mbed amọ ate edeeme enọ mme awo. <verse eid="LUK 9:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 9:17" />Afịd awo emaeta enyʌñ ekop uyʌkkọ, ndin mme mbed emaetañ ñyọhọnsʌhọ ayọhọ akpasa duob mme iba.<verse eid="LUK 9:17" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pita Atañ Anwa-anwa ke Yisọs Ado Krais</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 9:18" />Akem naña Yisọs akesʌkkọ abọñ akam ikpọọñ, mme mbed amọ ekenyʌñ eba ye anye, anye amaabịp ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Mme atu awo ebo ke ami ndo anie?”</char><verse eid="LUK 9:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 9:19" />Ammọ emaebọọrọ, “Ubaak awo ebo ke afo ado Yọọn Aduọkmmọọñ; usʌk ebo ke ado Elaiya; usʌk enyʌñ ebo ke ado keed ke atu mme prọfed esed a-atịmmeke adimana.”<verse eid="LUK 9:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 9:20" />Anye amaabịp ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ado ndufo-o? Ebo ke ami ndo anie?”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 9:20">Pita amaabọọrọ, “Afo ado Krais ake Abasi.”<verse eid="LUK 9:20" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Atañ Abaña Ñkpa Amọ ke Ini Iso</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 9:21" />Yisọs amaadʌt ammọ utọñ ate ke etañ ewọt awo ndomokeed ibaña imọ. <verse eid="LUK 9:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 9:22" />Anye amaadian do ate, <char style="wj">“Ayịn Awo ana abọ nsio-nsio ndutʌhọ, ndin mme ñkpoon aku, mme andikpeeb mbed ye mme ñkpisọñ eyaesịn anye, eyaewot anye, ado ke ayọhọ usen ita anye ayaaset ke ñkpa.”</char><verse eid="LUK 9:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 9:23" />Ndin anye amaabo afịd ammọ, <char style="wj">“Awo keed akeedodo ayemme ido mbed mmi, ana anye akañ idem amọ anyʌñ aben krọs amọ kwa usen añkeene miin.</char> <verse eid="LUK 9:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 9:24" /><char style="wj">Sia awo akeedodo a-ayemme adinyaaña uwem amọ ayaaduọọk uwem amọ, ado awo akeedodo a-aduọọkkọ uwem amọ ke ntak mmi ayaanyaaña uwem amọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 9:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 9:25" /><char style="wj">Nsoo ido ufọn awo adinie afịd ederimbod ado aduọọk uwem amọ?</char> <verse eid="LUK 9:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 9:26" /><char style="wj">Adieke awo akoppo abuud ambaña miin ye ikọ mmi, Ayịn Awo ayaakop abuud abaña anye ke ini anye adiidi ke ubọọñ amọ ye ubọọñ Ete ye mme ndisana enyere.</char><verse eid="LUK 9:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 9:27" />
    <char style="wj">“Ke akpanikọ ke ami ntañ inọọ ndufo nte, usʌk mbon e-edaaha mi idiitappa ñkpa tutu ammọ ekịt abioubọọñ Abasi.”</char><verse eid="LUK 9:27" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ukpʌhọ Uduud</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 9:28" />Ñkpọ nte usen itiaita amaakeboiyo nte Yisọs aketañ ikọ ami, anye amaaben Pita, Yems ye Yọọn adọọk anyọñ abod adikibọñ akam. <verse eid="LUK 9:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 9:29" />Naña anye akesʌkkọ abọñ akam, iso amọ amaakpəho, afọñidem amọ amaakappa asesem nte akebkeb. <verse eid="LUK 9:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 9:30" />Ideen iba, Moses ye Elaiya, emaebiọññọ ke uyamma ubọọñ, editañ ikọ ye Yisọs. <verse eid="LUK 9:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 9:31" />Ammọ eketañ ikọ ebaña ñkpa Yisọs ke Yeruselem a-anye adiinam nọ adisu. <verse eid="LUK 9:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 9:32" />Idab amaayeet Pita ye nsaña amọ eti-eti, ado ammọ eketaat anyen, emaekịt ubọọñ amọ ye awo iba e-ekedaaha ye anye. <verse eid="LUK 9:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 9:33" />Ke idaha ideen iba ami ekedakkake ekpọñ Yisọs, Pita amaabo anye, “Eteufọk, a-afọn ñnyịn adiba mi. Yak ñnyịn ibọp atayad ita, keed unie fiin, keed anie Moses, keed anie Elaiya.” (Pita ikidiọọñọke se anye aketañ.)<verse eid="LUK 9:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 9:34" />Naña Pita akesʌkkọ atañ ikọ ami, ntọñanyọñ amaateññe afʌk ammọ, ndin ndịk amaanam ammọ ke adikidʌk ntọñanyọñ ado. <verse eid="LUK 9:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 9:35" />Ndin uyio amaato ntọñanyọñ ate, “Anye ami ado Ayịn mmi, a-ami mmekke, ikpañ utọñ inọ anye.” <verse eid="LUK 9:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 9:36" />Ke ini uyio ado akedoppo, ammọ emaekịt ke Yisọs akeda ikpọọñ. Mme mbed emaemʌm ñkpọntịppe ami esịn ke esịd ammọ, ikiinyʌññọ itañ se ammọ ekekịt inọ awo ndomokeed.<verse eid="LUK 9:36" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Akọk Ayịn A-adimọn Akemʌmmọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 9:37" />Edem usen ado, ke ammọ emaekesọiyọ ke anyọñ abod edi, eka udịm awo emaedisoobo anye. <verse eid="LUK 9:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 9:38" />Awo keed ke atu ado amaabọọñ ke akpọsọñ uyio ate, “Andikpeeb, mmuukpeiye fiin, di se ayịn awodeen mmi, sia anye ado ukweeñe ayịn mmi. <verse eid="LUK 9:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 9:39" />Sịbidịd keed asimʌm anye, anam anye abọọñ ñkpo, anam anye ndiyaañ tutu efuud awuọñọ anye ke inua. Isisọppọ iyaak anye, ndin ayaasobo anye. <verse eid="LUK 9:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 9:40" />Mmaakpeiye mme mbed mfo nte edibịn idiọọk sịbidịd ami esio, ado ammọ ikikanna.”<verse eid="LUK 9:40" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 9:41" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ anye ate, <char style="wj">“O ndufo mbon unana mbuọdidem ye ukwañ emana, ami ndiikpeene die ye ndufo ñnyʌñ iyọ ndufo? Ben ayịn akparawa mfo di mi.”</char><verse eid="LUK 9:41" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 9:42" />Naña ayịn ado asañake akpere, dimọn ado amaaduọọk anye ke isọñ anyʌñ anam anye atuatuak ndiyaañ. Ado Yisọs amaasua anọ idiọọk sịbidịd ado, akọk ayịn ado udọñọ anyʌñ ayaak anye anọ ete amọ. <verse eid="LUK 9:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 9:43" />Idem amaakpa ammọ eti-eti abaña adudu Abasi.</para>
  <para style="s1" vid="LUK 9:43">Yisọs Atañ Abaña Ñkpa Amọ Ayọhọ Akañ Iba</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 9:43">Naña afịd awo ekesʌkkọ eba ke ñkpaidem ebaña afịd se Yisọs akenam, anye amaabo mme mbed amọ ate, <verse eid="LUK 9:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="LUK 9:44" /><char style="wj">“Inekke ikpañ utọñ ke se ami ñyem aditañ inọọ ndufo: Eyaetap Ayịn Awo enọ mbon awo.”</char> <verse eid="LUK 9:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="LUK 9:45" />Se Yisọs aketañ ikinwañake ammọ. Amaayañña ammọ ifiọk, ado ammọ emaekop ndịk adibịp anye se ado awuọñọ.<verse eid="LUK 9:45" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" sid="LUK 9:46" />Mfaaña amaaba ke atu mme mbed adidiọọñọ me anie ke atu ammọ ado andikpon ñkan. <verse eid="LUK 9:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="LUK 9:47" />Yisọs amaadiọọñọ akikere ammọ ndin anye amaaben etəkayịn adaaha ke ñkañ amọ. <verse eid="LUK 9:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="LUK 9:48" />Ndin anye amaabo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Awo akeedodo a-adaarake etəkayịn ami ke anyịñ mmi andaara miin; ñko awo akeedodo andaarake miin adaara anye a-akendọññọ miin. Sia awo asịppe akan ke atu ndufo, anye ado andikpon ñkan.”</char><verse eid="LUK 9:48" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adidat Anyịñ Yisọs Mbịn Dimon</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" sid="LUK 9:49" />Yọọn amaabo Yisọs ate, “Eteufọk, ñnyịn imaikịt awo nte abịn mme dimọn asio ke anyịñ mfo, ndin ñnyịn imainwana adikpan anye sia anye idooho keed ke atu ñnyịn.”<verse eid="LUK 9:49" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" sid="LUK 9:50" />Yisọs amaabo anye, <char style="wj">“Ikiikpan anye, sia awo ndomokeed i-imiibiọọñọke ndufo ada ye ndufo.”</char><verse eid="LUK 9:50" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mbon Sameria Ebiọọñọ Yisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" sid="LUK 9:51" />Ke ini amaakekpere adiben Yisọs ñkpọñ isọñ ndọọk ke hefịn, anye amaasak iso ase Yeruselem. <verse eid="LUK 9:51" /><verse number="52" style="v" sid="LUK 9:52" />Anye amaadọñ mme isʌñutom amọ ate ibem imọ iso eka ke esịd idʌñ abio Sameria ekebono ñkpọ ke mbeeñeidem ibet imọ, <verse eid="LUK 9:52" /><verse number="53" style="v" sid="LUK 9:53" />ado mbon abio ado ikidaarake anye sia anye akeduakka adidiboiyo ñkaa Yeruselem. <verse eid="LUK 9:53" /><verse number="54" style="v" sid="LUK 9:54" />Ke ini mme mbed amọ, Yems ye Yọọn ekekịtte ami, ammọ emaebịp Yisọs ete, “Abọọñ, afo ameyem nọ ñnyịn ikoot ikañ nọ ato hefịn asọiyọ adisobo ammọ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9:54 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Usʌk mme ikpañwed edian ebo, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">ammọ, </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">kpa naña Elaiya akenam</char></note>?” <verse eid="LUK 9:54" /><verse number="55" style="v" sid="LUK 9:55" />Yisọs amaakanna asua anọ ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 9:55" /><verse number="56" style="v" sid="LUK 9:56" />Ndin ammọ emaekappa ekaa abio mfen.<verse eid="LUK 9:56" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ekọmudua Adikeene Yisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="57" style="v" sid="LUK 9:57" />Naña ammọ ekesañake ke usʌñ, ete keed amaabo anye, “Ami ñyaukeene fiin ñkaa itie nte afo akaaka.”<verse eid="LUK 9:57" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="58" style="v" sid="LUK 9:58" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ anye ate, <char style="wj">“Mme ewaikọd enieñe adu, mme inuen anyọñ enieñe efọk, ado Ayịn Awo inieghe itie nte anye adaak iwuod.”</char><verse eid="LUK 9:58" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="59" style="v" sid="LUK 9:59" />Anye amaabo awodeen mfen ate, <char style="wj">“Ñkeene miin.”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 9:59">Ado awo ado amaabọọrọ ate, “Abọọñ, yak ami ñka diin ñkebuuk ete mmi.”<verse eid="LUK 9:59" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="60" style="v" sid="LUK 9:60" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ anye, <char style="wj">“Yak mme akpañkpa ebuuk mme akpañkpa ammọ, ado afo kaa ke kwọrọ abioubọọñ Abasi.”</char><verse eid="LUK 9:60" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="61" style="v" sid="LUK 9:61" />Awo mfen amaabo, “Abọọñ, ami ñyaukeene fiin; ado yak ami ñka diin ñkekọọm mbon ufọk mmi unyọñọ.”<verse eid="LUK 9:61" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="62" style="v" sid="LUK 9:62" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ anye ate, <char style="wj">“Ibaaha awo a-asịnne ubọk ke ufʌñisọñ akem akanna anyen ase edem a-adotto adinam utom abioubọọñ Abasi.”</char><verse eid="LUK 9:62" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 9" />
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="LUK 10" />
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Adọñ Mbed Ata mme Duob mme Iba Utom</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 10:1" />Ke mme ñkpọ ami emaekeboiyo, Abọọñ Yisọs amaasio awo ata mme duob mme iba<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Usʌk mme ikpañwed ewet </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ata mme duob</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; se ñko ke <char style="xt"><ref loc="LUK 10:17">Luk 10:17</ref></char></char></note> mfen, ate esaña iba-iba, ibem imọ iso eka ke mme abio ye mme itie i-imọ iduakka adika. <verse eid="LUK 10:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 10:2" />Anye amaabo ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Idọk akpon, ado mme anam utom iwakka. Ke ntoro, ibeeñe Abọọñ idọk ibo anye anọ mme anam utom eka ke inwañ idọk amọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 10:3" /><char style="wj">Ndufo ikaiya! Ado itoiyo ke ami isio ndufo ndọñ nte mme edọñ ke atu mme ewaikọd.</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 10:4" /><char style="wj">Ikiikama ekpad akʌk me ekpad, me ikpaukod; ikiinyʌñ ikọọm awo ndomokeed ke usʌñ.</char><verse eid="LUK 10:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 10:5" />
    <char style="wj">“Ufọk akeedodo a-ndufo edʌkkọ, yak akpa ikọ ndufo ado, ‘Yak emem aba ke ufọk ami!’</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 10:6" /><char style="wj">Ndin akpedo ayịn emem aba do, emem ndufo ayaasʌhọ ye ammọ; akpedo ayịn emem ibaaha do, emem ado ayaatịmme ikeene ndufo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 10:7" /><char style="wj">Inyʌñ iba do ke ufọk ado, idia inyʌñ inwọñ ñkpọ se ammọ inọọ, sia anam utom adot adibọ akʌkutom. Ikiisaaña kwa ufọk awo.</char><verse eid="LUK 10:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 10:8" />
    <char style="wj">“Ndin abio keed akeedodo a-ndufo edʌkkọ, ammọ ekpinyịmme ndufo, ibọ se inọọ idia.</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 10:9" /><char style="wj">Ikọk mbon udọñọ e-ebaaha do, inyʌñ ikwọrọ inọ ammọ ibo, ‘Abioubọọñ Abasi i-ikpere ndufo idem.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 10:10" /><char style="wj">Ado ndufo imaidʌk abio ndin ammọ idaarake ndufo, ikpọñ do idʌk ke mme efaak abio ado, isian ammọ ite,</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 10:11" /><char style="wj">‘Ñnyịn imikeñ kpa ntan abio ndufo a-ayịreke ke ñkpad ñnyịn nọ ado ñkpọ ndʌdutọñ inọ ndufo: Ndin itʌm idiọọñọ ibo ke abioubọọñ Abasi ikpere ndufo.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 10:12" /><char style="wj">Ami idọkkọ ndufo, ayaafọn ye Sọdọm ke akpatre usen ubiideikpe akan utọ abio ado.</char><verse eid="LUK 10:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 10:13" />
    <char style="wj">“Adọdiọọk inọ ndufo Korasin! Adọdiọọk inọ ndufo Bedsaida! Sia akpedo ekenam afịd mme utịppeñkpọ ami ke Tai ye Sidọn, mbon ado ekpaekesịne afọñ ikpo ekappa esịd enyʌñ etua ñkpọfiọk tọọñọ ako.</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 10:14" /><char style="wj">Ñkpọ ayaafọn ye Tai ye Sidọn ke usen ubiideikpe ikan ndufo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 10:15" /><char style="wj">Ñko amaado afo Kapanum, ado nte afo ayem udịppe fiin ekedot ke hefịn? Iyoo, eyausuuhọ fiin enịm ke Hedis.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10:15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho, Abioekpo</char></note><verse eid="LUK 10:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 10:16" />
    <char style="wj">“Awo akeedodo a-akoppo uyio ndufo, a-akop uyio mmi; awo akeedodo i-isịnne ndufo, ansịn miin; ndin awo a-ansịnne miin, a-asịn anye a-akendọññọ miin.”</char><verse eid="LUK 10:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 10:17" />Mbed ata mme duob mme iba emaenyọñ edi ye idaara, ete, “Abọọñ, ke anyịñ mfo, kpa mme dimọn emaesuuk iwuod inọ ñnyịn.”<verse eid="LUK 10:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 10:18" />Anye amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Mmaakịt Setan naña ato hefịn adiduọ nte akebkeb.</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 10:19" /><char style="wj">Ami mminọ ndufo adudu adifiik udʌkikọd ye ikpeyen ke ñkpad, ñnyʌñ inọ ndufo adudu adikan afịd adudu mme asua; ñkpọ ndomokeed idiikommo ndufo ke usʌñ akeedodo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 10:20" /><char style="wj">Ado ikiidaara sia mme sịbidịd esuuk iwuod inọ ndufo, ikap idaara sia e-ewet anyịñ ndufo ke hefịn.”</char><verse eid="LUK 10:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 10:21" />Ke ukem ini ado, Yisọs ye ayọhọ idaara a-atooho Adisana Sịbidịd amaabo, <char style="wj">“Mmutooro fiin Ete, Abọọñ anyọñ ye isọñ, naña afo adịp mbon aniọñ ye mme adiọọñọ ñkpọ mme ñkpọ ami, ado ayaara anọ ntəkayịn. Ii, Ete, sia ami ado se unem fiin esịd.</char><verse eid="LUK 10:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 10:22" />
    <char style="wj">“Ete mmi amaayaak afịd ñkpọ ansịn miin ke ubọk. Awo ndomokeed idiọọñọke se Ayịn ado, ibọhọke Ete, awo ndomokeed ñko idiọọñọke se Ete ado, ibọhọke Ayịn ye mbon a-anye amekke adiyaara anye nnọọ.”</char><verse eid="LUK 10:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 10:23" />Ndin Yisọs amaawọññọ iso aneme ndịbe-ndịbe ye mbed amọ ate, <char style="wj">“Afọfọn anọ mme anyen e-ekịtte se ndufo ekịt.</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 10:24" /><char style="wj">Ami ntañ inọ ndufo ke uwak mme prọfed ye ndidem emaeyem ikịt mme ñkpọ se ndufo ekịt, ado ammọ ikikịtte, ye adikop mme ñkpọ se ndufo ekop, ado ikikoppo.”</char><verse eid="LUK 10:24" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñke Eti Awo Sameria</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 10:25" />Ndin ataifiọk mbed keed amaadidomo Yisọs idomo, abịp anye ate, “Andikpeeb, nsoo ke ndiinam nọ nnie nsi-nsi uwem?”<verse eid="LUK 10:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 10:26" />Yisọs amaabịp anye, <char style="wj">“Nsoo ke ewet ke Mbed? Afo akoot die?”</char><verse eid="LUK 10:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 10:27" />Anye amaabọọrọ ate, “ ‘Ma Abọọñ Abasi mfo ke afịd esịd mfo ye ke afịd ukpọñ mfo ye ke afịd adudu mfo ye ke afịd akikere mfo’; nyʌñ, ‘Ma mbọhọidʌñ mfo nte idem mfo.’ ”<verse eid="LUK 10:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 10:28" />Yisọs amaabo anye, <char style="wj">“Amebọọrọ nnen-nnen. Nam ntoro ndin ayaadu uwem.”</char><verse eid="LUK 10:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 10:29" />Ado sia anye akeyemme iwọt naña imọ inekke ifọn, anye amaabịp Yisọs ate, “Anie ado mbọhọidʌñ mmi?”<verse eid="LUK 10:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 10:30" />Yisọs ndin amaatop ñke ami anọ anye: <char style="wj">“Ete keed aketo Yeruselem adika Yeriko, ado ke usʌñ, mme amauke emaemʌm anye etịm, ewai anye afọñ, enọññọ anye unan, ndin ekekịt ke anye akpere ñkpa, edakka ekpọñ anye.</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 10:31" /><char style="wj">Aku keed amaadisaña usʌñ ado aboiyo, ado anye akekịt awo ñkpọnnam ado, amaabọọk idem ke mbeñ usʌñ uko afrọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 10:32" /><char style="wj">Ukem ado ñko, awo keed a-aketooho ubon Lifai, amaadiboiyo, akọkkọ anyen ase anye, anyʌñ asaña afrọ ke mbeñ ikọd uko.</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 10:33" /><char style="wj">Awo Sameria, a-akekaaha isañ ke usʌñ ado, amaakedikịt anye, udʌk amọ amaamʌm anye.</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 10:34" /><char style="wj">Anye amaabịne anye, akeyet anye mme unan, anyʌñ atọkkọ adan ye ukọd aduọk ke mme anyen unan ado. Anye amaanyʌñ abọp mme unan awo ñkpọnnam ami, aben anye adot ke dọñki amọ akaa akenịm ke ufọkisen, anyʌñ ase ñkpọ abaña anye.</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 10:35" /><char style="wj">Edem usen, anye amaasio denari</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10:35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">denarius keed akesido akʌk utom usen debra (se ke <char style="xt"><ref loc="MAT 20:2">Mat 20:2</ref></char>)</char></note> <char style="wj">iba anọ akama ufọkisen ate, ‘Kaa iso se anye anyen, ke mmaanyọñ ndi, ñyaadikpe se adodo a-afo uduubiat.’</char><verse eid="LUK 10:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 10:36" />
    <char style="wj">“Ke atu awo ita ami, anie ke akikere mfo akedo mbọhọidʌñ anọ awo a-mme amauke eketịmme mi?”</char><verse eid="LUK 10:36" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 10:37" />Ata akpeeb mbed amaabọọrọ ate, “Awo a-aketuaha anye mbọm.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 10:37">Yisọs amaabo anye, <char style="wj">“Nyọñ nyʌñ ke nam ntoro.”</char><verse eid="LUK 10:37" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs ke Ufọk Mmeri ye Mmata</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 10:38" />Naña Yisọs ye mme mbed amọ ekesʌkkọ esaña ke usʌñ, anye amaadiwuọ idʌñ a-awonwaan keed a-akekereke Mmata akebeereke usʌñ ufọk amọ anọ anye. <verse eid="LUK 10:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 10:39" />Anye amaanie ayịneka awonwaan a-akekereke Mmeri, a-akeketieghe adiana Abọọñ akop se anye aketañ. <verse eid="LUK 10:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 10:40" />Esịd ikinemme Mmata akeene uwak ñkpọ se Mmeri akeyaak anọ anye ikpọọñ anam. Ami akesịn anye amaadi adibo Yisọs ate, “Abọọñ, ado nte ufịnake fiin naña ayịneka mmi Mmeri asaana afịd utom ayaak annọ miin ikpọọñ? Bo anye adisịn unwam annọ miin!”<verse eid="LUK 10:40" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 10:41" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ anye ate, <char style="wj">“Mmata, Mmata, afo amefịna idem anyʌñ atịmede esịd mfo abaña uwak ñkpọ,</char> <verse eid="LUK 10:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 10:42" /><char style="wj">ado ñkpọ keed ke awo akpenekke ayem. Mmeri a-amek anye a-afọnnọ akan, a-adooho awo ndomokeed idiibọọhọ anye.”</char><verse eid="LUK 10:42" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 10" />
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="LUK 11" />
  <para style="s1">Ukpeebñkpọ Yisọs ke Abaña Ubọñ Akam</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 11:1" />Usen keed, ke Yisọs amaakebọñ akam ama, mbed amọ keed amaadibo anye ate, “Abọọñ, ikpeep ñnyịn naña ebọñ akam, ukem naña Yọọn akekpeep mme mbed amọ.”<verse eid="LUK 11:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 11:2" />Yisọs amaabo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Imaibọñ akam, ibo:</char></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 11:2">
    <char style="wj">“ ‘Ete,</char>
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">11:2 </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Usʌk mme ikpañwed ewet, </char>
      <char style="fqa" closed="false">Ete ñnyịn ke hefịn</char>
    </note></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 11:2">
    <char style="wj">ukpono anie anyịñ mfo,</char></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 11:2">
    <char style="wj">yak abioubọọñ mfo adi.</char>
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">11:2 </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Usʌk mme ikpañwed ewet </char>
      <char style="fq" closed="false">adi. </char>
      <char style="fqa" closed="false">Yak enam uduak mfo ke isọñ kpa naña enam ke hefịn</char>
    </note><verse eid="LUK 11:2" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 11:3" />
    <char style="wj">Inọ ñnyịn se idia ke usen ke usen.</char><verse eid="LUK 11:3" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 11:4" />
    <char style="wj">Feen inọ ñnyịn ke mme idiọọkñkpọ ñnyịn,</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 11:4">
    <char style="wj">kpa naña ñnyịn ifeen inọọ afịd awo i-idueghe ñnyịn.</char>
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">11:4 </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek ado </char>
      <char style="fq" closed="false">afịd awo </char>
      <char style="fqa" closed="false">ake ikamake ñnyịn isʌñ</char>
    </note></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 11:4">
    <char style="wj">Kuuyak ñnyịn idʌk ke idomo.</char>
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">11:4 </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Usʌk mme ikpañwed edian </char>
      <char style="fq" closed="false">idomo </char>
      <char style="fqa" closed="false">ado fak ñnyịn sio ke ubọk andidiọọk</char>
    </note>
    <char style="wj">’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 11:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 11:5" />Akema Yisọs amaabo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Akpedo anam awo ndufo keed anie ufan, akem ufan ado adi ke ufọọd akonayio adibo ate, ‘Ufan, mbọk ñwọọt ebəho uyo ita,</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 11:6" /><char style="wj">ke nnie ufan mmi a-atooho anyan usʌñ isañ adi, ndin nnieghe ñkpọ se nnọ anye.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 11:7" /><char style="wj">Akpedo anam ufan amọ asịne ke esịd ufọk abọọrọ, ‘Kumfịna miin. Ñnyịn imaikọkọk usʌñ; ñko ami ye nditọ mmi imidọdʌk idab. Mbooho ñkan ndakka nda ndunọ fiin ñkpọ ndomokeed idahami.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 11:8" /><char style="wj">Idọkkọ ndufo ke akpesʌkado a-anye imiididakkake ida ke ntak a-anye adooho ufan amọ, ado ke ntak ufan amọ asʌkkọ asọñ ayịre anye, anye ayaadakka ada akenọ anye se anye ayeyem.</char><verse eid="LUK 11:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 11:9" />
    <char style="wj">“Ke ntak ado, ami ibo ndufo: Ibeeñe ke eyainọ; iyem ke eyaekịt; ikọñ ke eyaebeere usʌñ inọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 11:10" /><char style="wj">Sia awo keed akeedodo a-abeeñeke ayaabọ; awo a-ayemme ayaakịt; ñko awo a-akọññọ, eyaebeere usʌñ enọ anye.</char><verse eid="LUK 11:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 11:11" />
    <char style="wj">“Anie ke atu ndufo e-edoññoke mme ete, ke ayịn ndufo akpibeeñe iyak anye aben udʌkikọd anọ?</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 11:12" /><char style="wj">Me akpebeeñe ñkwaunen anye aben ikpeyen anọ?</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 11:13" /><char style="wj">Adieke ndufo e-edoññoke ndiọi ediọọñọke adinọ nditọ ndufo nti enọ, die ndin ke Ete ndufo ke hefịn imiidiinọọhọ Adisana Sịbidịd esọk mbon e-ebeeñeke anye.”</char><verse eid="LUK 11:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs ye Belsibọb</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 11:14" />Ke ini Yisọs akebịnne imuum dimọn asio awo ke idem, imuum ado amaatañ ikọ; ndin idem amaakpa afịd atu awo. <verse eid="LUK 11:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 11:15" />Ado ubaak ammọ emaebo, “Anye akama Belsibọb, akpan abọọñ mme dimọn, abịn mme dimọn asịññe.” <verse eid="LUK 11:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 11:16" />Usʌk mbon awo emaedomo anye idomo ke adiyem idiọọñọ a-atooho hefịn.<verse eid="LUK 11:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 11:17" />Ado Yisọs amaadiọọñọ akikere ammọ, ndin abo ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Abio ndomokeed a-abakkake ada ke idem amọ ikpọọñ inieghe nsọọñọnda; ufọk u-ubakka abaaha ana aduọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 11:18" /><char style="wj">Setan akpenwana ekọñ ye idem amọ, abioubọọñ amọ adiisaña die ida? Ntañ ami sia ndufo ebo ke ami ñkama Belsibọb mbịn mme dimọn nsịññe.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 11:19" /><char style="wj">Akpedo ndat Belsibọb mbịn mme dimọn nsịññe, ke adudu anie ke mme nsaña ndufo edat ebịn ammọ esịññe? Ke ntak ami, ammọ eyaedo mme abiideikpe inọ ndufo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 11:20" /><char style="wj">Ado akpedo ndat adudu ubọk Abasi mbịn mme dimọn nsịññe, abioubọọñ Abasi a-adisịm ndufo.</char><verse eid="LUK 11:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 11:21" />
    <char style="wj">“Akpọsọñ awo amaakama ñkpọ uko ekọñ amọ akpeme ufọk amọ, inie amọ ana ke emem.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 11:22" /><char style="wj">Ado awo a-asọññọ adudu akan anye amaadinwana ye anye, akan anye ubọk, ayaakoono mme ñkpọ ekọñ a-anye akedotto anyen, anyʌñ abakka ñkpoduoho se anye ama adat.</char><verse eid="LUK 11:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 11:23" />
    <char style="wj">“Awo akeedodo imiidaaha ye ami, anwanwana ye ami, ndin awo akeedodo imiiñkeeneke miin itañ ibək, asuasuan.</char><verse eid="LUK 11:23" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Aditịmme Ndi Idiọọk Sịbidịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 11:24" />
    <char style="wj">“Idiọọk sịbidịd amaawuọ awo ke idem, anye asaaña ayọọn ayem itie nte abọ nduọkadudu, ado ikịtte. Ke ini anye imiikịtte itie, anye ate, ‘Ami ñyaatịmme ñnyọñ ufọk añkekpọññọ.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 11:25" /><char style="wj">Ndin anye amaato adi, adikịt naña emaekekwọọk itie ado asana, etuum ñkpọ ebono.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 11:26" /><char style="wj">Akem anye akaa akekoono mme sịbidịd itiaba mfen e-ebakka ibak ekan anye, ndin ammọ ekaa ekedʌñọ do. Ndin utịd awo ado akappa adiọọk akan akpa.”</char><verse eid="LUK 11:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 11:27" />Ke ini Yisọs akesʌkkọ atañ mme ikọ ami, awonwaan ke atu ado amaabọñ ke akpọsọñ uyio ate, “Afọfọn anọ eka a-akumanna anyʌñ ubọọk fiin.”<verse eid="LUK 11:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 11:28" />Ado anye amaabọọrọ, <char style="wj">“Akap afọfọn anọ mbon e-ekoppo ikọ Abasi enyʌñ enam se ekop.”</char><verse eid="LUK 11:28" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Idiọọñọ Yọna</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 11:29" />Ke mme atu awo emaekenekke ewak, Yisọs amaabo, <char style="wj">“Emana ami ado ndoom emana. Anye ayem idiọọñọ, ado idiikịtte idiọọñọ mfen ikan anye e-ekenọọhọ Yọna.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 11:30" /><char style="wj">Sia kpa naña Yọna akedo idiọọñọ anọ mbon Ninife, kpa ntoro ke Ayịn Awo adiido inọ emana ami.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 11:31" /><char style="wj">Abọọñanwaan Usuuk ñko ayaadakka ada abiom emana ami ikpe, sia anye amaato ke ataa utịd ederimbod adi adikpañ utọñ ñkop aniọñ Sọlọmọn; idahami, se ikpon ikan Sọlọmọn a-aba ami.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 11:32" /><char style="wj">Mbon Ninife eyaetie ke ikpe ebaña mbon emana ami enyʌñ ebiom ammọ ikpe; sia ammọ emaekappa esịd ato ke ukwọrọikọ Yọna; ndin idahami, se ikpon ikan Yọna mmọ mi.</char><verse eid="LUK 11:32" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Utuenikañ Idem Awo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 11:33" />
    <char style="wj">“Awo ndomokeed idomoke utuenikañ inịm ke itie se idedịbe, me iben isịn ke usan ikʌp. Ado edomo utuenikañ edot ke ñkpọ udod utuenikañ, nọ mbon se idʌk idi emọọnọ ñkpọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 11:34" /><char style="wj">Anyen mfo ado utuenikañ idem mfo. Anyen mfo amaanie nsọñidem,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11:34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek </char><char style="fq" closed="false">nsọñidem</char><char style="ft" closed="false">awuọñọ edifọọn ubọk enọ</char></note> <char style="wj">afịd idem mfo ñko ayọhọ ye unwana. Ado anyen mfo imiinieghe</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11:34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek </char><char style="fq" closed="false">nsọñidem</char><char style="ft" closed="false">awuọñọ mfọnido </char></note> <char style="wj">nsọñidem, afịd idem mfo ayọhọ ye ekịm.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 11:35" /><char style="wj">Kpeme, mbaak unwana a-abaaha ke idem mfo adido ekịm.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 11:36" /><char style="wj">Ndin adieke afịd idem mfo ayọhọke ye unwana, inyʌññọ iba itie e-ekịm abaaha, afịd itie ayaayamma kpa naña unwana ikañ ayamma atọ awo.”</char><verse eid="LUK 11:36" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Asueñ mme Farisi ye Nta Akpeeb Mbed</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 11:37" />Yisọs aketañ ikọ ama, Farisi keed amaakoot anye ufọk ate adidia ñkpọ ye imọ, ndin anye amaakaa aketie afekke abere ke akpokoro ndidia. <verse eid="LUK 11:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 11:38" />Farisi ado akekịt ke anye ikitooho iyie ubọk mbemiso adia ñkpọ <char style="add">(naña ido mme Yuu asido)</char> idem amaakpa anye.<verse eid="LUK 11:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 11:39" />Ndin Abọọñ amaabo anye ate, <char style="wj">“Ndufo mme Farisi eyet edem usan ye edem kọọb asana, ado esịd ndufo ayọhọ ye udọrọitọñ ye ibak.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 11:40" /><char style="wj">Ndufo mme ndisịme! Idooho andikinam edem anam kpa esịd ñko?</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 11:41" /><char style="wj">Ado amaado se isịne ndufo ke idem, ifọn ido ye mbon uweene, ndin afịd ñkpọ ayaado adisana inọ ndufo.</char><verse eid="LUK 11:41" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 11:42" />
    <char style="wj">“Adọdiọọk inọ ndufo mme Farisi, sia ndufo enọ Abasi mbakka keed ke itie duob ke sutọ-sutọ mfañ ñkpọ inwañ, ado ndufo efre unen ye ima Abasi. Ndufo ekpesʌk enọọnọ Abasi ubaak keed ke itie duob enyʌñ edian unen ye ima.</char><verse eid="LUK 11:42" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 11:43" />
    <char style="wj">“Adọdiọọk inọ ndufo mme Farisi, sia ndufo emaaha ñkpoon itie ke mme sinakọk ye ekọọm ukpono ke mme anwa udua.</char><verse eid="LUK 11:43" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="LUK 11:44" />
    <char style="wj">“Adọdiọọk inọ ndufo, sia ndufo etie nte udi a-awo imiinịmme idiọọñọ, ndin mme awo esaña ke anyọñ ado eboiyo ado idiọọñọke ke udi ke ado.”</char><verse eid="LUK 11:44" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" sid="LUK 11:45" />Ataifiọk mbed keed amaabọọrọ Yisọs ate, “Andikpeeb, afo umautañ mme ñkpọ ami, afo amisọñ ñnyịn anyen ñko.”<verse eid="LUK 11:45" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" sid="LUK 11:46" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ anye ate, <char style="wj">“Adọdiọọk inọ ndufo mme ntaifiọk mbed, sia ndufo efiighe mme awo ye mbiomo a-ammọ imiikanna ibiom; ndin ndufo idịppeke nnuun ubọk keed inwam ammọ ke usʌñ ndomokeed.</char><verse eid="LUK 11:46" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" sid="LUK 11:47" />
    <char style="wj">“Adọdiọọk inọ ndufo, sia ndufo emekọọk udi enọ mme prọfed, ado mme eteete ndufo ekewoot ammọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="LUK 11:48" /><char style="wj">Awuọ ke ndufo emetie ntiense esọọñọ se mme eteete ndufo ekenam; ammọ emaewoot mme prọfed, ndin ndufo edikọkọọk udi enọ mme prọfed ado.</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:48" /><verse number="49" style="v" sid="LUK 11:49" /><char style="wj">Ke ntak ami, Abasi ke aniọñ amọ amaabo, ‘Ami ñyaanọ mme prọfed ye mme abọsịd esọk ammọ, ubaak mme prọfed ye mme abọsịd ammọ eyaewoot, usʌk ammọ eyaetʌkkọ.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:49" /><verse number="50" style="v" sid="LUK 11:50" /><char style="wj">Ke ntak ado, eyaebịp mbon emana ami ebaña iyiib afịd mme prọfed se ekewowot tọọñọ ke ntọọñọ ederimbod,</char> <verse eid="LUK 11:50" /><verse number="51" style="v" sid="LUK 11:51" /><char style="wj">tọọñọ ke iyiib Ebeel tutu awuọ ake Sakaraiya, e-ekewotto ke ufọọd itie uwa ye esịd tembịd. Ii, ke akpanikọ, afịd ñkpọ ami adiidoro emana ami ke iwuod.</char><verse eid="LUK 11:51" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="52" style="v" sid="LUK 11:52" />
    <char style="wj">“Adọdiọọk inọ ndufo mme ntaifiọk mbed, sia ndufo emeben ukpọhọde ifiọk efep. Ndufo ke idem ndufo idʌkkọ, emenyʌñ ebiọọñọ mbon mfen e-ekesʌkkọ edọdʌk.”</char><verse eid="LUK 11:52" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="53" style="v" sid="LUK 11:53" />Yisọs akekpọñ itie ado, mme Farisi ye mme akpeeb mbed emaefaaña se anye aketañ enyʌñ ekaa iso etọ anye mme mbuume, <verse eid="LUK 11:53" /><verse number="54" style="v" sid="LUK 11:54" />ebet adimʌm anye ke se anye adiitañ.<verse eid="LUK 11:54" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 11" />
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="LUK 12" />
  <para style="s1">Ndʌdutọñ ye Nsọọñọukod</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 12:1" />Ke ini atu awo emaekeyọhọ uwak tọsịn tutu mme awo edufiighe emọ-emọ, Yisọs amaatọọñọ adikwọrọ ikọ ke akpa ifed nnọọ mme mbed amọ, ate, <char style="wj">“Ikpeme yiis mme Farisi, a-adooho mbubịk.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 12:2" /><char style="wj">Ibaaha se efọfʌk i-imiidiiyaarake, inyʌññọ iba se ededịp i-imiidiinaaha ke eferife.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 12:3" /><char style="wj">Ibaaha se afo atañ ke ekịm, a-awo imiidiikoppo ke uweemeayio, ndin adu a-afo adọññọ ke utọñ ke esịd ubeed eyaesuan ke mme akọm ufọk.</char><verse eid="LUK 12:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 12:4" />
    <char style="wj">“Mme ufan mmi, ami ibo ndufo nte, ikiibaak mbon e-ekanna ewot ikpọkidem kpọd ado ikanna adinam ñkan ado.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 12:5" /><char style="wj">Ado ami ñyaiwọt ndufo anye a-ndufo ekpebaaha: Ibaak anye a-adooho amaawot ikpọkidem ama, amaana anie adudu aditop nsịn ke ukpe nsi-nsi ikañ. Ii, ke akpanikọ, ibaak anye ado.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 12:6" /><char style="wj">Idooho nsiak ition ke enyam ke kọbọ iba? Kpayeado, Abasi ifreke ammọ ndomokeed.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 12:7" /><char style="wj">Ke akpanikọ, e-ebat afịd ided iwuod ndufo. Ke ntoro, ikiifeghe ndịk; sia ekọmudua ndufo akpon akan uwak nsiak.</char><verse eid="LUK 12:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 12:8" />
    <char style="wj">“Ami idọkkọ ndufo nte, awo se idiiñyimme miin anwa-anwa, Ayịn Awo ayaanyʌñ anyịmme anye ke iso mme enyere Abasi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 12:9" /><char style="wj">Ado awo añkañña miin ke iso mbon awo, eyaenyʌñ ekañ anye ke iso mme enyere Abasi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 12:10" /><char style="wj">Ndin eyaefeen enọ awo a-atañña ikọ adian Ayịn Awo, ado awo akeedodo a-atañña ikọ emiom adian Adisana Sịbidịd idiinieghe adifeen.</char><verse eid="LUK 12:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 12:11" />
    <char style="wj">“Emaiben ndufo eka ke mme sinakọk, ke iso mme andikara ye ikpọ mme adaidaha, ikiikere naña ediifak idem ndufo me se ediitañ,</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 12:12" /><char style="wj">sia Adisana Sịbidịd ayaitemme ndufo se ediitañ.”</char><verse eid="LUK 12:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñke A-abañake Ndisịme Imọ Awo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 12:13" />Awo ke atu ado amaabo Yisọs ate, “Andikpeeb, dọkkọ ayịneka mmi yak abakka udeeme ñkpọ akpa mmi annọ.”<verse eid="LUK 12:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 12:14" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ anye ate, <char style="wj">“Ete, anie akemmek miin nte abiideikpe me adeemeñkpọ ke ufọọd ndufo?”</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 12:15" />Yisọs amaadian do ate, <char style="wj">“Ikpeme! Iba ke mfadidem ibaña mme nsio-nsio idiọọk itọñ; uwem awo ikọñọke ke uwak ñkpọ se anye anie.”</char><verse eid="LUK 12:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 12:16" />Ñko anye amaatop ñke ami anọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Isọñ imọ awo keed amaadʌk ñkpọ inwañ eti-eti.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 12:17" /><char style="wj">Imọ awo ami amaakere ke esịd ammọ ate, ‘Nsoo ke ami ndiinam? Ami nnieghe itie se mbon afịd uwak ñkpọ inwañ ami.’</char><verse eid="LUK 12:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 12:18" />
    <char style="wj">“Ndin anye amaabo, ‘Se ami mbo nnam ado ami. Ñyaawuut mme ise mmi, mmaana mbọp mme ise se ikpoon, ndin ñyaakoono akpakʌb ñkpọ inwañ mmi ñkebono ke ndo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 12:19" /><char style="wj">Amaama ami ñyaabo idem mmi nte, “Afo amenie uwak nti ñkpọ se idiiba ikpeene ke uwak isua. Dat uwem usʌk-usʌk, dia, nwọñ nyʌñ kop inem uwem.” ’</char><verse eid="LUK 12:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 12:20" />
    <char style="wj">“Ado Abasi amaabo anye, ‘Afo ndisịme awo! Kpa akonayio ami eyaeyem uwem mfo uto fiin. Anie ndin adiinie afịd se afo akekọọ anịm anọ idem ado?’</char><verse eid="LUK 12:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 12:21" />
    <char style="wj">“Kpa ntom ke adiiwuọọñọ inọ awo a-akọọhọ mme inie abon anọ idem amọ ado inieghe inie ke ñkañ Abasi.”</char><verse eid="LUK 12:21" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Kuufịna Idem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 12:22" />Ndin Yisọs amaabo mme mbed amọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ke ntoro ami ibo ndufo ikiifịna idem ibaña uwem ndufo, me nsoo ke ediidia; me ikpọkidem ndufo, me nsoo ke ediisịne.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 12:23" /><char style="wj">Sia uwem akan ndidia, ikpọkidem anyʌñ akan afọñ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 12:24" /><char style="wj">Ikere ibaña mme inuen anyọñ. Ammọ itọọhọtọ, idọkkọdọk, inyʌññọ inie aba me ise; ado Abasi abọọk ammọ. Nwaanwa dise ndufo a-adooho ekọmudua ndufo akpon akan ake mme inuen!</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 12:25" /><char style="wj">Anie ke atu ndufo ikeme adidian awa keed ke uwem amọ ato ke adifịna?</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 12:26" /><char style="wj">Adieke ndufo imiikanna inam etək-etək ñkpọ ami, ntak a-ndufo efịnake ebaña mbon ñko-o?</char><verse eid="LUK 12:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 12:27" />
    <char style="wj">“Se naña mme ñkpokpoñ ikọd ekọt. Ammọ inamma utom inyʌññọ ituak afọñ. Ado ami idọkkọ ndufo ke Sọlọmọn ke afịd ubọọñ amọ ikisịneke afọñ se iyaiya nte keed ke atu mme ñkpokpoñ ikọd ami.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 12:28" /><char style="wj">Adieke Abasi anọọhọ ñkpokpoñ ke ikọd nsiine, a-adooho ammọ eba mfịn, ñkpọñ ekpooño ammọ efọọmọ ke ikañ, nsoo ikpinam ke anye anekke ase ñkpọ ibaña ndufo; ndufo mbon etək mbuọdidem!</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 12:29" /><char style="wj">Ikiinyʌñ isịn esịd ndufo ke se ediidia me se ediinwọñ; ikiikere ibaña ado.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 12:30" /><char style="wj">Sia mbon ederimbod imiidiọọñọke Abasi esịn esịd ke mme ñkpọ ntom, ndin Ete ndufo adọdiọọñọ ke ndufo emeyem mme ñkpọ ami.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 12:31" /><char style="wj">Ado ndufo ikap isịn esịd iyem abioubọọñ Abasi, ndin eyaedian afịd mme ñkpọ ami inọ ndufo.</char><verse eid="LUK 12:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 12:32" />
    <char style="wj">“Ikiikop ndịk, etək udịm edọñ, sia Ete ndufo a-akop inemesịd adinọ ndufo abioubọọñ Abasi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 12:33" /><char style="wj">Inyam inie ndufo inyʌñ idat inwam mme uweene. Inọ idem ndufo ekpad akʌk i-imiidiitahake, ñkpọuto ke hefịn i-imiidiikpuuho, ke itie inọ imiidiikpereke, utañkpọ inyʌññọ isobo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 12:34" /><char style="wj">Sia itie nte ñkpọuto mfo ana, kpa ke ndo ke esịd mfo adiisịne.</char><verse eid="LUK 12:34" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adiba ke Ukpeme</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 12:35" />
    <char style="wj">“Isiine afọñ, ibeeñe idem utom, inam mme utuenikañ ndufo esak,</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 12:36" /><char style="wj">nte mbon e-ebeeñeke idem ebet eteufọk ammọ adiito usọrọ ndọ ndi, nọ ato do anye amaato adi idikọñ usʌñ ammọ ebeere ini keed enọ anye.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 12:37" /><char style="wj">Adiifọfọn inọ nditọufọk e-eteufọk adiito idikịt ammọ naña eba ke mbeeñeidem. Ke akpanikọ ke ibo ndufo, eteufọk ayaasịne afọñ aba ke mbeeñeidem, abo nditọufọk esuuk etie ke akpokoro ndidia, ndin anye ayaase ñkpọ abaña ammọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 12:38" /><char style="wj">Adiifọfọn inọ mme nditọufọk e-eteufọk adiito idikịt naña ammọ eba ke mbeeñeidem, akpekọm ke ufọọd akonayio me idaha ayio ayemme adisiere.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 12:39" /><char style="wj">Ado idiọọñọ ntom: Adieke anieufọk akpekediọọñọke idaha ini ke akonayio i-inọ adiidi ufọk amọ, anye akpaakekpeme ufọk amọ, ndin ikpikiyakka nọ inọ adʌk.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 12:40" /><char style="wj">Ana ndufo ñko ebeeñe idem, sia Ayịn Awo adiidi ke awa a-ndufo imiidiibeeñeke ibet anye.”</char><verse eid="LUK 12:40" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 12:41" />Pita amaabịp ate, “Abọọñ, afo atop ñke ami inọ ñnyịn me atop anọ afịd awo?”<verse eid="LUK 12:41" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 12:42" />Abọọñ amaabọọrọ ate, <char style="wj">“Anie ndin ado anam akpanikọ ye anie aniọñ etubom mbon utom, e-eteufọk anịmme ke iwuod nọ asikpe akʌk ndidia anọ mbon utom ke akem ini?</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 12:43" /><char style="wj">Ayaafọn anọ ayịnufọk e-eteufọk anyọññọ adikịt naña anye anam se ekebo anye anam.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="LUK 12:44" /><char style="wj">Ke akpanikọ ke ibo ndufo, ayaanịm anye ke iwuod afịd ñkpọ se anye anie.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="LUK 12:45" /><char style="wj">Ado ayịnufọk akpekere ke eteufọk imọ atinyọñ idi ayaakpeene, ndin atọọñọ adifiomo mme nditọufọk mbon ñko, ata, anwọñ, akpa mmịn,</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="LUK 12:46" /><char style="wj">eteufọk amọ ayaanyọñ adi ke usen a-ayịnufọk ami imiikikpeññe idem ye ke awa a-anye imiidiọọñọke. Eteufọk amọ ayaanọ anye ufen anyʌñ abịn anye nọ akeba ye mbon imiinịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ.</char><verse eid="LUK 12:46" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" sid="LUK 12:47" />
    <char style="wj">“Ayịnufọk a-adiọọñọke uduak eteufọk amọ ado inamma mbeeñeidem, inyʌññọ inam se eteufọk amọ ayem enam, ayaabọ uwak ntiim.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="LUK 12:48" /><char style="wj">Ado ayịnufọk i-imiidiọọñọke uduak eteufọk amọ ado anam ñkpọ se idot ufen, ayaabọ etək-etək ufen. Amaado awo e-ekenọọhọ uwak, eyaebịp uwak ñkpọ eto anye; ñko awo e-eyaaha uwak ñkpọ esịn ke ubọk, eyaenyʌñ eyem uwak ñkpọ eto anye.</char><verse eid="LUK 12:48" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Aben Ubakka Adi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" sid="LUK 12:49" />
    <char style="wj">“Ami ñkedi adisịn ikañ ke ederimbod; ubaha nte adooho ikañ ado amaasaasak!</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:49" /><verse number="50" style="v" sid="LUK 12:50" /><char style="wj">Ami mmenie uduọkmmọọñ adina, ndin se naña mba ke mfʌhọ tutu uduọkmmọọñ ado akweeñe!</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:50" /><verse number="51" style="v" sid="LUK 12:51" /><char style="wj">Ekere ke ñkeben emem ndi isọñ? Iyoo, ñkeben ubakka ndi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:51" /><verse number="52" style="v" sid="LUK 12:52" /><char style="wj">Tọọñọ ke idahami, awo ition eyaeba ke ubon, ndin ubakka ayaaba ke ufọọd ammọ, ita eyaebakka eda ye iba ako, iba eyaenyʌñ ebakka eda ye ita ako.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:52" /><verse number="53" style="v" sid="LUK 12:53" /><char style="wj">Ete ayaatuaha ye ayịn amọ, ayịn ayaanyʌñ atuaha ye ete; eka ayaatuaha ye ayịn awonwaan amọ, ayịn awonwaan ayaanyʌñ atuaha ye eka; eka ebe ayaatuaha ye anwaan ayịn amọ, anwaan ayịn ayaanyʌñ atuaha ye eka ebe.”</char><verse eid="LUK 12:53" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adikappa mme Ini</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="54" style="v" sid="LUK 12:54" />Yisọs amaabo atu awo ate, <char style="wj">“Ndufo imaikịt naña ntọñanyọñ ato usobutịn adi, idaha-idaha ado ndufo ete, ‘Edịm ayaadep,’ edịm anyʌñ adep.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:54" /><verse number="55" style="v" sid="LUK 12:55" /><char style="wj">Ñko afịm a-atooho usuuk amaafịme, ndufo ete, ‘Ayio ayaada,’ anye anyʌñ ado ntoro.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:55" /><verse number="56" style="v" sid="LUK 12:56" /><char style="wj">Ndufo mme mbubịk! Ndufo emediọọñọ naña ekappa naña ayio adiiba akeene naña isọñ ye anyọñ aba. Anam die ndin nọ ndufo imiikanna ikappa idiọọñọ se utọ ini ntom ada anọ?</char><verse eid="LUK 12:56" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="57" style="v" sid="LUK 12:57" />
    <char style="wj">“Nsoo inam nọ ndufo imiikanna ibiide inọ idem ndufo se ido nnen-nnen? </char> <verse eid="LUK 12:57" /><verse number="58" style="v" sid="LUK 12:58" /><char style="wj">Ke ini awo usua mfo ubenne fiin abịne akpe ikpe esob, nwana nam emem ye anye ke usʌñ, imiidooho ntoro anye ayauben fiin abịne abiideikpe, ndin abiideikpe ayauyaak fiin anọ adaaha, ndin adaaha ayausịn fiin ke ufọk ñkpakọb.</char> <verse eid="LUK 12:58" /><verse number="59" style="v" sid="LUK 12:59" /><char style="wj">Ami udọkkọ fiin nte, afo uduuwuọhọ tutu afo akpe akpatre akʌk.”</char><verse eid="LUK 12:59" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 12" />
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="LUK 13" />
  <para style="s1">Ikappa Esịd Mbaak Iditak</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 13:1" />Ke ini ado, mme awo emaeba e-ekedidọkkọke Yisọs ebaña ubaak mbon Kalili a-Pailed akedatta iyiib ammọ awuak ke mme ñkpọ uwa. <verse eid="LUK 13:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 13:2" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ndufo ekere ebo ke mbon Kalili ekebọ ufen ami sia ammọ ekenamma idiọọk ñkpọ ekan afịd mbon Kalili mfen?</char> <verse eid="LUK 13:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 13:3" /><char style="wj">Ami ibo ndufo ke idooho ntoro. Ibọhọke ndufo etua ñkpọfiọk, ndufo ñko eyaetak ntoro.</char> <verse eid="LUK 13:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 13:4" /><char style="wj">Me ndufo ekere ke awo duob mme itiaita a-tọwa Silọm akefiighe awot emaedue ñkpọ ekan afịd awo e-ekedʌññọ ke Yeruselem?</char> <verse eid="LUK 13:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 13:5" /><char style="wj">Ami ibo ndufo ke idooho ntoro. Ado ibọhọke ndufo ekappa esịd, afịd ndufo ñko eyaetak.”</char><verse eid="LUK 13:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 13:6" />Akem anye amaatop ñke ami anọ ammọ, ate: <char style="wj">“Ete keed akenie eto fik ke inwañ amọ, akema anye amaakaa akese me anwịm mfịd, ado ikịtte mfịd ndomokeed.</char> <verse eid="LUK 13:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 13:7" /><char style="wj">Ndin anye amaabo akpemeinwañ fain ate, ‘Isua ita ado ami, mmesaña ndise me ñyaakịt mfịd ke eto fik ami, ado ñkịtte. Kpịkke anye duọọk. Ntak a-anye akpedaaha ke isọñ ñkaña-a?’</char><verse eid="LUK 13:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 13:8" />
    <char style="wj">“Akpemeinwañ amaabọọrọ ate, ‘Ete, yak anye amaana aba do ke ñkpọ nte isua keed mfen, ndin ami ñyaadọk mben amọ ñkanna ñnyʌñ ndọñ mme ñkpadia.</char> <verse eid="LUK 13:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 13:9" /><char style="wj">Anye akpeñwịm mfịd abem idaha ntom, saana yaak, ado imiinwịmme, kpịkke duọọk.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 13:9" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ekọk Mbʌñọ ke Usen Sabad</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 13:10" />Ke usen Sabad, Yisọs akekpeep ñkpọ ke sinakọk, <verse eid="LUK 13:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 13:11" />ndin awonwaan i-idiọọk sịbidịd akenamma anye adọñọ mbʌñọ ke ñkpọ nte isua duob mme itiaita amaaba do. Udọñọ ami amaanwịn anye tutu ikanna inekke ida. <verse eid="LUK 13:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 13:12" />Ke ini Yisọs akekịtte anye, amaakoot anye adat, ate yak anye awuọ adi iso, ndin amaabo anye ate, <char style="wj">“Awonwaan, u-ukpọk fiin eyaak ke udọñọ mfo.”</char> <verse eid="LUK 13:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 13:13" />Anye amaadot awonwaan ado ubọk, ndin ke ndo-ndo ado anye amaanekke ada, anyʌñ atooro Abasi.<verse eid="LUK 13:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 13:14" />Ado andikara sinakọk amaakop iyadesịd ke ntak a-Yisọs akekọkkọ udọñọ ke usen Sabad, ado anam anye amaabo, “Usen itiokeed ana inọ ndufo adinam utom. Mmọdo di nọ edukọk udọñọ ke mme usen ado, idooho ke usen Sabad.”<verse eid="LUK 13:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 13:15" />Ado Abọọñ amaabọọrọ anye ate, <char style="wj">“Ndufo mbon mbubịk! Nte ndufo keedekeed isitatta abaakenañ me dọñki ndufo isio ke abaenañ iben ikinọ mmọọñ ke usen Sabad?</char> <verse eid="LUK 13:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 13:16" /><char style="wj">Ndin ikpinaaha ekpọk awonwaan ami eyaak, ayịn Ebraham, a-Setan akesịnne ke ñkpakọb ke afịd isua duob mme itiaita ami ke usen Sabad?”</char><verse eid="LUK 13:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 13:17" />Ke ini anye aketañña ikọ ami, abuud amaanam afịd mme asua amọ, ado uwak awo emaenem esịd ke afịd nti utịppeñkpọ a-anye akenamma.<verse eid="LUK 13:17" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñke Ñkpasi Mọstad ye Yiis</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 13:18" />Ndin Yisọs amaabịp abo, <char style="wj">“Nsoo ke abioubọọñ Abasi abit? Ami ndiidat nsoo ndomo ye abioubọọñ Abasi?</char> <verse eid="LUK 13:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 13:19" /><char style="wj">Anye abit ñkpasi mọstad a-atọ inwañ akebenne atọ ke inwañ amọ. Ndin anye amaatịppe, akọt akappa eto, ndin mme inuen anyọñ ekesọrọ ke mme ñkọk amọ.”</char><verse eid="LUK 13:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 13:20" />Anye amaamaana abịp, <char style="wj">“Nsoo ke ami ndiidat ndomo ye abioubọọñ Abasi?</char> <verse eid="LUK 13:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 13:21" /><char style="wj">Anye abit yiis, a-awonwaan akedomoke asịn ke udomo ndomuyo ata</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13:21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Me ñkpọ nte kilokram 27</char></note> <char style="wj">a-akenamma nọ ndomuyo atịt.”</char><verse eid="LUK 13:21" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mfafaha Usʌñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 13:22" />Ndin Yisọs amaakpeep ñkpọ ke uwak ñkpoon ye ntək abio naña anye akeboiyoke aka Yeruselem. <verse eid="LUK 13:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 13:23" />Awo keed amaabịp anye ate, “Abọọñ me nte ibad-ibad awo kpọd ediibọkkọ?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 13:23">Yisọs amaabo ammọ ate, <verse eid="LUK 13:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 13:24" /><char style="wj">“Idomo afịd ukeme ndufo adisaña ke mfafaha usʌñ ndʌk, sia ami idọkkọ ndufo, uwak awo eyaedomo ukeme adidʌk ado idiikanna.</char> <verse eid="LUK 13:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 13:25" /><char style="wj">Anie ufọk amaadadakka ada akʌk usʌñ, afo ayaada ke esiin akọñ usʌñ anyʌñ akpeiye abo, ‘Abọọñ beere usʌñ inọ ñnyịn.’</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 13:25">
    <char style="wj">“Ado anye ayaibọọrọ ndufo ate, ‘Ami idiọọñọke ndufo, miidooho anye ayaabo ndufo eto uke edi?’</char><verse eid="LUK 13:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 13:26" />
    <char style="wj">“Ndin ndufo eyaebọọrọ, ‘Ñnyịn ikisidia ndidia inyʌñ inwọñ ñkpọ ye afo; afo amaanyʌñ akpeep ñkpọ ke efaak ñnyịn.’</char><verse eid="LUK 13:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 13:27" />
    <char style="wj">“Ado anye ayaibọọrọ ndufo, ‘Ami idiọọñọke ndufo me nte ndufo eto. Idakka iñkpọñ miin, afịd ndufo mme anam ndiọi!’</char><verse eid="LUK 13:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 13:28" />
    <char style="wj">“Ntuaña ayaaba, ntaeded ayaanyʌñ aba, ke ini ediikịt Ebraham ye Aisik ye Yekọb ye afịd mme prọfed ke abioubọọñ Abasi, ado isịññe ndufo ke idem ndufo etop eduọọñọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 13:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 13:29" /><char style="wj">Mme awo eyaeto ke usakkautịn ye ke usobutịn, adoro ye usuuk, eyaenyʌñ edidat itie ammọ ke usọrọ abioubọọñ Abasi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 13:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 13:30" /><char style="wj">Ke akpanikọ, mbon e-ekedooho akpatre eyaekappa edo akpa, ndin mbon e-ekedooho akpa, eyaekappa edo akpatre.”</char><verse eid="LUK 13:30" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Afʌhọ Abaña Yeruselem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 13:31" />Etək ini akeboiyo, ubaak mme Farisi emaedibo Yisọs, “Kpọñ itie ami kaa itie mfen sia Herọd ayem aduwot fiin.”<verse eid="LUK 13:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 13:32" />Anye amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Kaa kedọkkọ ewaikọd ado bo ke ‘ami ñyaakaa iso mbịn mme dimọn ñnyʌñ ñkọk udọñọ mfịn ye ñkpọñ, ndin ke ayọhọ usen ita, ami ñyaama se ñkeduak adinam.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 13:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 13:33" /><char style="wj">Ñkọm a-abaaha ntom, ami ñyaasịn ifịk nnam utom mfịn ye ñkpọñ ye ubakñkpọñ, ndin ñyaakaa iso ke isañ mmi, sia ke akpanikọ prọfed ndomokeed inaaha akpa ke itie mfen ke imiibọhọke Yeruselem!</char><verse eid="LUK 13:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 13:34" />
    <char style="wj">“O Yeruselem, O Yeruselem ndufo e-ewotto mme prọfed enyʌñ etọọñ mbon e-enọọhọ isọk ndufo ke itiad, akañ ifañ ke ami ñyem adikoot nditọ ndufo mbok itie keed nte eka unen abok nditọ ke idak mba amọ, ado ndufo inyịmmeke.</char> <verse eid="LUK 13:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 13:35" /><char style="wj">Sese, eyaak ñwuudo ufọk ndufo inọ ndufo. Ami ntañ ami inọ ndufo, ndufo idiñkịtte miin aba tutu ndufo ebo, ‘Afọfọn anọ anye a-adiighe ke anyịñ Abọọñ.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 13:35" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 13" />
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="LUK 14" />
  <para style="s1">Yisọs ke Ufọk Farisi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 14:1" />Ke usen Sabad keed, naña Yisọs akekaaha asen ke ufọk adaaha mme Farisi, uwak awo emaeba do e-ekesakka anyen ese se anye anam. <verse eid="LUK 14:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 14:2" />Awo ñyọọk keed amaaba ke iso amọ ke itie ado. <verse eid="LUK 14:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 14:3" />Yisọs amaabịp mme Farisi ye mme ntaifiọk mbed e-ekebaaha do ate, <char style="wj">“Anen adikọk awo udọñọ ke usen Sabad me inenne?”</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 14:4" />Afịd ammọ emaedobo, isioho uyio. Ndin Yisọs amaamʌm awo ado akọk udọñọ, anyʌñ anọ anye anyọñ.<verse eid="LUK 14:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 14:5" />Ndin Yisọs amaabịp ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Adieke awo keed ke atu ndufo a-anieghe ayịn, me abaakenañ, a-aduọhọ adʌk ube mmọọñ ke usen Sabad, nte anye ikpisọppọsọp idem isio anye ke ube ado?”</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 14:6" />Ammọ ikinyʌññọ inie ibọọrọ se enọ.<verse eid="LUK 14:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 14:7" />Mi ke anye aketop ñke anọ mbon se ekekoot ndidia, ke anye amaakekịt naña ammọ emek mme itie ukpono ke akpokoro ndidia. Yisọs amaabo ammọ ate, <verse eid="LUK 14:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 14:8" /><char style="wj">“Awo akpukoot fiin usọrọ ndọ, kuudọọk ukutie ke ekamba itie; sia awo akponno itie ukan fiin akpedi,</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 14:9" /><char style="wj">andinie usọrọ ayaadukoot fiin ate, ‘Kpọñ itie nọ awo ami.’ Ndin afo ayaakpọñ itie ado ke abuud.</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 14:10" /><char style="wj">Ado emaukoot fiin usọrọ, kaa ke tie ke akpatre ñkpọitie ke edem tutu anie usọrọ adukoot fiin abo, ‘Ufan dọọk di ekamba itie.’ Idahado, afo ayaanie ukpono ke iso mme awo se iba do.</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 14:11" /><char style="wj">Sia awo akeedodo a-akokkoke idem, eyaesuuhọ anye itie; ado awo a-asuuhọke idem eyaebenne anye.”</char><verse eid="LUK 14:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 14:12" />Anye ndin amaakanna iso ase andikikoot anye ndidia, ate, <char style="wj">“Ke ini afo akoodo awo ndidia uweemeayio, me ake ndubiayio, kuukoot mme ufan mfo, nditọeka mfo, me uyakka, me mme mbọhọidʌñ mfo e-emọinyọke. Ukpunam ntom, ammọ eyaenyʌñ ukoot fiin usiene.</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 14:13" /><char style="wj">Ado afo umaunam usọrọ, koot mbon uweene, mme inyọọn ye mbʌñọ ye nnan.</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 14:14" /><char style="wj">Ke adinam ntom, afo ayaabọ adidiọñ. Ñkọm a-adooho ammọ ikanna unọ fiin usiene, afo ayaabọ usiene ke adised ke ñkpa ndinen awo.”</char><verse eid="LUK 14:14" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñke Ekamba Usọrọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 14:15" />Awo keed ke itie ndidia akekop mme ikọ ami, anye amaabo Yisọs ate, “Afọfọn anọ awo a-adiidia ndidia ke itie usọrọ ke abioubọọñ Abasi.”<verse eid="LUK 14:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 14:16" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ anye ate, <char style="wj">“Abọọñ keed akenam ekamba usọrọ, akoot uwak-uwak awo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 14:17" /><char style="wj">Ini usọrọ akekem, anye amaasio ayịnufọk ate asaña adọkkọ mbon se anye akekoot abo, ‘Idi, ke e-enam afịd ndutʌm ema.’</char><verse eid="LUK 14:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 14:18" />
    <char style="wj">“Ado afịd ammọ keedekeed emaetọọñọ adinọ ebeeñe. Akpa awo amaabo, ‘Ami adisʌk ndep ufa inwañ adodo, ndin ana ami ñka ñkese naña aba. Mbọk kuuyat esịd ke ñkanna ndi.’</char><verse eid="LUK 14:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 14:19" />
    <char style="wj">“Ayọhọ awo iba ate, ‘Ami adisʌk ndep mme abaakenañ utọ inwañ ition adodo, ndin ñyem adikidomo ammọ nse naña eba. Mbọk kuuyat esịd ke mmebeeñe; ñkanna ndi.’</char><verse eid="LUK 14:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 14:20" />
    <char style="wj">“Awo mfen amaabo, ‘Ami ndọ ufa anwaan mmi-mmi, ke ntoro ndiikanna ndi.’</char><verse eid="LUK 14:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 14:21" />
    <char style="wj">“Ayịnufọk amaanyọñ aditañ afịd ami anọ eteufọk amọ. Esịd amaayat eteufọk, anam anye amaanọ ayịnufọk uyio abo ‘Sọsọp dʌk ke mme efaak ye mme inuuk abio, ke koot mme uweene, mbʌñọ ye mme inyọọn, ye nnan di.’</char><verse eid="LUK 14:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 14:22" />
    <char style="wj">“Ayịnufọk amaadibo eteufọk, ‘Emaenam se afo akebo enam, ado itie asʌk asọsʌhọ.’</char><verse eid="LUK 14:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 14:23" />
    <char style="wj">“Akem eteufọk amaatịmme adọñ ayịnufọk amọ ate, ‘Wuọ ka mme akpọusʌñ ye mme ñwaaña usʌñ idʌñ, nyʌñ ke nyịk ammọ, koot nọ edʌk edi, nọ ufọk mmi adiiyọhọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 14:24" /><char style="wj">Ami ntañ inọ ndufo, ndomo awo keed se ñketo ñkoot ke akpa ini a-adiidia ndidia mmi ibaaha.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 14:24" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ekọmudua Adido Mbed Krais</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 14:25" />Ataa uwak awo emaesaña ye Yisọs, ndin anye amaawọññọ iso abo ammọ ate: <verse eid="LUK 14:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 14:26" /><char style="wj">“Awo akeedodo añkeeneke miin, ndin isuaha ete ye eka, anwaan ye nditọ, nditọeka ideen ye ibaan; ii, kpa ye idem uwem amọ, ikanna ido mbed mmi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 14:27" /><char style="wj">Ndin awo akeedodo i-imiibenne krọs amọ iñkeene miin, ikemeke adido mbed mmi.</char><verse eid="LUK 14:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 14:28" />
    <char style="wj">“Adieke awo keed ke atu ndufo akpeyemme adibọp tọwa, nte afo ukpubemmeiso usuuk utie ubat se ufọk ado adiikpa, ase me afo amenie akʌk se ikem se uduukama ubọp anye uma?</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 14:29" /><char style="wj">Sia adieke afo asịnne itiad idakisọñ amaa, ndin ukanna ubọp anye uma, afịd awo e-ekịtte anye eyaunọ ñnyọ,</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 14:30" /><char style="wj">ete, ‘Awo ami amaatọọñọ ibọp ufọk, ndin ikanna ikweeñe.’</char><verse eid="LUK 14:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 14:31" />
    <char style="wj">“Ñko, anie adidem ikpiyem ika ekọñ ye adidem mfen, itieghe ke akpa ifed iduuñọ me iyaikan iben mbon ekọñ tọsịn duob ikinwana ye anye a-anieghe mbon ekọñ tọsịn edịb?</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 14:32" /><char style="wj">Anye akpekịt ke idiikanna, ana asio isʌñutom adọñ naña udịmekọñ mbon ñko imiikpereke, akekpeiye abo yak mmimọ inam emem.</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 14:33" /><char style="wj">Ukem-ukem ado, awo ndufo akeedodo idiikanna ido mbed mmi anye imiisaanake afịd se anye anie iyaak.</char><verse eid="LUK 14:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 14:34" />
    <char style="wj">“Inʌñ afọn, ado inʌñ imiinieghe inem aba, nsoo ke ediinam nọ anye amaana anem?</char> <verse eid="LUK 14:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 14:35" /><char style="wj">Utọ inʌñ ado ibaaha ufọn inọ isọñ, inyʌññọ iba ufọn inọ itoon mbio; ukweeñe ado aditop anye nduọọk.</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 14:35">
    <char style="wj">“Awo akeedodo a-anieghe utọñ, yak anye akop.”</char><verse eid="LUK 14:35" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 14" />
  <chapter number="15" style="c" sid="LUK 15" />
  <para style="s1">Ñke Edọñ Keed a-Akesoppo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 15:1" />Mme abọọ taks ye mbon a-mme awo ebatta nte mme anam ndiọiñkpọ emaediboho nọ ato do ekop se Yisọs anie aditañ. <verse eid="LUK 15:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 15:2" />Ado mme Farisi ye mme andikpeeb mbed emaedukuunọ ete: “Awo ami adʌk ndʌk ye mme anam ndiọi anyʌñ adia ndidia ye ammọ.”<verse eid="LUK 15:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 15:3" />Ndin Yisọs amaatop ñke ami anọ ammọ: <verse eid="LUK 15:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 15:4" /><char style="wj">“Keed ke atu ndufo akpenie edọñ ikie, ndin edọñ keed abọkkọ asop, nte anye ikpisaanake edọñ anaañ mme duob mme usʌkkeed ako ke akpautatan inịm ikiyem keed akesoppo do tutu anye akịt?</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 15:5" /><char style="wj">Ndin anye amaakịt edọñ keed ado, anye ayaabenne adot ke itọñ anyọñ ufọk.</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 15:6" /><char style="wj">Amaakewuọ ufọk, anye akoot mme ufan amọ ate, ‘Idaara ye ami; mmekịt edọñ mmi a-akesoppo.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 15:7" /><char style="wj">Ami idọkkọ ndufo nte kpa ke ukem usʌñ ado, idaara ayaakpon ke hefịn eti-eti ke ntak idiọọk awo keed a-akappake esịd akan ndinen awo anaañ mme duob mme usʌkkeed imiinieghe ntak adikappa esịd.</char><verse eid="LUK 15:7" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñke Akpoho Keed a-Akesoppo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 15:8" />
    <char style="wj">“Akpedo anam awonwaan anie kọbọ</char>
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">15:8 </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek ado </char>
      <char style="fqa" closed="false">drakma </char>
      <char style="fq" closed="false">duob, </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">a-adooho akʌk utom usen debra</char>
    </note> <char style="wj">duob, ndin keed abọkkọ anye asop, me anye idiidomoke utuenikañ, ikwọọk ufọk, iyem kọbọ keed ado tutu anye akịt?</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 15:9" /><char style="wj">Ndin anye amaakịt kọbọ ado, anye akoot mme ufan ye mbọhọidʌñ amọ ate, ‘Ididaara ye ami ke mmekịt akʌk mmi a-akesoppo.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 15:10" /><char style="wj">Ke ukem usʌñ ado ami ibo ndufo, ke idaara a-aba ke atu mme enyere Abasi ke ntak idiọọk awo keed a-akappake esịd.”</char><verse eid="LUK 15:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñke Ete Anie Mbọm</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 15:11" />Yisọs amaamaana adian do, <char style="wj">“Ete keed amaaba a-akenieghe nditọ ideen iba, akpan ye udọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 15:12" /><char style="wj">Udọ amaabo, ‘Ete, nnọ miin udeeme inie mmi.’ Ndin ete amaabakka inie amọ ke itie iba anọ ammọ awo iba.</char><verse eid="LUK 15:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 15:13" />
    <char style="wj">“Ikikpeenekekpeene, Udọ amaakoono afịd se anye akenie adakka isañ akaa anyan idịd. Akekewuọ do, anye amaaketahade inie amọ ke adidu abʌd-abʌd uwem.</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 15:14" /><char style="wj">Ke anye amaaketahade inie amọ ama, ekamba akañ amaadisịm afịd abio ado, ndin anye amaatọọñọ adiba ke akpọsọñ unana.</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 15:15" /><char style="wj">Ke ntoro, anye amaakeyaak idem amọ anọ awo abio ado adinam utom usen; ndin awo ado amaanọ anye utom adinọ mme edi ndidia ke mme inwañ edi amọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 15:16" /><char style="wj">Amaadọñ anye adidia ñkpọk ndidia se mme edi ekesidia ñkama mmʌm idịb, ado awo ikinọọhọ anye ñkpọ ndomokeed.</char><verse eid="LUK 15:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 15:17" />
    <char style="wj">“Ke iwuod amaaketekke anye inaa, Udọ amaabo idem amọ ate, ‘Mme nditọutom ifañ ke ufọk ete mmi inie se edia inyʌñ inie se esọsʌhọ, ado se miin mi naña akañ abo idiñwot!</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 15:18" /><char style="wj">Ami ñyaadakka mbịne ete mmi, ñnyʌñ ñkebo anye nte: Ete mmi, mmedue hefịn, ñnyʌñ udue fiin.</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 15:19" /><char style="wj">Ami ndotto aba se añkoot ayịn mfo; ndat miin nte keed ke atu nditọutom mfo.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 15:20" /><char style="wj">Ndin anye amaadakka abịne ete amọ.</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 15:20">
    <char style="wj">“Ke ini ete amọ akedaaha akịt anye ko ke anyan usʌñ, mbọm amọ amaanam anye; ndin anye amaanyʌñ afeghe abịne Udọ, akefat anye anyʌñ atʌm anye inua.</char><verse eid="LUK 15:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 15:21" />
    <char style="wj">“Udọ amaabo ete amọ, ‘Ete mmi, ami mmedue hefịn mmenyʌñ udue fiin. Ami ndotto aba se añkoot ayịn mfo.’</char><verse eid="LUK 15:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 15:22" />
    <char style="wj">“Ado ete amọ amaanọ nditọufọk uyio ate, ‘Usọp! Idat afọñ se iyaiya ikan idisịn Udọ. Isịn anye ñkpainuun ke ubọk, ye ikpaukod ke ukod.</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 15:23" /><char style="wj">Iwot afọn idem abaakenañ e-ekebọọhọ enịm. Yak inam usọrọ inyʌñ idaara.</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 15:24" /><char style="wj">Sia ayịn mmi ami amaakpa ndin amaana adu uwem; anye amaasop ndin imimaana ikịt anye.’ Ndin usọrọ amaatọọñọ.</char><verse eid="LUK 15:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 15:25" />
    <char style="wj">“Ke afịd ini ami, Akpan mmọdo ke inwañ akeba asʌk anam utom. Ke anye amaakenyọñ adikpere ufọk, anye amaakop uyio ikwọ ye unek.</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 15:26" /><char style="wj">Anye amaakoot ayịnufọk keed abịp me nsoo ido.</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 15:27" /><char style="wj">Ayịnufọk ado amaabọọrọ anye ate, ‘Udọ eka mfo anyọñ adi, ndin ete mfo a-awot ataa afọn idem abaakenañ sia anye a-adiwuọ ufọk ke ifuuro ye nsọñidem.’</char><verse eid="LUK 15:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 15:28" />
    <char style="wj">“Akpan amaakop iyadesịd anyʌñ asịn adidʌk ufọk ñkewuana ye ammọ. Ndin ete amọ amaawuọ esiin akekpeiye anye.</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 15:29" /><char style="wj">Ado anye amaabọọrọ ete amọ ate, ‘Sese! Afịd mme isua eboiyoke mi, ami mmewa idem nnam utom unọ fiin, ñkop item, nsọññọ iwuod ñnyʌññọ umiom fiin. Ado kpaanam afo unnọọhọ miin etək ñyịn ebod ubo ñwot nnam usọrọ ye mme ufan mmi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 15:30" /><char style="wj">Ado Udọ mfo ami a-akekesuanna inie mfo ye mme akpara akenyọñ adi, afo adimʌm afọn idem abaakenañ awot anọ anye!’</char><verse eid="LUK 15:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 15:31" />
    <char style="wj">“Ete amọ amaabọọrọ anye ate, ‘Akpan mmi, afo aba mi ye ami afịd-afịd ini, afịd ñkpọ se ami nnie, ado afo anie.</char> <verse eid="LUK 15:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 15:32" /><char style="wj">Akena ñnyịn idaara inyʌñ ikop inemesịd, sia ayịneka mfo ami amaakpa ndin a-amaana adu uwem; anye amaasop, ndin imimaana ikịt anye.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 15:32" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 15" />
  <chapter number="16" style="c" sid="LUK 16" />
  <para style="s1">Ñke a-Abañake Mbufiọk Akamautom</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 16:1" />Ndin Yisọs amaabo mme mbed amọ ate: <char style="wj">“Imọ awo keed amaaba e-ekedidọkkọke anye ebo ke akamautom amọ atahade inie amọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 16:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 16:2" /><char style="wj">Ndin anye amaakoot akamautom amọ abo anye ate, ‘Nsoo ke ñkop ami ubaña fiin? Nam ibad nnọ miin naña akekama utom sia ubooho udo akamautom mmi aba.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 16:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 16:3" />
    <char style="wj">Akamautom amaabo idem amọ ate, “Nsoo ke mbo nnam idahado? Eteufọk mmi ayambịn ke utom. Ami nnieghe inweek ñkem se ñkekịm isọñ; ndin ami mmenyʌñ ñkop abuud adibeeñe ebeeñe.</char> <verse eid="LUK 16:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 16:4" /><char style="wj">Afọn, mmediọọñọ se mbo nnam nọ ato do emaembịn ke utom mme awo eyak ñwakka ufọk ammọ.”</char><verse eid="LUK 16:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 16:5" />
    <char style="wj">Ndin anye amaakoot afịd awo se ikikama eteufọk amọ isʌñ anyʌñ abịp akpa awo ate, “Akʌk ifañ ke afo akama eteufọk mmi?”</char><verse eid="LUK 16:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 16:6" />
    <char style="wj">Anye amaabọọrọ, “Ñkama tian adan ọlif ikie usʌkkeed.”</char>
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">16:6 </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte lita 3,000</char>
    </note></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 16:6">
    <char style="wj">“Akamautom amaabo anye, ‘Sọp idem, dat ñwed isʌñ mfo, kpịkke wet tian adan ikie inaañ mme aba mme duob.’</char><verse eid="LUK 16:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 16:7" />
    <char style="wj">“Ndin akamautom amaabịp ayọhọ awo iba, ‘Nsoo ke akama?’</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 16:7">
    <char style="wj">“Anye amaabọọrọ, ‘Ñkama</char>
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">16:7 </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte tọọn 30</char>
    </note> <char style="wj">akpasa abakpa tọsịn keed.’</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 16:7">
    <char style="wj">“Akamautom amaabo anye, ‘Sọp idem, dat ñwed isʌñ mfo, kpịkke wet akpasa abakpa ikie itiaita.’</char><verse eid="LUK 16:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 16:8" />
    <char style="wj">“Eteufọk amọ amaatooro adinam idiọọk akamautom ami sia anye amaanie mbufiọk. Sia mbon ederimbod ami imiidiọọñọke Abasi enie mbufiọk ke emaebiinam ñkpọ ye emọ-emọ awo ekan mbon e-ediọọñọke Abasi e-enyʌññọ esaña ke unwana.</char> <verse eid="LUK 16:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 16:9" /><char style="wj">Ami ibo ndufo, ikama inie ederimbod ami ikọ mme ufan inọ idem ndufo, mbaak inie ado amaakweeñe ibọ ndufo esịn ke nsi-nsi itieidʌñ.</char><verse eid="LUK 16:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 16:10" />
    <char style="wj">“Sia awo akeedodo a-akanna anam akpanikọ ke etək ñkpọ, a-akan anam akpanikọ ke ekamba ñkpọ. Awo akeedodo i-imiinamma akpanikọ ke etək ñkpọ ikanna inam akpanikọ ke ekamba ñkpọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 16:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 16:11" /><char style="wj">Ndin adieke afo umuukunamma akpanikọ ke naña akama inie ederimbod, anie adiinịm ke amekeme adinam akpanikọ ekpunọ ataa inie?</char> <verse eid="LUK 16:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 16:12" /><char style="wj">Ndin adieke umuunamma akpanikọ ye inie awo mfen, anie aduunọ fiin inie ake mfo?</char><verse eid="LUK 16:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 16:13" />
    <char style="wj">“Awo ndomokeed ikemeke adido ayịnufọk nnọọ eteufọk iba: Anye ayaama keed asua keed; imiidooho ntoro anye ayaanekke adiana keed ke idem akan keed. Ndufo ikemeke adima Abasi ye akʌk ukem-ukem.”</char><verse eid="LUK 16:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 16:14" />Mme Farisi e-ekemaaha akʌk, emaekop afịd ami enyʌñ etuun Yisọs inua. <verse eid="LUK 16:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 16:15" />Ami anam Yisọs amaabo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Ndufo edo mbon e-eyemme adido nti awo ke iso awo, ado Abasi adiọọñọ esịd ndufo. Se mme awo edat nte akpan ñkpọ ado ndek ke anyen Abasi.</char><verse eid="LUK 16:15" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Ukpeebñkpọ Mfen</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 16:16" />
    <char style="wj">“Emaekwọrọ enyʌñ ekpeep mme Mbed ye mme Prọfed tutu adiwuọ ini Yọọn. Tọọñọ ke idahado, esʌk ekwọrọ eti etob abioubọọñ Abasi, ndin afịd awo eyem usʌñ adinwana ndʌk ke esịd.</char> <verse eid="LUK 16:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 16:17" /><char style="wj">Ado ataa mmem-mmem ñkpọ hefịn ye isọñ adiboiyo mfep ñkan ntọi ikọ keed adiwuọ ke ñwed Mbed.</char><verse eid="LUK 16:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 16:18" />
    <char style="wj">“Awo akeedodo a-asịnne anwaan amọ akedọ awonwaan mfen a-asịn efịbe, ndin awodeen a-adọọhọ awonwaan e-ebe amaakesịn, a-asịn efịbe.</char><verse eid="LUK 16:18" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Imọ Awo ye Lasọrọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 16:19" />
    <char style="wj">“Imọ awo keed amaaba a-akesisịneke nsọñudua afọñ anyʌñ akop inem uwem afịd usen.</char> <verse eid="LUK 16:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 16:20" /><char style="wj">Ke inuaatob amọ, abeeñe ebeeñe keed a-akekereke Lasọrọs amaatie, ndin inia amaafʌk anye afịd idem,</char> <verse eid="LUK 16:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 16:21" /><char style="wj">anye amaanie udọñ adiikpidia mbeñe ndidia se ikiduọññọ ito akpokoro awo inie ado. Mme ewa ñko emaesididai mme inia ke idem amọ.</char><verse eid="LUK 16:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 16:22" />
    <char style="wj">“Akekem koo, abeeñe ebeeñe ami amaakpa, ndin mme enyere emaeben anye ekenịm ke ikpanesịd Ebraham. Imọ awo amaanyʌñ adikpa, ndin emaebuuk anye.</char> <verse eid="LUK 16:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 16:23" /><char style="wj">Ke abioekpo, ke itie a-anye akebaaha ke ufen, anye amaadịppe anyen akịt Ebraham ke anyan usʌñ ye Lasọrọs do ke ñkañ amọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 16:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 16:24" /><char style="wj">Anye amaabọọñ ate, ‘Ete Ebraham, ntua miin mbọm nyʌñ dọñ Lasọrọs adeep mmọọñ ke nnuun ubọk amọ adindeññe miin edeme, sia ami mba ke akpọsọñ ufen ke ikañ ami.’</char><verse eid="LUK 16:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 16:25" />
    <char style="wj">“Ado Ebraham amaabọọrọ anye ate, ‘Yịn mmi, toiyo ke ayio uwem afo amaanie nti ñkpọ ke ini Lasọrọs akekịtte ukuud, ado idahami anye a-abọ idọñesịd, ado afo aba ke ndutʌhọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 16:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 16:26" /><char style="wj">Ke adidian do, ekamba ukpe i-ibakka ñnyịn ye afo, a-anamma mbon se iyem ito umi ñkaa udo ikanna, mbon se inyʌñ iyem ito udo ndi umi ikanna.’</char><verse eid="LUK 16:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 16:27" />
    <char style="wj">“Imọ awo amaabọọrọ ate, ‘Mmukpeiye fiin ete, dọñ Lasọrọs aka ubon mmi,</char> <verse eid="LUK 16:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 16:28" /><char style="wj">sia ami mmenie nditọeka ideen ition. Yak anye akedʌt ammọ utọñ, mbaak ammọ edinyʌñ edi utọ itie ndutʌhọ ami.’</char><verse eid="LUK 16:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 16:29" />
    <char style="wj">“Ebraham amaabọọrọ, ‘Ammọ e-enie Moses ye mme Prọfed; yak ammọ ekpañ utọñ enọ mbon ndo.’</char><verse eid="LUK 16:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 16:30" />
    <char style="wj">“ ‘Awo inie amaabo, Iyoo, Ete Ebraham, ado awo akpeto abioekpo akedọkkọ ammọ, eyaekappa esịd.’</char><verse eid="LUK 16:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 16:31" />
    <char style="wj">“Ebraham amaabọọrọ, ‘Adieke ammọ miikpañña utọñ inọ Moses ye mme Prọfed, ammọ idiinịmme, akpọkọm awo abʌkkọ ke udi adika.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 16:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 16" />
  <chapter number="17" style="c" sid="LUK 17" />
  <para style="s1">Idiọọkñkpọ, Mbuọdidem ye Ubiọñutom</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 17:1" />Yisọs amaabo mme mbed amọ ate: <char style="wj">“Ñkpọiduọ ayaadi, ado adọdiọọk anọ andidiido ntak iduọ ado.</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 17:2" /><char style="wj">Akpaafọn inọ ammọ adieke ekpekọọñọ ammọ itiad ke itọñ etop ammọ esịn ke akpainyañ akan ammọ edido ñkpọiduọ a-anamma keed ke atu ntəkayịn ami anam idiọọkñkpọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 17:3" /><char style="wj">Ke ntoro, ikpeme idem ndufo.</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 17:3">
    <char style="wj">“Ayịneka</char>
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">17:3 </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek </char>
      <char style="fqa" closed="false">adelfọs</char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">adaaha anọ </char>
      <char style="fq" closed="false">ayịneka</char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">a-adooho </char>
      <char style="fqa" closed="false">awodeen me awonwaan</char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">, anyʌñ asʌk ada anọ emọ-emọ mbed, me ado awodeen me ado awonwaan.</char>
    </note> <char style="wj">mfo ke Krais akpenam idiọọkñkpọ, sua nọ anye. Anye akpetua ñkpọfiọk, feen nọ anye.</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 17:4" /><char style="wj">Akpekọm anye udue fiin akañ itiaba ke usen ndin atịmme adi adukpe ubọk akañ itiaba, abo: ‘mmetua ñkpọfiọk,’ ana afo afeen anọ anye.”</char><verse eid="LUK 17:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 17:5" />Mme mbed emaebo anye ete, “Abọọñ nam mbuọdidem ñnyịn akpon.”<verse eid="LUK 17:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 17:6" />Anye amaabọọrọ ammọ, <char style="wj">“Akpekọm ndufo enie mbuọdidem a-asịppe nte ñkpasi mọstad, emekeme edibo ekamba eto a-akponno nte ukịm, ‘Wʌkkọ kaa kewʌhọ ke akpainyañ,’ ndin anye ayaakop uyio ndufo.</char><verse eid="LUK 17:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 17:7" />
    <char style="wj">“Awo ndufo keed akpenie ayịnufọk a-akaaha ufʌñ inwañ me ukpeme edọñ, nte anye akpaabo ayịnufọk ado, ke amaato inwañ adi, ‘Di suuk tie ke akpokoro dia ñkpọ’?</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 17:8" /><char style="wj">Nte anye ikpikappa ibo, ‘Nam ndidia ndubi nnọ ndia, nyʌñ da mbet idaha a-ndiaha ñkpọ, ndin mmaadia ñnyʌñ ñnwọñ mma, afo amekeme adidia ñnyʌñ ñnwọñ’?</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 17:9" /><char style="wj">Me anye ayaakọọm ayịnufọk ado ke adinam se akenaa nte anam?</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 17:10" /><char style="wj">Ntom ke ami ibo ndufo, imainam afịd se ekebo ndufo enam, akpena ebo, ‘Ñnyịn ido nditọutom i-imiidotto, ñnyịn inam ubiọñutom ñnyịn kpọd.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 17:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Akọk mme Akpamfia Duob</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 17:11" />Idaha a-Yisọs akekaaha Yeruselem, anye amaaboiyo ke adaña Sameria ye Kalili. <verse eid="LUK 17:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 17:12" />Nte anye akedʌkkọ idʌñ keed, ideen duob e-ekedọñọke akpamfia<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17:12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">akpamfia</char><char style="ft" closed="false">ada anọ mme nsio-nsio udọñọ ñkpọnta ake ataaha awo ke ikpaidem</char></note> emaedisoobo anye. Ammọ emaeda nsan-nsan, <verse eid="LUK 17:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 17:13" />enyʌñ ebọọñ ke akpọsọñ uyio ete, “Yisọs, Eteufọk, itua ñnyịn mbọm.”<verse eid="LUK 17:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 17:14" />Ke ini Yisọs akekịtte ammọ, anye amaabo ate, <char style="wj">“Ikaa ikiwọt mme aku idem ndufo.”</char> Nte ammọ ekesañake ke usʌñ, emaenam ammọ esana, ndin idem amaasọñ ammọ.<verse eid="LUK 17:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 17:15" />Keed ke atu ammọ, ke amaakekịt ke udọñọ ikweeñe, amaatịmme aditooro Abasi ke akpọsọñ uyio. <verse eid="LUK 17:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 17:16" />Anye amaaduọ ke ukod Yisọs anyʌñ akọọm anye. Awo ado akedo awo Sameria.<verse eid="LUK 17:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 17:17" />Yisọs amaabịp ate, <char style="wj">“Nte idooho awo duob ke ekenam esana? Usʌkkeed ako-o?</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 17:18" /><char style="wj">Ibaaha awo ndomokeed a-atịmmeke adinọ Abasi ekọọm ke imiibọhọke asenawo ami?”</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 17:19" />Yisọs amaabo anye, <char style="wj">“Dakka nyọñ; mbuọdidem mfo anam idem usọñ.”</char><verse eid="LUK 17:19" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adidi Abioubọọñ Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 17:20" />Usen keed, mme Farisi emaekebịp anye me abioubọọñ Abasi adiidi ini akee. Yisọs amaabọọrọ ate, <char style="wj">“Adidi abioubọọñ Abasi idooho ñkpọ a-ndufo ekemeke adikịt,</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 17:21" /><char style="wj">mme awo idiinyʌññọ ibo, ‘Se anye mi’ me ‘Se anye ko,’ sia abioubọọñ Abasi mmọdo aba ke atu ndufo.”</char><verse eid="LUK 17:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 17:22" />Ndin anye amaabo mme mbed amọ, <char style="wj">“Ini asʌk adi a-ndufo ediiyem adikịt keed ke atu mme usen Ayịn Awo ado idiikịtte.</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 17:23" /><char style="wj">Mme awo eyaidọkkọ ndufo, ‘Se anye ko,’ me ‘Se anye mi.’ Ikiifeghe ikeene ammọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 17:24" /><char style="wj">Sia Ayịn Awo ke usen amọ adiitie nte akebkeb, a-akeppeke anọ unwana tọọñọ ke mbeñ ikpaanyọñ keed tutu awuọ mbeñ uko.</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 17:25" /><char style="wj">Ado akpa, ana anye akịt uwak ukuud, ñko emana ami eyaesịn anye.</char><verse eid="LUK 17:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 17:26" />
    <char style="wj">“Ukem naña aketịppe ke ayio Nua, adiinyʌñ ido ntoro ke mme usen Ayịn Awo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 17:27" /><char style="wj">Mme awo ekesʌk edia, enwọñ, edọ enyʌñ enọ ke ndọ tutu usen Nua akedʌkkọ ubom. Ndin mmọọñ ukwọ amaadisobo afịd ammọ.</char><verse eid="LUK 17:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 17:28" />
    <char style="wj">“Ukem ado ke akedo ke ayio Lọọd. Mme awo ekesʌk edia, enwọñ, edep, enyam, etọ, edọk, enyʌñ ebọp ufọk.</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 17:29" /><char style="wj">Ado usen Lọọd akewuọhọ akpọñ Sọdọm, ikañ ye sọlfọ emaeto hefịn edep esobo afịd ammọ.</char><verse eid="LUK 17:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 17:30" />
    <char style="wj">“Kpa ukem ado ke adiitịppe ke usen e-ediiyaara Ayịn Awo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 17:31" /><char style="wj">Ke usen ado, awo a-adoroke ke anyọñ akọm, ke ini inie amọ abaaha ke esịd ufọk, inaaha asọiyọ aka ikoono inie amọ. Ukem ado, awo a-abaaha ke inwañ anam utom, inaaha atịmme aka ufọk akedat ñkpọ ndomokeed.</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 17:32" /><char style="wj">Itoiyo anwaan Lọọd!</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 17:33" /><char style="wj">Awo akeedodo a-ayemme adinyaaña uwem amọ ayaaduọọk uwem amọ. Ñko awo akeedodo a-aduọọkkọ uwem amọ ayaanyaaña uwem amọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 17:34" /><char style="wj">Ami idọkkọ ndufo, ke akonayio ado, awo iba eyaenaa ke ñkpana keed, eyaedat keed ekpọñ anye ako.</char> <verse eid="LUK 17:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 17:35" /><char style="wj">Ibaan iba eyaeba ke itie ukọkñkpọ, eyaeben keed ekpọñ keed.</char> [<verse eid="LUK 17:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 17:36" /><char style="wj">Ideen iba eyaeba ke inwañ, eyaeben keed ekpọñ keed.”</char>]<verse eid="LUK 17:36" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 17:37" />Mme mbed emaebịp anye ete, “Abọọñ, ke mmọọ?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 17:37">Anye amaabọọrọ, <char style="wj">“Itie nte akpo ana, mme utere eyaekeboho ke ndo.”</char><verse eid="LUK 17:37" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 17" />
  <chapter number="18" style="c" sid="LUK 18" />
  <para style="s1">Ñke Ebekpa ye Abiideikpe</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 18:1" />Ndin Yisọs amaatop ñke ami anọ mbed amọ adiwọt ammọ ufọn awo adibọñ akam afịd ini, iduọhọ idodanyen tutu anye abọ se ayem. <verse eid="LUK 18:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 18:2" />Anye amaabo ammọ: <char style="wj">“Abiideikpe amaaba ke abio keed, i-imiikibaaha Abasi inyʌññọ iteeñe awo ndomokeed anyen.</char> <verse eid="LUK 18:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 18:3" /><char style="wj">Ke abio ado, ebekpa keed amaaba ñko a-akesidiighe abịne anye ye ebeeñe keed ate, ‘Kpe unen ikpe nnọ miin ye asua mmi.’</char><verse eid="LUK 18:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 18:4" />
    <char style="wj">“Abọọñ ado ikikamma isọp ñkpe ikpe nnọọ mma ado. Ke amaakekpeene koo anye amaatọọñọ ibo ke esịd amọ ate, ‘Akpesʌkado a-ami mmiiteeñeke Abasi anyen, inyʌññọ imbeghe se mme awo ekere,</char> <verse eid="LUK 18:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 18:5" /><char style="wj">ado sia ebekpa ami amfịnake miin abọhọ, ñyaakịt mbo ke anye anie unen amọ, mbaak anye adikappa ammʌm miin anwan.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 18:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 18:6" />Ndin Abọọñ amaabo, <char style="wj">“Kop se akpe ukwañ ikpe ami atañ do.</char> <verse eid="LUK 18:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 18:7" /><char style="wj">Nte Abasi idiikpeeghe unen ikpe inọ mme andimek ikọd amọ e-eseemeke ekoot anye uweemeayio ye akonayio? Me anye ayaatre adikpe unen nnọọ ammọ?</char> <verse eid="LUK 18:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 18:8" /><char style="wj">Ami ntañ inọ ndufo, anye ayaakịt ke ammọ e-ebọ unen ammọ usọp-usọp. Ado ini Ayịn Awo adiidi, anye ayaadikịt mbuọdidem ke iso isọñ?”</char><verse eid="LUK 18:8" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñke Farisi ye Abọọ Taks</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 18:9" />Yisọs ndin amaatop ñke ami anọ mbon e-ekekereke ke mmimọ imifọn ikan mbon mfen, ndin ekappa esọsọọn mbon mfen. <verse eid="LUK 18:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 18:10" /><char style="wj">“Ideen iba ekekaa tembịd adibọñ akam, keed awo Farisi, anye ako abọọ taks.</char> <verse eid="LUK 18:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 18:11" /><char style="wj">Farisi amaada ke idem amọ abọñ akam ate: ‘Abasi mmukọọm fiin sia ami mmiibaaha naña mbon mfen ebañña: Mme inọ, mme anañña ndiọi, mme asịn efịbe, me nte abọọ taks ami.</char> <verse eid="LUK 18:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 18:12" /><char style="wj">Ami nsitre ndidia akañ iba ke udua keed, ñnyʌñ ñkpe ayọhọ ubaak keed ke itie duob ke afịd se ami nnie nnọ Abasi.’</char><verse eid="LUK 18:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 18:13" />
    <char style="wj">“Ado abọọ taks amaasanna ada anyan usʌñ, ikidịppeke ukpọk anyen ise hefịn, ado abenne ubọk amia ke ikpanesịd amọ aseeme ate, ‘Abasi ntua miin anam idiọọkñkpọ mbọm.’ </char><verse eid="LUK 18:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 18:14" />
    <char style="wj">“Ami ntañ inọ ndufo, abọọ taks ami amaanyọñ ufọk amọ ye utoppo ikpe ke iso Abasi. Sia awo akeedodo a-akokkoke idem, eyaesuuhọ anye, ado eyaebenne awo a-asuuhọke idem.”</char><verse eid="LUK 18:14" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ntəkayịn ye Yisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 18:15" />Mme awo emaekoono mme nsekayịn edi ete Yisọs adot ammọ ubọk. Ado mme mbed amọ ekekịt ami, emaesua enọ ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 18:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 18:16" />Ndin Yisọs amaakoot ntəkayịn ado adat, anyʌñ abo, <char style="wj">“Iyak ntəkayịn edi eñkeene miin, ikiikpan ammọ, sia abioubọọñ Abasi anie utọ mbon ami.</char> <verse eid="LUK 18:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 18:17" /><char style="wj">Ke akpanikọ ke ntañ inọọ ndufo, awo akeedodo i-imiidiidatta abioubọọñ Abasi nte etəkayịn, idiikanna idʌk do.”</char><verse eid="LUK 18:17" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Imọ Awo ye Abioubọọñ Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 18:18" />Adaukara keed amaabịp Yisọs ate, “Eti andikpeeb, nsoo ke ana ami nnam nọ nnie uwem nsi-nsi?”<verse eid="LUK 18:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 18:19" />Yisọs amaabo anye, <char style="wj">“Nsinam afo añkoot miin eti? Ibaaha awo a-adooho eti ke miibọhọke Abasi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 18:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 18:20" /><char style="wj">Afo amediọọñọ mme mbed: ‘Kuusịn efịbe, kuuwot awo, kuuyịp inọ, kuutie ntiense nsu. Kpono ete ye eka mfo.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 18:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 18:21" />Anye amaabọọrọ Yisọs ate, “Ami mmenịm afịd mme mbed ami tọọñọ ke uyịn mmi.”<verse eid="LUK 18:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 18:22" />Yisọs akekop ibọọrọ ami, amaadọkkọ anye ate, <char style="wj">“Afo asʌk anaanana ñkpọ keed. Kaa ke nyam afịd se afo anie, kpọñ akʌk ado nọ nditọ uweene, ndin afo ayaanie akpan inie ke abio Abasi. Ndin di, ñkeene miin.”</char><verse eid="LUK 18:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 18:23" />Awo ami akekop ami, esịd amaabʌññọ anye, sia anye amaanie ñkpọ ataa eti-eti. <verse eid="LUK 18:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 18:24" />Yisọs amaabenne iso ase anye, ate, <char style="wj">“Ado ataa akpọsọñ ñkpọ mbon inie edidʌk abioubọọñ Abasi!</char> <verse eid="LUK 18:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 18:25" /><char style="wj">Ke akpanikọ, ado mmem-mmem ñkpọ kamel adiboiyo ke adudu abiaween ñkan awo inie adidʌk abioubọọñ Abasi.”</char><verse eid="LUK 18:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 18:26" />Mbon se ikikop ikọ ami emaebịp Yisọs ete, “Anie awo ndin akeme inie adinyaaña?”<verse eid="LUK 18:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 18:27" />Ndin Yisọs amaabọọrọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ñkpọ se isọñ ke ubọk awo isọññọ ke ubọk Abasi.”</char><verse eid="LUK 18:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 18:28" />Pita amaabo anye, “Ñnyịn imikpọñ afịd se ñnyịn ikinie ukeene fiin.”<verse eid="LUK 18:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 18:29" />Yisọs amaabo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Ke akpanikọ ke idọkkọ ndufo, ibaaha awo ndomokeed akpọññọ ufọk amọ, me anwaan, me nditọeka ideen, me nditọ eka ibaan me ete me eka, me nditọ, ke ntak abioubọọñ Abasi,</char> <verse eid="LUK 18:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 18:30" /><char style="wj">a-adiitre adibọ se iwak ikan ado ke emana ami, ye nsi-nsi uwem ke emana mfen.”</char><verse eid="LUK 18:30" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Atañ Abaña Ñkpa Amọ Ayọhọ Akañ Ita</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 18:31" />Yisọs amaakoot mme mbed amọ duob mme iba asịkke ada, anyʌñ adọkkọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ñnyịn iyaika Yeruselem, ndin afịd se mme prọfed ewet ebaña Ayịn Awo ayaasu.</char> <verse eid="LUK 18:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 18:32" /><char style="wj">Eyaeyaak anye esịn ke ubọk mme Gentile. Ammọ eyaesuenne anye, esaha, enyʌñ etọọñ anye etab;</char> <verse eid="LUK 18:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 18:33" /><char style="wj">ammọ eyaemia anye enyʌñ ewot anye. Ke ayọhọ usen ita, anye ayaamaana aset.”</char><verse eid="LUK 18:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 18:34" />Mme ikọ ami ikinwañake mme mbed amọ, ammọ ikinyʌññọ idiọọñọ se anye aketañ abaña; akeba ammọ usem-usem.<verse eid="LUK 18:34" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Anam Nnan Abeeñe Ebeeñe Akịt Usʌñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 18:35" />Yisọs akesaña akpere Yeriko, nnan keed amaatie ke mben usʌñ asʌk abeeñe ñkpọ. <verse eid="LUK 18:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 18:36" />Nnan ami akekop uyom atu awo naña efịt ediboiyo, anye amaabịp se ido. <verse eid="LUK 18:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 18:37" />Ammọ emaebo anye, “Yisọs awo Nasared asaña aboiyo.”<verse eid="LUK 18:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 18:38" />Anye amaasio ñkpo akoot ate, “Yisọs Ayịn Defid, ntua miin mbọm.”<verse eid="LUK 18:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 18:39" />Mbon se ikidat usʌñ emaeduat anye ete akʌp inua, ado anye amaadọdiọñ abọọñ ate, “Ayịn Defid, ntua miin mbọm.”<verse eid="LUK 18:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 18:40" />Yisọs amaatuak ada, ate eben nnan ado isọk imọ. Emaekeben anye idikpere, Yisọs amaabịp anye, <verse eid="LUK 18:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 18:41" /><char style="wj">“Nsoo ke afo ayem ami nnam unọ fiin?”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 18:41">Anye amaabọọrọ ate, “Abọọñ, ami ñyem adimọọnọ ñkpọ.”<verse eid="LUK 18:41" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 18:42" />Yisọs amaabo anye, <char style="wj">“Mọọnọ usʌñ; mbuọdidem mfo unyaaña fiin.”</char> <verse eid="LUK 18:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 18:43" />Kpa ke idahado anye amaamọọnọ ñkpọ, adakka akeene anye; asaña atooro Abasi. Atu awo ado e-ekekịtte ñkpọ ami emaekeene etooro Abasi.<verse eid="LUK 18:43" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 18" />
  <chapter number="19" style="c" sid="LUK 19" />
  <para style="s1">Sakiọs Abọọ Taks</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 19:1" />Usen keed Yisọs amaasaña aboiyo ke Yeriko. <verse eid="LUK 19:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 19:2" />Ete keed amaaba do a-akekereke Sakiọs. Anye akedo etubom mme abọọ taks anyʌñ ado imọ awo. <verse eid="LUK 19:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 19:3" />Anye amaayem adidiọọñọ me anie ke Yisọs ado, ado anye ikikanna imọọnọ Yisọs ke ntak atu awo sia anye akedo imək awo. <verse eid="LUK 19:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 19:4" />Anye amaafeghe akedọọk anyọñ eto sikamọ a-akedaaha ke usʌñ a-Yisọs akeduakka adisaña mboiyo.<verse eid="LUK 19:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 19:5" />Ke ini Yisọs akekewuọhọ itie ado, anye amaabenne anyen ke anyọñ anyʌñ abo anye ate, <char style="wj">“Sakiọs, sọiyọ di idahami. Ana ami mba ke ufọk mfo mfịn ami.”</char> <verse eid="LUK 19:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 19:6" />Anye amaasọiyọ ini keed anyʌñ adaara Yisọs.<verse eid="LUK 19:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 19:7" />Afịd awo se ikikịt adinam ami emaetọọñọ adidukuunọ ete, “Anye aka asen ke ufọk anam idiọọkñkpọ.”<verse eid="LUK 19:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 19:8" />Ado Sakiọs amaadakka ada abo Abọọñ ate, “Sese, Abọọñ! Idaha-idahami ami mmekpọñ inie mmi mbakka keed ke itie iba nnọ mme uweene, ndin akpedo mmaatʌk awo ndomokeed, ñyaakpe anye itie inaañ se ñkebọọ.”<verse eid="LUK 19:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 19:9" />Yisọs amaabo anye, <char style="wj">“Mfịn ami adinyaaña asịm ufọk ami, sia ete ami ñko ado ayịn Ebraham.</char> <verse eid="LUK 19:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 19:10" /><char style="wj">Sia Ayịn Awo akedi adiyem ñnyʌñ ñnyaaña mbon se isop.”</char><verse eid="LUK 19:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñke Akʌk Duob</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 19:11" />Ke ini ammọ ekesʌkkọ ekpañ utọñ ekop se Yisọs aketañ, anye amaatop ñke mfen anọ ammọ sia anye amaakpere Yeruselem, ñko mme awo ekekere ke abioubọọñ Abasi ayaadisịm kpa idahado. <verse eid="LUK 19:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 19:12" />Anye amaabo, <char style="wj">“Awuọiso ete keed amaakaa isañ ke anyan idịd nọ ekenam anye adidem, ndin anyọñ adi ke ndutʌm ado amaakweeñe.</char> <verse eid="LUK 19:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 19:13" /><char style="wj">Anye amaakoot nditọufọk amọ duob anyʌñ anọ ekpad akʌk mina duob.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19:13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">mina akedo ñkpọ nte akʌk utom afiọñ ita.</char></note> Ndin amaabo ammọ, <char style="wj">‘Ikama akʌk ami inyam udua tutu ami ñnyọñ ndi.’</char><verse eid="LUK 19:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 19:14" />
    <char style="wj">“Ado nditọufọk amọ ikimaaha anye, ndin emaedọñ utom enọ anye ete, ‘Ñnyịn iyemme ete ami ado adidem ñnyịn.’</char><verse eid="LUK 19:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 19:15" />
    <char style="wj">“Kpayeado, ekesʌk enanam anye adidem, anye amaanyʌñ anyọñ adi. Ndin anye amaadọñ ekoot nditọufọk amọ a-anye akenọọhọ akʌk nọ ato do anye adiọọñọ se udod ammọ ekenam.</char><verse eid="LUK 19:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 19:16" />
    <char style="wj">“Akpa awo amaadibo, ‘Ete, ekpad akʌk duob adoro ke akʌk a-afo akennọọhọ.’</char><verse eid="LUK 19:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 19:17" />
    <char style="wj">“Ete ami amaabo anye, ‘Amenam eti-eti, eti ayịnufọk mmi. Sia afo amenam akpanikọ ke etək ñkpọ, dat ukara ke abio duob.’</char><verse eid="LUK 19:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 19:18" />
    <char style="wj">“Ayọhọ awo iba amaawuọ adibo, ‘Ete, ekpad ition adoro ke akʌk a-akennọọhọ.’</char><verse eid="LUK 19:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 19:19" />
    <char style="wj">“Eteufọk amọ amaabọọrọ anye ate, ‘Afọn, afo kaara abio ition.’</char><verse eid="LUK 19:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 19:20" />
    <char style="wj">“Ayịnufọk mfen amaawuọ adibo, ‘Ete, se akʌk mfo mi, mmaabọp akʌk ado ke afọñ ñkenịm.</char> <verse eid="LUK 19:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 19:21" /><char style="wj">Ami ñkubaabaak fiin, sia afo ado akpọsọñ awo. Afo ado awo a-adatta ke itie umuukunịmme, anyʌñ adọk ke itie afo umuukutọọhọ.’</char><verse eid="LUK 19:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 19:22" />
    <char style="wj">“Eteufọk amọ amaabọọrọ anye ate, ‘Ami ñyaabiide ikpe mfo ñkeene ikọ inua mfo, afo ibak ayịnufọk! Ado nte afo ukudiọọñọke ke ami ndo akpọsọñ awo, ke ndo awo a-ndatta ke itie a-mmeñkenịmme ñnyʌñ ndọk ke itie a-mmeñketọọhọ?</char> <verse eid="LUK 19:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 19:23" /><char style="wj">Nsoo ndin ikido ntak a-afo umuukubenne akʌk mmi ukunịm ke itie unịm akʌk, nọ ato do ami mmaakpeto ndi, ñkpedibọ akʌk mmi ye udod?’</char><verse eid="LUK 19:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 19:24" />
    <char style="wj">“Eteufọk amọ amaabo mbon e-ekedaaha do ate, ‘Ibọ anye akʌk amọ idian inọ awo a-anieghe ekpad akʌk duob.’</char><verse eid="LUK 19:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 19:25" />
    <char style="wj">“Ammọ emaebo anye, ‘Ete, anye anenie ekpad duob.’</char><verse eid="LUK 19:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 19:26" />
    <char style="wj">“Anye amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, ‘Ami ibo ndufo ke afịd awo a-anieghe, eyaedian uwak enọ anye, ado awo i-imiinieghe ndomokeed, eyaebọ anye kpa etək se anye anie.</char> <verse eid="LUK 19:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 19:27" /><char style="wj">Amaado mme asua mmi i-imiikiyemme ami ndo adidem ammọ, koono ammọ di nyʌñ woot ammọ mi ke iso mmi.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 19:27" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Adʌk Yeruselem nte Adidem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 19:28" />Ke Yisọs amaaketañ ikọ ami ama, anye amaasak iso akaa Yeruselem. <verse eid="LUK 19:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 19:29" />Naña anye akekpereke Betfas ye Betani ke Abod Ọlif, anye amaadọñ mbed amọ iba ate, <verse eid="LUK 19:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 19:30" /><char style="wj">“Ikaa ke idʌñ a-adaaha ke iso ndufo ko, ndufo imaidʌk, eyaekịt abaak enañmbakara naña ayịre, a-adooho kpaanam awo ndomokeed idoroke ke anyọñ amọ. Itat anye iben idi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 19:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 19:31" /><char style="wj">Awo akpibịp abo, ‘Nsoo ido nọ etat anye?’ ibọọrọ anye ibo, ‘Abọọñ ayem.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 19:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 19:32" />Mme mbed e-ekedọññọ emaenyʌñ ekekịt kpa naña Yisọs akebo. <verse eid="LUK 19:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 19:33" />Ke ini ammọ ekesʌkkọ etat ñyịn enañmbakara ado, mme andinie emaebịp ammọ ete, “Nsoo ido nọ ndufo etat ñyịn enañmbakara ado?”<verse eid="LUK 19:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 19:34" />Ammọ emaebọọrọ, “Abọọñ ayem anye.”<verse eid="LUK 19:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 19:35" />Ammọ emaeben ñyịn enañmbakara ado esọk Yisọs, etop afọñ ammọ efʌk, enyʌñ edịppe Yisọs edot ke anyọñ amọ. <verse eid="LUK 19:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 19:36" />Ke ini anye akewatta aka ke usʌñ, mme awo emaetat afọñ anyọñidem ammọ ebịt ke usʌñ nọ anye asaña aboiyo.<verse eid="LUK 19:36" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 19:37" />Anye akedikpere uwakka usʌñ a-akaaha Abod Ọlif, afịd mme mbed ke inemesịd, emaetọọñọ aditooro Abasi ke akpọsọñ uyio ke afịd utịppeñkpọ se ammọ ekekịt, ete:<verse eid="LUK 19:37" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 19:38" />“Afọfọn anọ adidem a-adiighe ke anyịñ Abọọñ!”</para>
  <para style="b" vid="LUK 19:38" />
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 19:38">“Emem aba ke hefịn, ubọọñ anyʌñ aba ke ataa anyọñ!”<verse eid="LUK 19:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 19:39" />Usʌk mme Farisi ke atu awo ado emaebo Yisọs ete, “Andikpeeb, sua nọ mme mbed mfo!”<verse eid="LUK 19:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 19:40" />Anye amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ami ibo ndufo nte, ammọ ekpedop uyio, mme itiad eyaesio uyio.”</char><verse eid="LUK 19:40" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 19:41" />Ke anye amaakekpere Yeruselem, akịt abio ado, anye amaatua abaña anye, <verse eid="LUK 19:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 19:42" />ate, <char style="wj">“Ubaha nte afo, kpa afo, akpekediọọñọke ke usen mfịn ami se idiidat emem usọk fiin, ado idahami ado ndedịbe ñkpọ ke anyen mfo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 19:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 19:43" /><char style="wj">Ini ayaadi a-mme asua ndufo ediibọp ndibene ikanna ndufo ikʌk enyʌñ ifiọk ndufo ke afịd ñkañ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 19:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="LUK 19:44" /><char style="wj">Ammọ eyaitọ ndufo esuan ke isọñ, ikanna ndufo ye nditọ ndufo ekʌk ke esịd akwere ndufo. Ammọ idiiyakka itiad adoro ke itiad, sia ndufo ikidiọọñọke ini a-Abasi akediighe adise ndufo.”</char><verse eid="LUK 19:44" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs ke Tembịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" sid="LUK 19:45" />Ke Yisọs amaakedʌk akwere tembịd, anye amaatọọñọ adibịn mbon e-ekenyamma ñkpọ do nsio. <verse eid="LUK 19:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="LUK 19:46" />Anye amaabo ammọ, <char style="wj">“E-ewewet ebo, ‘Ufọk mmi adiido ufọk ubọñ akam’; ado ndufo emeben anye enịm ‘afe mbon inọ.’ ”</char><verse eid="LUK 19:46" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" sid="LUK 19:47" />Anye amaakpeep ñkpọ afịd usen ke tembịd. Ado mme ikpọ aku, mme akpeeb mbed ye mme adaaha emaeyem usʌñ adiwot anye. <verse eid="LUK 19:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="LUK 19:48" />Ado ammọ ikikịtte usʌñ naña ediisaña inam ami, sia afịd awo ekeyiire ke ikọ amọ.<verse eid="LUK 19:48" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 19" />
  <chapter number="20" style="c" sid="LUK 20" />
  <para style="s1">Eyem Adidiọọñọ nte Yisọs Adat Adudu</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 20:1" />Usen keed, naña Yisọs akesʌkkọ akpeep mme awo ñkpọ anyʌñ akwọrọ eti etob ke mme akwere tembịd, mme ñkpoon aku, mme andikpeeb mbed ye mme ñkpisọñ emaedi edisoobo ye anye. <verse eid="LUK 20:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 20:2" />Ammọ emaebịp anye ete, “Tañ inọ ñnyịn me nsoo utọ adudu ke afo akama anañña mme afịd ñkpọ ami. Anie ikunọọ fiin adudu ami?”<verse eid="LUK 20:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 20:3" />Anye amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ami ñko ñyaibịp ndufo mbịme keed. Indọkkọ miin:</char> <verse eid="LUK 20:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 20:4" /><char style="wj">Uduọkmmọọñ Yọọn, aketo hefịn, me aketo awo?”</char><verse eid="LUK 20:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 20:5" />Ammọ emaedọñọ adu ke idem ammọ ete, “Ñnyịn ikpibo ke aketo hefịn, anye ayaibịp, ‘Ntak a-ndufo imiikinịmme anye ke akpanikọ-ọ?’ <verse eid="LUK 20:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 20:6" />Ado ñnyịn ikpibo, ‘Aketo awo,’ afịd awo eyaitọọñ ñnyịn ke itiad sia ammọ ekenịm ke Yọọn ado prọfed.”<verse eid="LUK 20:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 20:7" />Ado anam ammọ emaebọọrọ ete, “Ñnyịn idiọọñọke nte aketo.”<verse eid="LUK 20:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 20:8" />Yisọs amaanyʌñ abọọrọ ammọ, <char style="wj">“Ami ndiinyʌññọ ntañ inọ ndufo nte ami ndat adudu nnañña mme ñkpọ ami.”</char><verse eid="LUK 20:8" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñke mme Akpemeinwañ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 20:9" />Anye amaakaa iso atop ñke ami anọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ete keed amaatọ inwañ fain, ayaak anọ mme akpemeinwañ ate ekpeme, ndin adakka akaa isañ a-anye imiikisọppọ inyọñ idi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 20:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 20:10" /><char style="wj">Ini idọk fain akedikem anye amaadọñ ayịnufọk ate akebọ ubaak mfịd ke inwañ fain isọk. Ado mme akpemeinwañ emaetịm anye, ebịn anye anyọñ ubọk-ubọk.</char> <verse eid="LUK 20:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 20:11" /><char style="wj">Anye amaamaana adọñ ayịnufọk mfen, ado ammọ emaemaana etịm anye, esuenne anye, enyʌñ ebịn anye anyọñ ubọk-ubọk.</char> <verse eid="LUK 20:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 20:12" /><char style="wj">Akem anye amaadọñ ayọhọ ayịnufọk ita, ado ammọ emaenọ anye unan, enyʌñ ebịn anye esio.</char><verse eid="LUK 20:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 20:13" />
    <char style="wj">“Ndin anie inwañ fain ado amaabo, ‘Nsoo ke ami ndiinam? Ami ñyaadọñ ayịn mmi awodeen, a-ami mmaaha; akeme ido ammọ eyaekpono anye.’</char><verse eid="LUK 20:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 20:14" />
    <char style="wj">“Ado ke ini mme akpemeinwañ ekekịtte ayịn ami, ammọ emaebiere ete, ‘Adiaakpa amọ ado ami. Yak ñnyịn iwot anye nọ ñnyịn ikappa ido mme adiaakpa.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 20:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 20:15" /><char style="wj">Ndin ammọ emaemʌm anye etop esio ke inwañ fain enyʌñ eben anye ekewot.</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 20:15">
    <char style="wj">“Nsoo ndin ke anie inwañ fain adiinam ammọ?</char> <verse eid="LUK 20:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 20:16" /><char style="wj">Anye ayaadiwoot mme akpemeinwañ ado anyʌñ ayaak inwañ fain anọ mbon mfen.”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 20:16">Ke ini mbon awo ekekoppo ñke ami, ammọ emaebo, “Nwaaña nsa-o!”<verse eid="LUK 20:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 20:17" />Yisọs amaatịñ anyen ase ammọ ndin abịp ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ndin nsoo ke se ewet ami awuọ:</char></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 20:17">
    <char style="wj">“ ‘Itiad a-mme abọbufọk ekesịnne</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 20:17">
    <char style="wj">a-akappa ado itiad inuuk’?</char><verse eid="LUK 20:17" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 20:18" />
    <char style="wj">Awo akeedodo a-adiiduọ ke itiad ami, adiibomo mbai-mbai; ndin awo i-itiad ami adiiduọ ifiik adiinuanuaha.”</char><verse eid="LUK 20:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 20:19" />Mme akpeeb mbed ye mme ikpọ aku emaeyem usʌñ naña ekpesaña emʌm anye usọp-usọp, sia ammọ emaediọọñọ ke anye aketop ñke ami ibaña mmimọ. Ado amọ emaebaak atu awo.<verse eid="LUK 20:19" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adikpe Taks Nnọọ Sisa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 20:20" />Ammọ emaenekke edukeene anye enyʌñ edọñ mbon uyeb e-ekenamma nte mmimọ ido nti awo ete ekeyep anye. Ammọ ekedot anyen adimʌm Yisọs ke ikọ inua nọ edat ado esaana anye eyaak enọ mme adaukara. <verse eid="LUK 20:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 20:21" />Mbon uyeb emaedomo Yisọs, enyʌñ ebịp anye ete, “Andikpeeb, ñnyịn imidiọọñọ ke afo ado atañ akpanikọ anyʌñ akpeep se ido unen, unyʌññọ ubaak awo anyen, ado akpeep usʌñ Abasi ke akpanikọ. <verse eid="LUK 20:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 20:22" />Anen ñnyịn adikpe taks nnọọ Sisa me inenne?”<verse eid="LUK 20:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 20:23" />Anye amaada akịt ñkara ammọ ndin amaabo ammọ ate, <verse eid="LUK 20:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 20:24" /><char style="wj">“Ñwọt akʌk ise. Ndise ye anyịñ anie eba ke akʌk ami?”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 20:24">Ammọ emaebọọrọ, “Ake Sisa.”<verse eid="LUK 20:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 20:25" />Anye amaabo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Iyaak se inie Sisa inọ Sisa, inyʌñ iyaak se inie Abasi inọ Abasi.”</char><verse eid="LUK 20:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 20:26" />Ammọ ikikanna imʌm anye ke ikọ inua a-anye aketañña ke iso afịd awo. Idem amaakpa ammọ ke ibọọrọ se Yisọs akenọọ, ndin ammọ ikikanna uyio isio.<verse eid="LUK 20:26" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adised ke Ñkpa ye Ndọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 20:27" />Ubaak mme Sadusi i-imiinịmme ke adised ke ñkpa aba, emaeben mbuume ebịne Yisọs ete, <verse eid="LUK 20:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 20:28" />“Andikpeeb, Moses amaawet abo, awodeen akpekpa akpọñ anwaan ibonno nditọ, ayịneka amọ awodeen ana aben ebekpa ado adọ nọ abon nditọ anọ anye. <verse eid="LUK 20:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 20:29" />Nditọeka ideen itiaba emaeba. Akpa awo amaadọ anwaan, akpa, inieghe ayịn. <verse eid="LUK 20:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 20:30" />Ayọhọ iba amaaben anwaan ami adọ. Anye ñko amaakpa inieghe ayịn. <verse eid="LUK 20:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 20:31" />Ayọhọ ita amaaben anwaan ado adọ, tutu asịm ayọhọ itiaba; ado afịd ammọ emaekpañña inieghe nditọ ito awonwaan ami. <verse eid="LUK 20:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 20:32" />Ke akpatre, awonwaan ado ñko amaakpa. <verse eid="LUK 20:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 20:33" />Ke adised ke ñkpa, anwaan anie ke mma ami adiido, sia naña ammọ ideen itiaba emaedọ kpa awonwaan keed ami?”<verse eid="LUK 20:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 20:34" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ ate, <char style="wj">“Mme awo ke emana ami edọ ndọ enyʌñ enọ ke ndọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 20:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 20:35" /><char style="wj">Ado mbon e-edotto adiwana ke uwem ini iso ye adised ke ñkpa idiidọọhọ ndọ inyʌññọ inọ ke ndọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 20:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 20:36" /><char style="wj">Sia ammọ idiikpaaha aba, ammọ eba nte mme enyere. Ammọ edo nditọ Abasi sia edo nditọ adised ke ñkpa.</char> <verse eid="LUK 20:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 20:37" /><char style="wj">Ado ke mbʌk ake Moses akekịtte naña ikañ asak ke ikọd, Moses ke idem amọ amaawọt ke mme akpañkpa e-eset sia ke mbʌk ami anye akoot Abọọñ ‘Abasi Ebraham ye Abasi Aisik ye Abasi Yekọb.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 20:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 20:38" /><char style="wj">Abasi idooho Abasi mme akpañkpa, ado Abasi mme aduuwem, sia afịd awo edu uwem ke anye.”</char><verse eid="LUK 20:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 20:39" />Ubaak mme andikpeeb mbed emaebọọrọ anye ete, “Ametañ afọn, andikpeeb!” <verse eid="LUK 20:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 20:40" />Tọọñọ ke usen ado awo ndomokeed ikikanna ibịp anye mbịme aba.<verse eid="LUK 20:40" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Krais Ado Ayịn Anie?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 20:41" />Ndin Yisọs amaabo ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Esaña die ebo ke Krais ado ayịn Defid?</char> <verse eid="LUK 20:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 20:42" /><char style="wj">Defid ke idem amọ atañ anwa-anwa ke Ñwed Saam:</char></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 20:42">
    <char style="wj">“ ‘Abọọñ amaabo Abọọñ mmi ate:</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 20:42">
    <char style="wj">“Tie ke ubọk nnasia mmi</char><verse eid="LUK 20:42" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 20:43" />
    <char style="wj">tutu ami nnam mme asua mfo</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 20:43">
    <char style="wj">edo ifịm udodukod mfo.” ’</char><verse eid="LUK 20:43" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="LUK 20:44" />
    <char style="wj">Defid akoot anye ‘Abọọñ.’ Anye akpenam die ado ayịn Defid?”</char><verse eid="LUK 20:44" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ndʌdutọñ ke Abaña mme Akpeeb Mbed</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" sid="LUK 20:45" />Naña atu awo ekesʌkkọ ekpañ utọñ, Yisọs amaabo mme mbed amọ ate, <verse eid="LUK 20:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="LUK 20:46" /><char style="wj">“Inekke ikpeme mme andikpeeb mbed. Ammọ ema adisịne ñweem-ñweem afọñidem nsaaña ñkanna ke efaak, enyʌñ eyem mbon awo ekọọm ammọ ke anwa udua ye ukpono, ema mme ñwuọnda itie ke mme sinakọk ye mme itie ukpono ke mme itie usọrọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 20:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="LUK 20:47" /><char style="wj">Ammọ ema adifuuk mme ebekpa mbọi ufọk, enyʌñ ewọt idem ke adibọñ ñnyan akam. Utọ ibon ami eyaebọ akpọsọñ ufen.”</char><verse eid="LUK 20:47" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 20" />
  <chapter number="21" style="c" sid="LUK 21" />
  <para style="s1">Enọ e-Ebekpa Anọọhọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 21:1" />Yisọs akedịppe anyen ke anyọñ, anye amaakịt naña mme imọ awo esịn mme enọ ammọ ke akebe usịn enọ ke tembịd. <verse eid="LUK 21:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 21:2" />Anye amaanyʌñ akịt uweene ebekpa keed naña asịn kọbọ iba. <verse eid="LUK 21:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 21:3" />Anye amaabo, <char style="wj">“Ke akpanikọ ke ibo ndufo, enọ ake ebekpa ami akan afịd ake mbon ñko.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 21:4" /><char style="wj">Afịd ibon ami ekenọ ekeene naña ammọ enie ñkpọ etre; ado anye ke uweene amọ, anọ afịd se anye akenie adidat ndu uwem.”</char><verse eid="LUK 21:4" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Uwuud Tembịd ye mme Idiọọñọ Utịd Ayio</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 21:5" />Usʌk mme mbed emaeneme ebaña naña ekebana tembịd ke Yeruselem nọ ayaiya; emaenyʌñ etañ ebaña mme nsọñudua enọ e-ekebonno do enọ Abasi. Ado Yisọs amaabo ammọ ate, <verse eid="LUK 21:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 21:6" /><char style="wj">“Ke afịd se ndufo ekịt ami, ayaaba ini i-itiad keed imiidiidoroke ke itiad, eyaenʌk afịd ado eduọọk ke isọñ.”</char><verse eid="LUK 21:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 21:7" />Ammọ emaebịp anye ate, “Andikpeeb, idahake ke mme ñkpọ ami ediitịppe? Nsoo idiido idiọọñọ ke mme ñkpọ ami eyaetịppe?”<verse eid="LUK 21:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 21:8" />Anye amaabọọrọ, <char style="wj">“Inekke ikpeme mbaak edibiaña ndufo. Sia mme awo eyaedi ke anyịñ mmi, ete, ‘Ami ndo anye’ edian do ebo ‘Ini akpere.’ Ikiikeene ammọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 21:9" /><char style="wj">Ndufo imaikop ekọñ ye ntịme, ikiikop ndịk. Ana mme ñkpọ ami ebemiso etịppe, ado utịd idiidiighe diin.”</char><verse eid="LUK 21:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 21:10" />Anye amaadian abo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Idịd ayaanwana ye idịd; abioubọọñ ayaanwana ye abioubọọñ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 21:11" /><char style="wj">Ikpọ unyeñisọñ, akañ ye nsio-nsio udọñọ ke nsio-nsio itie, mme anie ndịk ñkpọntịppe ye ikpọ idiọọñọ e-etooho hefịn eyaebañña.</char><verse eid="LUK 21:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 21:12" />
    <char style="wj">“Ado mbemiso afịd ami atịppe, ammọ eyaimuum ndufo enyʌñ etʌkkọ ndufo. Eyaeyaak ndufo enọ ke mme sinakọk, enyʌñ esịn ndufo ke ñkpakọb, ndin eyaenyʌñ eben ndufo ekaa iso mme ndidem ye mme adaukara ke ntak anyịñ mmi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 21:13" /><char style="wj">Ndin ami ayaanam ndufo edọdiọñ edo mme ntiense mmi enọ ammọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 21:14" /><char style="wj">Ado ibiere ke esịd ndufo ke idiinieghe iduọesịd ibaña se ediitañ ifakka idem.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 21:15" /><char style="wj">Sia ami ñyaitemme ndufo ikọ ñnyʌñ inọ aniọñ ake mme asua ndufo mmiidiikanna ifaaña.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 21:16" /><char style="wj">Mme ete, eka, nditọeka, ufan, aduuk ye imaan eyaetap ndufo, ndin ammọ eyaewot usʌk ndufo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 21:17" /><char style="wj">Afịd awo eyaisua ndufo ke ntak mmi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 21:18" /><char style="wj">Ado ided iwuod ndufo ndomokeed idiitakka.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 21:19" /><char style="wj">Isọọñọ ida, ndin ndufo eyaekan ke uwem.</char><verse eid="LUK 21:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 21:20" />
    <char style="wj">“Imaikịt naña udịmekọñ ekanna Yeruselem ekʌk, ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ini nsobo amọ akpere.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 21:21" /><char style="wj">Ndin yak mbon se iba ke Yudia efeeñe ekaiya mme ñkpoon abod, mbon se iba ke abio ewuọñọ, ndin mbon se iba ke esịd idʌñ ke etịmme ekaa esịd abio.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 21:22" /><char style="wj">Sia ini ufen ado ami ma afịd se ekewet adisu.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 21:23" /><char style="wj">Ado, mbọm ibaan e-esañake ye idịb ye ibaan e-esʌkkọ enọnọ mme nsekayịn eba ke utọ mme usen ado! Akpọsọñ ukuud ayaaba ke isọñ abio ye iyadesịd ñko ke abaña mme ibon ami.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 21:24" /><char style="wj">Ammọ eyaekpañña ke eduad ndin eyaenyʌñ ekoono ammọ nte mbon ñkpakọb ekaa nsio-nsio idịd. Mme Gentile eyaesọnnọ Yeruselem tutu ini mme Gentile anyʌñ aboiyo afep.</char><verse eid="LUK 21:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 21:25" />
    <char style="wj">“Mme idiọọñọ eyaeba ke utịn, afiọñ ye ntantaafiọñ. Ke ederimbod, mme idịd eyaekịt ukuud enyʌñ ekop ñkpaidem ebaña mme ayobio ye ufuud ke akpainyañ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 21:26" /><char style="wj">Mme awo eyaesʌkkọ ato ke mme anie ndịk ñkpọ, eduọ esịd ebaña se idiitịppe ke ederimbod, sia mme adudu ke mme hefịn eyaenyeeñe.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 21:27" /><char style="wj">Ke ini ado ammọ eyaekịt Ayịn Awo naña adi ke ntọñanyọñ ye adudu ye akwa ubọọñ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 21:28" /><char style="wj">Ke ini mme ñkpọ ami emaetọọñọ aditịppe, idaaña ida, idịppe iwuod ndufo ke anyọñ sia adinyaaña ndufo akpere.”</char><verse eid="LUK 21:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 21:29" />Anye amaatop ñke ami anọ ammọ: <char style="wj">“Se eto fik ye afịd mme eto mfen.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 21:30" /><char style="wj">Mfañ ammọ emaetọọñọ iseghe emediọọñọ ke ini ndaayio akpere.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 21:31" /><char style="wj">Kpayeado ndufo emaekịt afịd mme ñkpọ ami naña atịppe, ndufo ediọọñọ ke abioubọọñ Abasi akpere.</char><verse eid="LUK 21:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 21:32" />
    <char style="wj">“Ntañ akpanikọ inọ ndufo, emana ami idiiboiyoke ifep mbemiso mme ñkpọ ami etịppe.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 21:33" /><char style="wj">Anyọñ ye isọñ eyaeboiyo efep, ado tutu amama mme ikọ mmi idiiboiyoke ifep.</char><verse eid="LUK 21:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 21:34" />
    <char style="wj">“Ikpeme idem, mbaak ndufo idisịn esịd ke udiauwem, ukpa mmịn ye mme ñkpọ isọñ ami, ndin usen ado adibiọññọ ndufo adiwad-adiwad, ke unana idodanyen nte afia.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 21:35" /><char style="wj">Sia usen ado ana asịm afịd awo se idʌñ ke iso isọñ ami.</char> <verse eid="LUK 21:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 21:36" /><char style="wj">Iba ke mbeeñeidem afịd-afịd ini; inyʌñ ibọñ akam nọ enie ukeme adibọkkọ afịd se idiitịppe, nọ enyʌñ ekan eda ke iso Ayịn Awo.”</char><verse eid="LUK 21:36" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 21:37" />Yisọs amaasịkwọrọ ikọ ke tembịd kwa usen, amaado ndubiayio, anye akpọñ akeba ke abod e-ekekoodo Abod Ọlif, <verse eid="LUK 21:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 21:38" />ndin ayio amaasiere, afịd awo ebak edi edikop ukwọrọikọ amọ ke tembịd.<verse eid="LUK 21:38" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 21" />
  <chapter number="22" style="c" sid="LUK 22" />
  <para style="s1">Yudas Anyịmme Aditap Yisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 22:1" />Usen Usọrọ Uyo a-yiis imiisịneke, e-ekekoodo Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo, amaakpere. <verse eid="LUK 22:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 22:2" />Ndin mme ñkpoon aku ye mme akpeeb mbed emaeyem ñkara usʌñ naña ammọ ediisaña imʌm Yisọs ikiwot, sia ammọ ekefegheke atu awo. <verse eid="LUK 22:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 22:3" />Akekem Setan amaadʌk esịd Yudas Iskariọd a-akedooho keed ke atu mme mbed Yisọs duob mme iba. <verse eid="LUK 22:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 22:4" />Ndin anye amaakaa akeneme ye mme ñkpoon aku ye mme akpeme tembịd abaña naña anye akpekan atap Yisọs anọ ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 22:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 22:5" />Esịd amaadat ammọ ndin emaenyịmme adinọ anye akʌk. <verse eid="LUK 22:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 22:6" />Yudas amaanyịmme, anyʌñ atọọñọ iyem ufañ se anye adiitap Yisọs inọ ammọ idaha a-atu awo imiibaaha.<verse eid="LUK 22:6" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Akpatre Ndidia Ndubi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 22:7" />Amaakedikem usen Usọrọ Uyo a-yiis imiisịneke, a-akenaaha ewa edọñ Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo, <verse eid="LUK 22:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 22:8" />Yisọs amaadọñ Pita ye Yọọn ate ammọ, “Ikaa ikinam ndutʌm ibaña ndidia Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo.”<verse eid="LUK 22:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 22:9" />Ammọ emaebịp anye ete, “Ke ñke ke ayem ñnyịn ikinam ndutʌm?”<verse eid="LUK 22:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 22:10" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ: <char style="wj">“Imaidʌk abio, eyaekịt awodeen keed nte akama abañ mmọọñ. Ikeene anye ikaa ufọk a-anye akaaha,</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 22:11" /><char style="wj">inyʌñ ibo anieufọk ado ite, ‘Andikpeeb abịp abo: Akee ubeed isen ke ñkeme adidia Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo ye mme mbed mmi?’</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 22:12" /><char style="wj">Ndin anye ayaiwọt ndufo ekamba ubeed ke anyọñ, e-emaekebeeñe enịm. Inam ndutʌm do.”</char><verse eid="LUK 22:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 22:13" />Ammọ emaedakka edʌk abio enyʌñ ekekịt ukem-ukem naña Yisọs aketañ anọ ammọ, emaenyʌñ ebeeñe Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo.<verse eid="LUK 22:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 22:14" />Ke ini amaakekem, Yisọs ye mme mbed amọ duob mme iba emaesuuk etie ke akpokoro ndidia. <verse eid="LUK 22:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 22:15" />Yisọs ndin amaabo ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Anekke añwʌt miin adidia Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo ami ye ndufo mbemiso ami mbọ ndutʌhọ.</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 22:16" /><char style="wj">Sia ami ndiidiaha Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo mfen aba ye ndufo tutu adiwuọ asu ke abioubọọñ Abasi.”</char><verse eid="LUK 22:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 22:17" />Ke anye amaakeben kọọb, anye amaanọ Abasi ekọọm, ayaak anọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ibọ ideeme ke atu idem ndufo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 22:18" /><char style="wj">Ami ntañ inọ ndufo nte ke ami ndiiñwọññọ se ito mfịd fain aba, tutu abioubọọñ Abasi adi.”</char><verse eid="LUK 22:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 22:19" />Akema anye amaaben uyo, anyʌñ anọ ekọọm, abuuñ, ayaak anọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Anye ami ado ikpọkidem mmi, i-inọọhọ ndufo; inam ami adidat intoiyo miin.”</char><verse eid="LUK 22:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 22:20" />Kpa ke ukem usʌñ ado, ke emaekedia ndidia ndubi ema, anye amaaben kọọb, ate, <char style="wj">“Kọọb ami ado ufa edioomo ke iyiib mmi, e-eduọkkọ inọọ ndufo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 22:21" /><char style="wj">Ado awo a-adintap miin mmọ mi ye ami ke akpokoro.</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 22:22" /><char style="wj">Ayịn Awo adiinyọñ naña ekebiere. Ado adọdiọọk anọ awo a-adiitap anye!”</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 22:23" />Mbed amọ emaetọọñọ adibịp idem ammọ me anie awo ke atu mmimọ idiinam utọ ñkpọ ami.<verse eid="LUK 22:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 22:24" />Akem mfaaña ye eniin amaatọọñọ ke atu ammọ, me anie ke atu ammọ akpon itie akan. <verse eid="LUK 22:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 22:25" />Yisọs amaabo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Mbọọñ mme Gentile ekaara ammọ naña emama, ndin mbon e-ekamake adudu ekoot idem ammọ mme Anọunwam.</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 22:26" /><char style="wj">Inaaha ado ntoro ke atu ndufo. Utu ke ado, yak awo se ikpon ikan ke atu ndufo akappa atie nte andisịb ñkan, ndin yak adaiso ke atu ndufo akappa atie nte ayịnufọk inọ ndufo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 22:27" /><char style="wj">Anie awo ikpon ikan, anditie ke akpokoro ndidia me andiben ndidia ndinọ? Nte idooho anditie ke akpokoro? Ado ami mba ke ufọọd ndufo nte andinam ñkpọ inọọ ndufo. </char> <verse eid="LUK 22:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 22:28" /><char style="wj">Ndufo edo mbon e-ebereke ye ami ke mme ini idomo mmi.</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 22:29" /><char style="wj">Ndin ami mmenịm abioubọọñ inọ ndufo, ukem-ukem naña Ete mmi akennọ miin,</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 22:30" /><char style="wj">nọ ato do ndufo edia enyʌñ enwọñ ke akpokoro abioubọọñ mmi, enyʌñ etie ke mme ebekpo, ekpe ikpe enọ mme esiin Isrel duob mme iba.”</char><verse eid="LUK 22:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 22:31" />Yisọs ndin amaabo Saimọn, <char style="wj">“Saimọn, Saimọn, Setan amaabo yak ekeñ afịd ndufo nte awo akeñ abakpa.</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 22:32" /><char style="wj">Ado ami mmaabọñ akam unọ fiin, mbaak mbuọdidem mfo adikpu. Ndin afo umautịmme udemme ke mbuọdidem, sọọñọ nditọ ete mfo idem.”</char><verse eid="LUK 22:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 22:33" />Ado Saimọn amaabọọrọ anye ate, “Abọọñ, ami mmebeeñe idem adisaña ye afo, akpọkọm adika ufọk ñkpakọb me ke ñkpa.”<verse eid="LUK 22:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 22:34" />Yisọs amaabo anye, <char style="wj">“Pita, ami udọkkọ fiin, mbemiso akikọunen akpọk mfịn ami, afo ayañkañ akañ ita ate ke imọ indiọọñọke miin.”</char><verse eid="LUK 22:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 22:35" />Ndin Yisọs amaabịp ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Idaha ami ñkisịññeke ndufo ndọñ utom, naña imiikikamake ekpad akʌk, me ndidia, me ikpaukod, anie naña ñkpọ akinana ndufo?”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 22:35">Ammọ emaebọọrọ, “Ñkpọ ikinanake ñnyịn.”<verse eid="LUK 22:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 22:36" />Anye amaabo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Idahami yak awo a-anieghe ekpad akʌk, aben, ake anie ekpad ndidia, yak aben, ñko akpedo unieghe akañkañ nyam afọñidem dat ke dep.</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 22:37" /><char style="wj">Ntañ ami inọ ndufo, ikọ e-ewette ete, ‘Ndin emaebat anye esịn ke atu mme anam idiọọkñkpọ’ ana asu ke idem mmi. Ii, ke akpanikọ, se ewet ami atọtọọñọ adisu.”</char><verse eid="LUK 22:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 22:38" />Mbed amọ emaebo anye, “Abọọñ, se eduad iba mi.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 22:38">Anye amaabo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Ado akem!”</char><verse eid="LUK 22:38" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Abọñ Akam ke Abod Ọlif</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 22:39" />Yisọs ye mme mbed amọ emaekaa Abod Ọlif, naña ido amọ akesido. <verse eid="LUK 22:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 22:40" />Ke anye amaakesịm do, anye amaabo mme mbed amọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ibọñ akam mbaak ndufo idiidʌk idomo.”</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 22:41" />Yisọs ndin amaasịkke akpọñ mme mbed ke idaha ubọk iyịrọ keed, aketọọñọ edọñ abọñ akam, <verse eid="LUK 22:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 22:42" /><char style="wj">“Ete mmi, akpedo afo amenyịmme, ben kọọb ami fep nnọ miin; ado yak ke ado ke unyịmme mmi, yak ado naña afo anyịmme.”</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 22:43" />Ndin enyere amaato ke hefịn adida anye ke iso anyʌñ asọọñọ anye idem. <verse eid="LUK 22:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="LUK 22:44" />Ke mbʌññọ esịd, anye amaanekke asịn idem abọñ akam tutu adikpọ a-akewuọñọke anye ke idem, akappa abit iyiib atọiyọ ke isọñ.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22:44 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ataa uwak akpa ikpañwed inieghe Luk 22:43, 44.</char></note><verse eid="LUK 22:44" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" sid="LUK 22:45" />Anye akekpọñ itie ubọñ akam amaatịmme abịne mme mbed amọ akekịt ke ammọ ekesʌk edaiya anọ ekaha ye akpọsọñ mfʌhọ. <verse eid="LUK 22:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="LUK 22:46" />Anye amaatọi ammọ, abịp ate, <char style="wj">“Nsoo ido ntak a-ndufo edaiyake? Idemme inyʌñ ibọñ akam mbaak ndufo ididʌk ke idomo.”</char><verse eid="LUK 22:46" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Emʌm Yisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" sid="LUK 22:47" />Ke anye akesʌkkọ atatañ mme ikọ ami, atu awo emaediwuọ. Keed ke atu mbed amọ, Yudas, akeboiyo iso, asaña abịne Yisọs aketʌm anye inua. <verse eid="LUK 22:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="LUK 22:48" />Ado Yisọs amaabịp anye ate, <char style="wj">“Yudas afo adi aditap Ayịn Awo ke ntʌminua?”</char><verse eid="LUK 22:48" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" sid="LUK 22:49" />Ke mbed Yisọs ekekịtte se ikiditịppe, ammọ emaebịp Yisọs ete, “Abọọñ, imikeme adikịm ammọ ke akañkañ?” <verse eid="LUK 22:49" /><verse number="50" style="v" sid="LUK 22:50" />Ndin awo ammọ keed amaasio eduad adiañña ayịnufọk ekamba aku utọñ nnasia.<verse eid="LUK 22:50" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" sid="LUK 22:51" />Ado Yisọs amaabo, <char style="wj">“Yak atre do!”</char> Ndin anye amaatuuk utọñ ete ado, anyʌñ akọk anye.<verse eid="LUK 22:51" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="52" style="v" sid="LUK 22:52" />Ndin Yisọs amaabo mme ñkpoon aku ye mme ikpọ awo mbon ukpeme tembịd ye mme ñkpisọñ e-ekediighe edimʌm anye, ate, <char style="wj">“Ndufo ewuọñọ edi ye mme eduad ye mme akpeti nte eka adimʌm awo ntịme me inọ?</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:52" /><verse number="53" style="v" sid="LUK 22:53" /><char style="wj">Idaha ami ñkebaaha ye ndufo ke afe tembịd, ibaaha awo ndufo a-akenyanna ubọk antuuk miin. Ufañ ndufo ado ami, ini a-adudu ekịm akarake.”</char><verse eid="LUK 22:53" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pita Akañ Yisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="54" style="v" sid="LUK 22:54" />Ammọ emaemʌm anye, eben edakka ekaa ufọk ekamba aku. Pita amaakpeeñ ñkpad isañ, akeene nsan-nsan. <verse eid="LUK 22:54" /><verse number="55" style="v" sid="LUK 22:55" />Ke ammọ emaekebara ikañ ke ufọọd esịd akwere, eyem itie ebono, Pita amaakekeene atie ye ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 22:55" /><verse number="56" style="v" sid="LUK 22:56" />Abọikpa ayịnufọk keed akekịt naña Pita atie awue ikañ, amaawuuk anyen ase anye, ate, “Awo ami akeba ye anye.”<verse eid="LUK 22:56" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="57" style="v" sid="LUK 22:57" />Ado Pita amaakañ ate, “Abọikpa, ami ndiọọñọke anye.”<verse eid="LUK 22:57" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="58" style="v" sid="LUK 22:58" />Etək ini akeboiyo, awo mfen amaakịt Pita, ate, “Afo ado keed ke atu nsaña amọ.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 22:58">Pita amaamaana akañ ate, “Ete, ndooho!”<verse eid="LUK 22:58" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="59" style="v" sid="LUK 22:59" />Ñkpọ nte awa keed akeboiyo, awo mfen amaadi aditañ uko-uko ye Pita, ate, “Ke akpanikọ, awo ami akesaña ye anye, sia anye ado awo Kalili.”<verse eid="LUK 22:59" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="60" style="v" sid="LUK 22:60" />Pita amaabọọrọ ate “Ete, ami ndiọọñọke se afo atuum ke inua!” Kpa idaha a-Pita akesʌkkọ atatañ ntoro, akikọunen amaakpọk. <verse eid="LUK 22:60" /><verse number="61" style="v" sid="LUK 22:61" />Abọọñ amaawọññọ iso awuuk anyen ase Pita, ndin anye amaatoiyo ikọ a-Yisọs akebooho anye ate, <char style="wj">“Mbemiso akikọunen akpọk mfịn, afo ayañkañ miin ñke nta.”</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:61" /><verse number="62" style="v" sid="LUK 22:62" />Ndin Pita amaawuọ esiin, aketua idod-idod ayịd.<verse eid="LUK 22:62" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mbio Ukpeme Enọ Yisọs Ñnyọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="63" style="v" sid="LUK 22:63" />Ideen e-ekekpemeke Yisọs emaetọọñọ edọọñ anye ndọk enyʌñ etịm anye. <verse eid="LUK 22:63" /><verse number="64" style="v" sid="LUK 22:64" />Ammọ emaebọp anye ñkịm ke anyen, ete anye, “Tañ prọfesi! Anie awo ikumia fiin?” <verse eid="LUK 22:64" /><verse number="65" style="v" sid="LUK 22:65" />Ammọ emaenyʌñ esueñ anye, etaañ ikọ usọñanyen edian anye.<verse eid="LUK 22:65" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs ke Iso Pailed ye Herọd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="66" style="v" sid="LUK 22:66" />Ke usiere, mme ñkpisọñ esob abio, ye mme ñkpoon aku ye mme akpeeb mbed emaewuọ ebono itie keed, ndin emaeben Yisọs edi ke iso ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 22:66" /><verse number="67" style="v" sid="LUK 22:67" />Ammọ emaebo Yisọs, “Akpedo afo ado Krais, tañ inọ ñnyịn.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 22:67">Yisọs amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Adieke ami ntañña inọọ ndufo, ndufo idinnịmme miin ke akpanikọ,</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:67" /><verse number="68" style="v" sid="LUK 22:68" /><char style="wj">ñko ami ñkpibịp ndufo, ndufo idimbọọrọke.</char> <verse eid="LUK 22:68" /><verse number="69" style="v" sid="LUK 22:69" /><char style="wj">Ado tọọñọ ke idahami, Ayịn Awo ayaatie ke ubọk nnasia Akwa Abasi.”</char><verse eid="LUK 22:69" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="70" style="v" sid="LUK 22:70" />Afịd ammọ emaedọñ uyio ebịp anye, “Nte afo ndin ado Ayịn Abasi?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 22:70">Anye amaabo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Ndufo etañ ke ami ndo Ayịn Abasi.”</char><verse eid="LUK 22:70" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="71" style="v" sid="LUK 22:71" />Ammọ ndin emaedọñ uyio keed ete, “Nsoo utọ ntiense mfen ke ñnyịn iyem aba? Ñnyịn imikop ito inua amọ.”<verse eid="LUK 22:71" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 22" />
  <chapter number="23" style="c" sid="LUK 23" />
  <para style="s1">Pailed Abịp Yisọs Mbịme</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 23:1" />Ndin afịd esob emaedakka eda enyʌñ eben Yisọs ekaa iso Pailed. <verse eid="LUK 23:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 23:2" />Ndin ammọ emaetọọñọ adidot anye uyio, ete, “Awo ami asịn nsọk ke idịd ñnyịn, ate mme awo ekuukpe taks enọọ Sisa, anyʌñ abo ke imọ ido Krais, adidem.”<verse eid="LUK 23:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 23:3" />Ke ntoro Pailed amaabịp Yisọs ate, “Afo ado adidem mme Yuu?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 23:3">Yisọs amaabọọrọ, <char style="wj">“Ado afo atañ ntoro.”</char><verse eid="LUK 23:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 23:4" />Ndin Pailed amaadọkkọ mme ikpọ aku ye atu awo ate, “Ami ñkịtte ndudue nnọ awo ami.”<verse eid="LUK 23:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 23:5" />Ado ammọ emaeyiire ete, “Ukpeebñkpọ amọ a-adat mfịna adi ke afịd Yudia. Anye aketọọñọ ke Kalili ndin idahami adiwuọ umi.”<verse eid="LUK 23:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 23:6" />Pailed akekop ami amaabịp me anye ato Kalili. <verse eid="LUK 23:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 23:7" />Ke ini anye akediọọñọke ke Yisọs akeba ke idak ukara Herọd anye amaanọ Yisọs esọk Herọd ke Yeruselem sia Herọd akeba do ke ini ado.<verse eid="LUK 23:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 23:8" />Herọd akekịt Yisọs, esịd amaanem anye sia ke ataa anyan ini anye amaanie udọñ adisoobo ye Yisọs. Se anye akekop abaña Yisọs amaanam anye anie idodanyen ke imọ iyaikịt naña anye anam utịppeñkpọ. <verse eid="LUK 23:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 23:9" />Herọd amaakwak Yisọs ye uwak mbuume ado anye ikibọọrọke anye. <verse eid="LUK 23:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 23:10" />Mme ñkpoon aku ye mme andikpeeb mbed e-ekebaaha do emaesọọñọ etañ ikọ ndoduyio ebaña Yisọs. <verse eid="LUK 23:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 23:11" />Herọd ye mbon ekọñ amọ emaesaha, enyʌñ edọọñ anye ndọk. Ke emaekesịn anye uyaiya afọñ ubọọñ emaetịmme enọ anye esọk Pailed. <verse eid="LUK 23:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 23:12" />Tọọñọ ke usen ado Pailed ye Herọd e-ekesidusuarake emaekappa edoñño ufan.<verse eid="LUK 23:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 23:13" />Pailed amaakoot mme ñkpoon aku ye mme adaukara ye afịd awo abok ke itie keed <verse eid="LUK 23:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 23:14" />anyʌñ abo ammọ ate, “Ndufo ekedat awo ami ensọk miin nte awo a-asịnne nsọk nọ mme awo esịn ntịme ke abio. Ami mmeduuñọ anye ke iso ndufo ado ñkịtte ndudue a-anamma ndufo etañ ikọ edian anye. <verse eid="LUK 23:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 23:15" />Herọd ikiinyʌññọ ikịt ndudue ke anye, ntak ado akenam anye atịmme anọ anye isọk ñnyịn. Nte ndufo ekịtte, anye idueghe ñkpọ a-adotto ufen ñkpa. <verse eid="LUK 23:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 23:16" />Ke ntoro, ami ñyaamia anye ñnyʌñ nsaana anye ñyaak.” <verse eid="LUK 23:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 23:17" />Nte mbed adooho, akena anye afeen ndudue awo keed enyʌñ esio anye ke ñkpakọb ke ini Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo.<verse eid="LUK 23:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 23:18" />Ado afịd atu awo emaebọñ ke uyio keed ete, “Iben awo ami ikaa! Isio Barabas inọ ñnyịn.” <verse eid="LUK 23:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 23:19" />(Ekesịn Barabas ke ñkpakọb sia anye amaasịn nsọk ke abio anyʌñ awot awo.)<verse eid="LUK 23:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 23:20" />Ke adiyem adisaana Yisọs ñyaak, Pailed amaamaana akpeiye ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 23:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 23:21" />Ado ammọ emaebọñ ke akpọsọñ uyio, “Ekọñ anye ke krọs, ekọñ anye ke krọs!”<verse eid="LUK 23:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 23:22" />Pailed amaakaa iso atañ ye ammọ ayọhọ akañ ita anyʌñ abịp ate, “Ntak-a? Nsoo ido ndudue amọ? Ami ñkịtte ntak ekpenọọhọ anye ufen ñkpa. Ke ntoro, ami ñyaanam enọ anye ufen ndin esaana anye eyaak.”<verse eid="LUK 23:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 23:23" />Ado ammọ emaebọñ ke akpọsọñ uyio, eyiire ete ekọñ anye ke krọs ndin uyio ammọ amaasọñ ada. <verse eid="LUK 23:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 23:24" />Ke ntoro Pailed amaabiide adinam uduak ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 23:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 23:25" />Anye amaasio awo e-ekekọppọ ke ntak usịn nsọk ke abio ye uwodawo, anye a-ammọ ekebooho yak esio, ado ayaak Yisọs anọ ammọ nọ ekenam ye anye naña ammọ eyem.<verse eid="LUK 23:25" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ekọñ Yisọs ke Krọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 23:26" />Naña mbon ekọñ ekebenne anye edakka, ammọ emaemʌm Saimọn awo Siriin ke usʌñ isañ a-anye akekaaha enyʌñ enam anye abiom krọs akeene Yisọs. <verse eid="LUK 23:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 23:27" />Umiañ awo emaekeene anye, ke atu ami ibaan emaesịne e-ekefʌhọke enyʌñ etuaha ebaña anye. <verse eid="LUK 23:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 23:28" />Yisọs amaakanna iso ase ammọ anyʌñ abo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Nditọ ibaan Yeruselem, ikiitua imbaña miin ado itua ibaña idem ndufo ye nditọ ndufo.</char> <verse eid="LUK 23:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 23:29" /><char style="wj">Sia ini asʌk adi a-ndufo ediibo, ‘Afọfọn anọ mme ada, mme idịb i-imiimanna ayịn akpa, ye mme eba a-ayịn imiiwọppọ akpa.’</char> <verse eid="LUK 23:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 23:30" /><char style="wj">Ndin,</char></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="LUK 23:30">
    <char style="wj">“ ‘Ammọ eyaebo mme ekamba abod, “Iduọññọ itọọñ ñnyịn!”</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="LUK 23:30">
    <char style="wj">Enyʌñ ebo ntək abod, “Ifuuk ñnyịn!” ’</char><verse eid="LUK 23:30" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 23:31" />
    <char style="wj">Sia adieke mme awo enamma mme ñkpọ ami idaha e-eto adooho ndisi, nsoo idiitịppe ini a-mfañ asaatta?”</char><verse eid="LUK 23:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 23:32" />Emaedat Yisọs ye mme ndiọi awo iba ekaa adiwot. <verse eid="LUK 23:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 23:33" />Ke ini ammọ emaekesịm itie e-ekekoodo Ñkpọkpọrọ, ammọ emaekọñ anye ke krọs ye ndiọi awo iba ado, keed ke ubọk nnasia amọ, keed ke ubọk ufiin. <verse eid="LUK 23:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 23:34" />Yisọs amaabo, <char style="wj">“Ete feen nọ ammọ, sia ammọ idiọọñọke se ammọ enam.”</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23:34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Usʌk mme ñkaan ikpañwed inieghe udịmikọ ami. </char></note> Ke emaekesịn ukañ, ammọ emaedeeme afọñ amọ.<verse eid="LUK 23:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 23:35" />Mbon awo emaeda ese, mme adaukara emaenyʌñ enọ anye inua ete, “Anye amaanyaaña mbon mfen, yak anye anyaaña idem amọ, akpedo anye ado Krais, Andimek Abasi.”<verse eid="LUK 23:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 23:36" />Mbon ekọñ ñko emaenyʌñ enọ anye inua. Ammọ emaenọ anye fineka ete anwọñ, <verse eid="LUK 23:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 23:37" />enyʌñ ebo ete, “Akpedo afo ado adidem mme Yuu, nyaaña idem mfo ise.”<verse eid="LUK 23:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 23:38" />Emaewet ñwed edian ke anyọñ itie a-anye akekọñọke, ete:</para>
  <para style="pc" vid="LUK 23:38">
    <char style="sc">Ami ado Adidem mme Yuu.</char><verse eid="LUK 23:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 23:39" />Keed ke atu mme anam idiọọkñkpọ a-akekọñọke ye anye, amaasọñ anye anyen ate: “Idooho afo ado Krais? Nyaaña idem mfo nyʌñ inyaaña ñnyịn!”<verse eid="LUK 23:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 23:40" />Ado anam idiọọk anye ako amaasua anọ anye ate, “Nte afo ubaaha Abasi, sia afo abọọhọ ukem ufen? <verse eid="LUK 23:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 23:41" />Inọ ñnyịn ufen a-adotto ye idiọọkñkpọ ñnyịn. Ado ete ami idueghe ke usʌñ ndomokeed.”<verse eid="LUK 23:41" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 23:42" />Ndin anye amaabo, “Yisọs, ntoiyo miin ke umaudʌk abioubọọñ mfo.”<verse eid="LUK 23:42" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 23:43" />Yisọs amaabọọrọ anye ate, <char style="wj">“Ami udọkkọ fiin akpanikọ, mfịn ami afo adiiba ye ami ke paradais.”</char><verse eid="LUK 23:43" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñkpa Yisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="LUK 23:44" />Akedo ke ñkpọ nte ñkanika duob mme iba uweemeayio, ekịm amaafʌk afịd isọñ tutu asịm ñkanika ita uweemeayio, <verse eid="LUK 23:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="LUK 23:45" />sia utịn amaatre adiyamma. Ndin afọñ ikpeghe tembịd amaasakka iba. <verse eid="LUK 23:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="LUK 23:46" />Yisọs amaabọñ ke akpọsọñ uyio ate, <char style="wj">“Ete, mmeyaak ukpọñ mmi usịn fiin ke ubọk.”</char> Ke anye amaaketañ ikọ ado ama, anye amaaduọk akpatre ibifịk amọ.<verse eid="LUK 23:46" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" sid="LUK 23:47" />Ke sentudiọn akekịtte se ikitịppe, amaatooro Abasi anyʌñ abo, “Ke akpanikọ awo ami akedo adinen awo.” <verse eid="LUK 23:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="LUK 23:48" />Afịd awo se ikida ise se ikitịppe emaemia ubọk ke esịd edaaña enyọñọ. <verse eid="LUK 23:48" /><verse number="49" style="v" sid="LUK 23:49" />Ado afịd awo se ikidiọọñọ Yisọs ye mme ibaan e-ekekeeneke anye tọọñọ ke Kalili ekeda nsan-nsan ese mme ñkpọ ami.<verse eid="LUK 23:49" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ebuuk Yisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" sid="LUK 23:50" />Ndin amaaba awo keed a-akekereke Yosef, awo Akwa Esob akọnsịn, a-akedooho eti ye adinen awo, <verse eid="LUK 23:50" /><verse number="51" style="v" sid="LUK 23:51" />i-idiikinyịmmeke edioomo ye adinam ammọ. Anye aketo abio Yudia ke ukañ Arimatia; anye ke idem amọ akenyʌñ atie abet adidi abioubọọñ Abasi. <verse eid="LUK 23:51" /><verse number="52" style="v" sid="LUK 23:52" />Anye amaakaa abịne Pailed akebeeñe ate inọ akpo Yisọs. <verse eid="LUK 23:52" /><verse number="53" style="v" sid="LUK 23:53" />Ndin anye amaakọññọ akpo Yisọs, awañ ke afọn linen anyʌñ anịm ke udi e-eketịppeke ke itiad a-adooho kpaanam awo ndomokeed ikibʌhọke. <verse eid="LUK 23:53" /><verse number="54" style="v" sid="LUK 23:54" />Akedo Usen Mbeeñeidem, sia Sabad akedo edem usen.<verse eid="LUK 23:54" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="55" style="v" sid="LUK 23:55" />Ibaan e-ekekeeneke Yisọs tọọñọ ke Kalili emaekeene Yosef ekekịt udi ye naña ekenịm akpo amọ. <verse eid="LUK 23:55" /><verse number="56" style="v" sid="LUK 23:56" />Ndin ammọ emaenyọñ ufọk enyʌñ ekebeeñe idem enam pefium se ediiben ikifiọññọ akpo Yisọs. Ado ammọ emaeduọk adudu ke usen Sabad nte mbed aketemmeke.<verse eid="LUK 23:56" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 23" />
  <chapter number="24" style="c" sid="LUK 24" />
  <para style="s1">Yisọs a-Aset ke Ñkpa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="LUK 24:1" />Ke akpa usen ke udua, ke usiere, ibaan emaeben mme anemufịk adan a-ammọ ekenamma ekaa udi. <verse eid="LUK 24:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="LUK 24:2" />Ammọ emaekekịt ke emaewere itiad esio ke udi, <verse eid="LUK 24:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="LUK 24:3" />ado ke ini ammọ ekedʌkkọ esịd udi, ammọ ikikịtte akpo Yisọs. <verse eid="LUK 24:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="LUK 24:4" />Nte ammọ ekesʌkkọ eda do ekere ebaña ñkpọ ami, ideen iba e-ekesịneke nsem-nsem afọñ a-akebịtte akebkeb, emaebiọññọ ke ñkañ ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 24:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="LUK 24:5" />Ke ndịk, ibaan ado emaesuuk iso ke isọñ, ado ideen ado emaebo ammọ ete, “Ntak a-ndufo eyemme aduuwem ke atu mme akpañkpa-a? <verse eid="LUK 24:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="LUK 24:6" />Anye ibaaha mi; anye a-aset. Itoiyo se anye akidọkkọ ndufo ke ini anye akesʌkkọ aba ye ndufo ke Kalili: <verse eid="LUK 24:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="LUK 24:7" /><char style="wj">‘Akena eyaak Ayịn Awo esịn ke ubọk mme anam idiọọk, ekọñ anye ke krọs, anye anyʌñ aset ke ayọhọ usen ita.’</char> ” <verse eid="LUK 24:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="LUK 24:8" />Ndin ammọ emaetoiyo ikọ amọ.<verse eid="LUK 24:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="LUK 24:9" />Ammọ emaekenyọñ udi edi emaeditañ afịd ñkpọ ami enọ mme mbed duob mme keed ye afịd mbon mfen. <verse eid="LUK 24:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="LUK 24:10" />Mmeri Makdalin, Yoana, ye Mmeri eka Yems ye mbon mfen e-ekebaaha ye ammọ ekedo mbon e-ekedọkkọke mme abọsịd mme ñkpọ ami. <verse eid="LUK 24:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="LUK 24:11" />Ado ammọ ikinịmme se ibaan ado eketañ ke akpanikọ, sia mbʌk ammọ akeba nte ndisịme ke utọñ ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 24:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="LUK 24:12" />Pita amaafeghe akaa udi, akenyuuñọ ase esịd udi, ado ikikịtte ñkpọ mfen ikan mme mbai afọñ linen e-ekekamake ewañ Yisọs naña ebono ke idem ammọ ikpọọñ. Anye ndin amaadakka anyọñ ye ñkpaidem, anyʌñ akere ke esịd amọ se ikitịppe.<verse eid="LUK 24:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Mbed Iba ke Usʌñ Emaus</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="LUK 24:13" />Kpasʌk ke usen ado, iba ke atu mme mbed Yisọs ekeka idʌñ keed a-akekereke Emaus, a-akedooho ñkpọ nte itiad itiaba<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24:13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte kilomita 11</char></note> tọọñọ ke Yeruselem. <verse eid="LUK 24:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="LUK 24:14" />Ammọ ekeneme nneme ebaña afịd ñkpọ se ikitịppe, <verse eid="LUK 24:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="LUK 24:15" />ado nte ammọ ekesʌkkọ eneme mme ñkpọntịppe ami, Yisọs ke idem amọ amaabiọññọ anyʌñ asaña ye ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 24:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="LUK 24:16" />Ado anyen ammọ ikitarake nọ ammọ ediọọñọ anye.<verse eid="LUK 24:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="LUK 24:17" />Anye amaabo ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Nsoo ke ndufo eneneme ke usʌñ?”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 24:17">Ammọ emaetuak eda, iso ammọ ayọhọ ye mfʌhọ. <verse eid="LUK 24:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="LUK 24:18" />Ndin keed ke atu ammọ, a-akekereke Kliopas, amaabọọrọ anye ate, “Afo ado asenawo ke Yeruselem umuudiọọñọke afịd se itịppe ke usen ifañ ami.”<verse eid="LUK 24:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="LUK 24:19" />Anye amaabịp ate, <char style="wj">“Mme nsoo ñkpọ?”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="LUK 24:19">Ammọ emaebọọrọ ete, “Abaña Yisọs awo Nasared akedooho prọfed, anie adudu ke ikọ ye ke adinam ke iso Abasi ye iso afịd awo. <verse eid="LUK 24:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="LUK 24:20" />Mme ñkpoon aku ye mme adaukara ñnyịn emaesaana anye eyaak nọ ebiere ikpe ñkpa enọ anye enyʌñ ekọñ anye ke krọs; <verse eid="LUK 24:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="LUK 24:21" />idodanyen ñnyịn akedo ke anye adiido andidiifak Isrel. Ikweeñeke ke ado, usen ita ado ami tọọñọ mme ñkpọ ami eketịppe. <verse eid="LUK 24:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="LUK 24:22" />Ke ado aboiyoke, ubaak ibaan ke atu ñnyịn emaenam idem ikpa ñnyịn. Ammọ ekeka udi ke ataa ubakusen, <verse eid="LUK 24:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="LUK 24:23" />ke ini ammọ imiikikịtte akpo Yisọs, ammọ emaenyọñ edidọkkọ ñnyịn ke mmimọ ikikịt mme enyere ke ñkukịd e-ekibooho mmimọ ke anye mmọdo ke uwem. <verse eid="LUK 24:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="LUK 24:24" />Ubaak mbon nsaña ñnyịn emaekaa udi enyʌñ ekekịt afịd ñkpọ naña ibaan ado eketañ, ado ammọ ikikịtte Yisọs.”<verse eid="LUK 24:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="LUK 24:25" />Anye amaabo ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Ndufo emesịme eti-eti, aditre adisọp nnịm afịd se mme prọfed eketañ ke akpanikọ!</char> <verse eid="LUK 24:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="LUK 24:26" /><char style="wj">Nte ikinaaha Krais abọ ufen ndin anye adʌk ke ubọọñ amọ?”</char> <verse eid="LUK 24:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="LUK 24:27" />Ndin anye amaatọọñọ ke Moses ye mme Prọfed mbon ñko anam anwaña ammọ mme afịd se eketañ ke ñwed Abasi a-abañake anye.<verse eid="LUK 24:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="LUK 24:28" />Ke ini ammọ emaekekpere itie a-ammọ ekekaaha, Yisọs amaanam nte isʌk idiikaka iso ke isañ. <verse eid="LUK 24:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="LUK 24:29" />Ado ammọ emaenekke eyịre anye ete aba ye mmimọ, sia ayio amaakaa adikịm; ndin anye amaakeba ye ammọ.<verse eid="LUK 24:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="LUK 24:30" />Ke ini ammọ ekesʌkkọ edia ñkpọ, anye amaaben uyo anọ ekọọm, abuuñ, ndin atọọñọ adideeme nnọọ ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 24:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="LUK 24:31" />Do ke anyen ammọ aketara, ndin ammọ emaediọọñọ anye; ado anye amaasop ammọ ke anyen. <verse eid="LUK 24:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="LUK 24:32" />Ndin ammọ emaebịp idem ammọ ete, “Nte esịd ñnyịn ikiduọhọ ini anye akesʌkkọ atañ ikọ ye ñnyịn anyʌñ akappa ñwed Abasi inọọ ñnyịn ke usʌñ?”<verse eid="LUK 24:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="LUK 24:33" />Kpa idahado ammọ emaetịmme enyọñ Yeruselem. Ndin ammọ emaekesoobo ye mme mbed duob mme keed nte eboho ye mme nsaña ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 24:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="LUK 24:34" />Mbon ado emaebo ammọ ete, “Abọọñ a-aset ke ñkpa ke akpanikọ, anyʌñ a-ayaara idem anọ Saimọn.” <verse eid="LUK 24:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="LUK 24:35" />Ndin ammọ awo iba emaetañ se ikitịppe ke usʌñ isañ, ye naña ammọ ekediọọñọ anye ke ini anye akebuuñọ uyo.<verse eid="LUK 24:35" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Awọt mme Mbed Idem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="LUK 24:36" />Ke ini ammọ ekesʌkkọ etatañ ke inua ebaña afịd mme ñkpọ ami, Yisọs ke idem amọ amaawuọ ada ke atu ammọ anyʌñ abo ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Emem aba ye ndufo!”</char><verse eid="LUK 24:36" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="LUK 24:37" />Ammọ emaedịkke enyʌñ ekop ndịk sia ekekere ke ikịt ekpo. <verse eid="LUK 24:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="LUK 24:38" />Ado anye amaabo ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Nsoo ido ntak e-esịd itịmekede ndufo; nsoo inyʌñ inam nọ ndufo enie eyịghe ke esịd ndufo?</char> <verse eid="LUK 24:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="LUK 24:39" /><char style="wj">Se ubọk ye ukod mmi nọ ediọọñọ ke ami ke ado! Intuuk miin ise; ekpo inieghe ikpọkidem ye akpọ naña ami nnie.”</char><verse eid="LUK 24:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="LUK 24:40" />Nte anye akesʌkkọ atañ ikọ ami, anye amaawọt ammọ ubọk ye ukod amọ. <verse eid="LUK 24:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="LUK 24:41" />Ammọ emaekop inemesịd tutu ikanna inịm se ekekịt, sia idem amaakpa ammọ eti-eti. Ndin anye amaabịp ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Emenie ñkpọ se edia mi?”</char> <verse eid="LUK 24:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="LUK 24:42" />Ammọ emaeben ibio nsaad iyak enọ anye. <verse eid="LUK 24:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="LUK 24:43" />Anye amaabọ anyʌñ ata ke iso ammọ.<verse eid="LUK 24:43" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="LUK 24:44" />Ndin anye amaabo ammọ, <char style="wj">“Se ami ñketañ inọọ ndufo ke idaha a-ami ñkesʌkkọ mba ye ndufo ado ami: Afịd se ekewet embaña miin ke Mbed Moses, ye ke ñwed mme Prọfed ye mme Saam ana asu.”</char><verse eid="LUK 24:44" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" sid="LUK 24:45" />Ndin anye amaanam ikọ Abasi anwaña ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 24:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="LUK 24:46" />Anye amaabo ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Se ewet ado ami: Krais ayaabọ ufen ndin aset ke ñkpa ke ayọhọ usen ita,</char> <verse eid="LUK 24:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="LUK 24:47" /><char style="wj">ñko ke anyịñ amọ eyaekwọrọ ukappaesịd ke adifeen ke mme idiọọkñkpọ nnọọ afịd mme idịd, tọọñọ ke Yeruselem.</char> <verse eid="LUK 24:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="LUK 24:48" /><char style="wj">Ndufo edoñño ntiense enọ mme ñkpọ ami.</char> <verse eid="LUK 24:48" /><verse number="49" style="v" sid="LUK 24:49" /><char style="wj">Ami ñyaanọ se Ete mmi akenwọñọ isọk ndufo; ado iba ke Yeruselem tutu adudu ato anyọñ adisịm ndufo.”</char><verse eid="LUK 24:49" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adidọọk Yisọs ke Anyọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" sid="LUK 24:50" />Ke Yisọs amaakeben ammọ asaña akewuọ ñkpere abio Betani, anye amaadịppe ubọk adiọñ ammọ. <verse eid="LUK 24:50" /><verse number="51" style="v" sid="LUK 24:51" />Ke anye akesʌkkọ adiọñ ammọ, anye amaasịkke akpọñ ammọ ndin emaeben anye edọọk ke hefịn. <verse eid="LUK 24:51" /><verse number="52" style="v" sid="LUK 24:52" />Ammọ emaekpono anye, enyʌñ etịmme enyọñ Yeruselem ye ekamba idaara. <verse eid="LUK 24:52" /><verse number="53" style="v" sid="LUK 24:53" />Ndin ammọ ekeba ke tembịd afịd ini etooro Abasi.<verse eid="LUK 24:53" /></para>
  <chapter eid="LUK 24" />
</usx>